<h2>一、民间故事与文化</h2>

<p><strong>1 寒妈</strong></p>

<p><strong>Legend Han Ma</strong></p>

<p>Legend Han Ma 传说在清代嘉庆戊辰年间，一个雨雪纷飞的冬日，普宁云落附近 山村的一位孝妇，恐其上山捡柴的家姑冻坏，亲送寒衣。奈何她体弱 腹饥，衣衫单薄，攀越陡径时，失足跌倒而冻死在望天岭下。因山高 路险，小径行人稀少，一时未被发现。 During Jiaqing period of the Qing dynasty (1808), on a snowy winter day, a widow who lived in a village near Yunluo (a town of Puning), feared that her aunt who went up the mountain to collect firewood would be frozen, so she went out to give her winter clothes personally. However, she was feeble and ragged. When crossing the steep path, she slipped and fell, and died of cold under the Wangtianling Mountains. This was a steep, desolate and untraversed place, so no one found the woman for a while. 恰巧在这时，上京赴试的赵厝寮村穷举子李光宪，途经这无名小 径。当他冒着寒风前进时，骤见地上倒着一位妇人，意欲相救。走进 一看，妇人已被冻僵。心底善良的他不忍村妇尸横荒径，备受日晒雨 淋，顿起埋葬之念，但在这荒山僻岭之中，苦无工具可用，若下山找 人相助又会耽误科期，左右为难间脱下蓝布长衫，遮盖于女尸之上， 并许诺若金榜题名，必回来建宫庙铭谢，揖别后便匆匆起程。 Coincidentally, Li Guangxian, a provincial candidate from Zhao Cuoliao village, who went to capital for the imperial examination, passed through this nameless path. When he endured the cold wind and moved forward, he suddenly saw a woman lying on the ground and wanted to help her. But when he looked closely, he found that she was already frozen. He is so kind that could not leave the female corpse exposed to the weather in the steep path. He wanted to bury her. But in this wilderness, no tool could be found. If he went down the mountain to find someone to help him, he would be late for the imperial examination. In a dilemma, he took off his blue cloth gown and covered the female corpse. He promised that if he succeed in the exam, he would come back to build a temple to express his gratitude, and then he made a bow with his hands folded in front in a hurry before he left. 传说李光宪进京考试后，主考宗师查阅其考卷，虽文章超群，书 法工整，却漏写了“馬”字一点，赞叹之余甚为惋惜。当他扬起朱笔 要批为错字时，怎料那漏笔之处竟被填补。宗师揉眼细察，原来是一 只蚂蚁填于失划地方，用中指弹去，重新要提笔打圈时，那只蚂蚁又</p>

<p>爬到失划地方。如此反复数次，宗师仍认为李光宪答案有错字，把考 卷放于不录取的文档上。但是李光宪的试卷却再次出现在宗师台面 前。宗师对此大为惊奇，传李光宪前来问话，才知道他上京途中，曾 在风雪山径上，将寒衣遮盖一位素不相识的冻死妇人尸体，深为感动， 连声称赞李光宪的美德，或许这是冻死妇女的报恩，也是文人之德。 宗师朱笔签批，皇上纳意，李光宪名题金榜，官封翰林。 After the imperial examination in Beijing, the examiner looked up Li Guangxian’s papers and found that his articles were superb, with neat calligraphy, but the word " 馬 (horse)" was written with one stroke missing. Therefore, the examiner felt very regretful about it. When he raised the writing brush with cinnabar to mark that word was a mistake, he did not expect the missing strokes to be filled. The examiner rubbed his eyes and inspected it carefully, only to discover that it was an ant filling the missing stroke in “ 馬” . He flicked the ant away with his middle finger. But when he re-raised the writing brush to circle the words, the ant had crawled back to where he was going to mark. After repeating this several times, the examiner still believed that Li Guangxian's answer was a mistake, and put the test paper into the rejected category. But Li Guangxian's test paper appeared again in front of the examiner's platform. The examiner was very surprised by this and then asked people to summon Li Guangxian to come for questioning. The examiner learned that on the way to Beijing, Li Guangxian had used a clothes to cover the body of an unknown woman who had been frozen to death on the windy and snowy mountain trail. The examiner was deeply moved by his kind deeds and praised Li Guangxian for his noble character. Perhaps this is the gratitude of the women who died of freezing, and it is also the virtue of literati. So after the chief examiner asked the emperor for instructions, Li Guangxian passed the imperial examination and became Hanlin Academician. 为了却承诺，李光宪专程来普宁望天石山下这无名小径，重寻冻 尸收埋，但其已化为一堆白骨，上面围满一群蚂蚁。李光宪命侍从将 骨骸拿到半山埋下，且在原地建成一庙，亲笔题了"冻媪寒婆"四字镌 于石匾，镀上金色，挂于庙门以祀之。寒婆庙宇建成后，来往行人为 了表示敬仰，必拾山草少许，放置庙侧，积多则焚火，以暖其寒。在 后世流传中将村妇从“寒婆”改称为“寒妈”（má）。并且那条无 名小径也被人们称为"寒婆径"，在流传中也改称为"寒妈径"。 In order to fulfill his previous promise, Li Guangxian came to the nameless path at the foot of Wangtianling Mountain in Puning to search for the frozen corpse again and bury her. But it has turned into a pile of bones, surrounded by a group of ants. Li Guangxian ordered the servant to take the bones to the middle of the</p>

<p>mountain and buried them, and built a temple in the original place. He inscribed the four characters "Dong Ao Han Po", which is used to express gratitude to Han Ma (Ma is the second tone in pinyin, má), on the stone plaque in person, plated with gold lacquer, and hung on the gate of the temple to worship Han Ma. After the Han Po Temple was built, pedestrians passing by would certainly pick up some firewood and place it on the side of the temple in order to show their respect for Han Ma. When enough firewood is piled up, light it to keep out the cold. In the spread of later generations, "Han Po" was renamed "Han Ma". Meanwhile, the nameless path was also called "Han Po path", and later renamed as "Han Ma path" in the circulation as well. 据普宁县志记载，清代举人林乔松曾为寒婆庙题对联“授衣千 古事，遗迹万年香”。自古以来，寒妈的孝心和李光宪的善举在民间 广为传诵，它启迪后人，行孝和行善是一种美德。 According to the annals of Puning County, Lin Qiaosong, a famous provincial candidate in the Qing Dynasty, once wrote a couplet for Han Ma temple, which said, " The coat deliver was a long ago donation, the virtue will perfume to each generation.” Since ancient times, the filial piety of Han Ma and the good deeds of Li Guangxian have been widely read among the people. It enlightens later generations that filial piety and doing good deeds are a kind of virtue. 编译温佳菲丁叶枫陆明滢</p>

<p><strong>2 妃子笑</strong></p>

<p><strong>Legend of Guifei Litchi</strong></p>

<p>Legend of Guifei Litchi 谈起美人，世人皆知杨贵妃；说起南国荔枝，无人不晓“一骑红 尘妃子笑”，贵妃和荔枝又是一个怎样美妙的传说呢? When it comes to beauty in the ancient China, everyone knows Yang Guifei (Concubine of Emperor Xuanzong of Tang Dynasty); when it comes to litchi in the South China, everyone knows that “quick delivery of litchi without seeing running horse is for Yang Guifei’s beaming”. So, what fabulous story lays out between them? 荔枝是驰名的岭南佳果，味极美，需鲜食。杨贵妃出生于古代盛 产荔枝的巴蜀，自小酷爱荔枝。此外，荔枝有些神奇利她的功效，不 仅能够促进皮肤的新陈代谢，还能延缓衰老。荔枝虽妙，但万万不可 贪嘴。广东民传“一啖荔枝三把火”，荔枝易热气上火，所以惯有荔 枝蘸盐水的吃法。而同为巴蜀的文人“吃货”苏东坡听成了“日啖荔 枝三百颗”，后有佳句“日啖荔枝三百颗，不辞长做岭南人”。 Particularly noted as Lingnan’s good fruit, litchi should be eaten in fresh, exceedingly delicious in taste. Yang Guifei comes from Bashu (now known as Sichuan Province) which was abundant with her favorite fruit--- litchi. She likes it ardently since childhood. Besides, it has some magical effects, which can promote the metabolism of skin, and delay the aging. While litchi is delicious, it should not be greedy to eat. Just as the Cantonese said “one litchi is equal to triple heatiness”, it is customary to reduce heatiness by dipping litchi in salt water. However, the literati of Song Dynasty and a renowned foodie, Su Dongpo, who was from Bashu too, misheard the Cantonese saying as “Having 300 lychees a day”, which became the masterpiece verses “having 300 lychees a day, then never hesitate to be a Lingnanese”.</p>

<p>为什么贵妃荔枝会名扬四方、流传千古呢？其一“妃子这一笑” 可谓可歌可泣。其二，当时在长安吃荔枝着实不是一件容易的事情。 相传唐明皇唐玄宗为满足美人杨贵妃的喜好，特令身边的红人高力 士，从家乡进贡荔枝到京城长安，只为美人尝鲜。为博红颜一笑，唐 明皇动用了当时所能动用的最极端的办法。 Why there have been too much publicity about Guifei Litchi? The first is that Tang’s love to Yang Guifei is an epic love story. The second is that people found it really hard to eat litchi in Chang 'an at that time. It is on everybody’s lips, in order to please Concubine Yang, Emperor Xuanzong of Tang ordered his favourite Gao Lishi to send litchi from his hometown to capital of Chang 'an, all for the beauty to taste in fresh. Tang resorted to the most extreme way of transportation available to get what she wants, which made him win the love from Guifei. “妃子笑”荔种便是应故事而生。远在广东高州有个根子镇，镇 上有个柏桥村，村里有个贡园，那里便是种满了贵妃独爱的南国珍品。 每到成熟之际，负责进贡荔枝的驿使，便从贡园中将采摘下来的新鲜 荔枝放进巨竹筒内，沿着荔枝古道，十万火急，直奔京城长安。因其 “果实一离本枝，一日色变，二日香变，三日味变，四五日之外，色 味尽去矣。”而素有“荔枝姑娘”之称。马不停蹄，人不喘歇，接力 快传，以保鲜美。 And 'Feizixiao' Litchi has come into being to meet this epic love story. Far away in Genzi town of Gaozhou City, Guangdong Province, there is a Baiqiao village with a Gongyuan ( an orchard for the royal) full of treasures of South China, which was deeply loved by Yang Guifei. When it was ripe, the courier was in charge of</p>

<p>delivering tribute of fresh litchis which were just pick from the Gongyuan into a giant bamboo tube, then delivered along the ancient Litchi Road at the highest speed to the capital Chang'an. Enjoying the reputation of “litchi girl”, litchi is plucked from the branch, color will change in one day, aroma will change in two days, flavor will change in three days. The litchi will be tasteless in four or five days, which means not being storable and transportable. So, the horses have to run without a stop, and the riders proceed without a rest, only for keeping of litchi fresh. “千年贡品”--茂名荔枝，历史气息可贵，游荔文化更是丰富。 每当荔红时节，便有以荔枝会友、以荔枝吟诗、以荔枝促商、以荔枝 兴游……然而，荔枝的价值远远不止这些。千百年来,多少果农的生 计、助学等皆受益于古荔。随着时间的流逝，荔枝依旧是人们无法 舍弃的南国珍品。如今岭南各地产区，每到丰收盛季都会举办荔枝节， 广为人知的是经济道路重头戏。然而鲜为人知的是，荔枝殊于色味之 外，文化之中。 As "Millennium tribute", Maoming litchi is rich in both history and tourism resources. When the litchi is ripe for harvest, the locals will celebrate by taking litchi to meet friends, to recite poetry, to encourage business, to go sightseeing, and so on. However, what the litchis bring to us is far more than these. For thousands of years, many fruit farmers have benefited from selling litchis for their livelihood and education. With the passage of time, litchi ---the treasure of South China---remains its irreplaceable flavor that people can't reject. Nowadays there are more various litchi festivals held in the harvest season than ever before in Lingnan. It is well-known that it aims to create more wealth. While it is little-known that litchi, the real treasure is not in its color and flavor, but in its culture. 编译吴雄燕</p>

<p><strong>3 湘子桥</strong></p>

<p><strong>Xiangzi Bridge</strong></p>

<p>Xiangzi Bridge 湘子桥，又名广济桥，坐落于广东省潮州市古城东门外，横跨韩 江，是古代广东通向闽浙的交通要道，潮州八景之一，也是中国四大 古桥之一，桥梁专家茅以升给予“世界上最早的启闭式桥梁”之称。 Xiangzi Bridge, also known as Guangji Bridge, is located outside the east gate of the ancient city of Chaozhou City, Guangdong Province, across the Hanjiang River. It is an important transportation route from Guangdong to Fujian and Zhejiang in ancient times. It is one of the eight scenic spots in Chaozhou and one of the four major ancient bridges in China. Bridge expert Mao Yisheng gave it the title of "the earliest open-close bridge in the world". 湘子桥的每一个桥墩至今都有好几百年的历史，从宋代建成第一 个桥墩到形成“十八梭船廿十四洲”的格局，前后共经历了300 多年。 在古代生产力落后的情况下，要建一座横跨大江的桥，人们认为这是 天方夜谭，所以潮州民间便流传许多“仙佛造桥”的传说。 Each pier of the Xiangzi Bridge has a history of hundreds of years. It took more than 300 years from the completion of the first pier in the Song Dynasty to the formation of the "18 shuttle boats and 24 continents". In the ancient times when the productive forces were backward, it was necessary to build a bridge across the river. People thought it was a fantasy. Therefore, Chaozhou folks have spread many legends of "immortal Buddha building bridges". 据说，唐代韩愈被贬潮州后，经常去东门游玩。但受到大江的阻 隔，就想着如果在中间有一座桥那就方便多了，但水深流急无法施工， 便请八仙和广济和尚帮忙建造，广济和尚负责西岸，八仙负责东岸。 为了早日把大桥建好，两边仙佛们都施法力，各显神通。 It is said that after being demoted to Chaozhou in the Tang Dynasty, Han Yu often visited the east gate. But being blocked by the big river, he thought that it would be much more convenient if there was a bridge in the middle. But the water was too deep and the water was too fast to construct, so he asked Baxian(eight immortals in Chinese legend)) and Guangji monk to help build it. Guangji monk was responsible for the west bank, and Baxian was responsible for the east bank. In order to build the bridge as soon as possible, the immortal Buddhas on both sides cast and showed their magical powers.</p>

<p>广济和尚跑到桑浦山来，把石头点化成羔羊。由广济和尚赶往潮 州城来。东岸八仙则跑去凤凰山，把山上石头变成猪群，也赶向工地。 八仙人多，分批赶猪，在铁拐李赶着最后一批猪下山时，那知半路碰 到一个孝妇在一口坟前啼哭，被这丧气一冲，符法失灵，石头乌猪再 也赶不动了。 Monk Guangji ran to Sangpu Mountain and turned the stone into a lamb. He drove a flock of lamb to Chaozhou city. The Eight Immortals on the East Coast ran to Phoenix Mountain, turned the rocks on the mountain into pigs, and rushed to the construction site. There were many Eight Immortals, and they drove the pigs in batches. When Tieguai Li was driving the last batch of pigs down the mountain, he met a filial woman crying in front of a grave on the way. He was frustrated by this. As a result, the spells failed and the stone pigs can no longer move. 广济和尚一人赶羊，顾此失彼，赶到潮州城，一数发现少了两只 羊，急忙回头寻找。当他找到了羊又往回赶时，却碰到当地的一个恶 霸地主，存心想夺取这些羊，便说：“你这和尚哪来的羊啊!分明是 我家的。”广济和尚被纠缠得不耐烦，便说：“既然是你家的羊，便 赶到你田里去吧！”地主把羊都赶到他自己的田里去，却变成一座座 乌石山，把地主的良田压掉了。 Monk Guangji drove the lamb alone, and rushed to Chaozhou City to find two lambs missing and hurriedly looked back. When he found the lamb and drove back, he met a local bully landlord who deliberately wanted to seize the sheep, and said, "How can a monk get lambs? It is clearly mine!" Monk Guangji was entangled. Getting impatient, he said, "Since it is your lamb, hurry to your field!" The landlord drove all the lambs to his own field, but turned into a mountain of black rocks, crushed the landlord’s fertile land. 八仙少了一群猪，广济和尚又掉了二只羊。大桥建到江心，便没 有石头可把桥接起来，大江两岸照旧还是被水隔断。铁拐李急得直跺 脚，结果把东岸桥墩踩低了一角，大家正不知如何是好，只见何仙姑 把手中宝莲花抛下，花瓣在江心散开来，变成了十八条梭船，对岸广 济和尚看了，急忙丢下手杖，手杖变成了一条长藤，把十八条梭船紧 紧连成一条浮桥。这样，人们为纪念仙佛合力造桥的功绩，便把此桥 既称为“湘子桥”，又叫“广济桥”。 The Eight Immortals lost a group of pigs, and the monk Guangji lost two more lambs. When the bridge was built to the middle of the river, there were no stones to connect the bridge, and the two banks of the river were still separated by water. Tieguai Li stomped his feet in anxious manner, and finally stepped on the east bank</p>

<p>pier by a corner. Everyone was not sure what to do, but He Xiangu dropped her hand in the treasure lotus, and the petals spread out in the heart of the river, turning into eighteen. Shuttle boat, the other side Guangji monk looked at, and hurriedly dropped his stick, which turned into a long vine, connecting the eighteen shuttle boats tightly into a pontoon bridge. In this way, people call this bridge both "Xiangzi Bridge" and "Guangji Bridge" in order to commemorate the achievements of the immortals and Buddhas in building bridges. 湘子桥除了桥上的十八梭船和二十四楼台外，桥下更是暗藏玄 机。清朝雍正时期，为防洪水，在湘子桥底西桥第八墩和东桥第十二 墩各放置了一头鉎牛，并在牛头刻了“镇桥御水”的字样。后来，韩 江发大水把东边的鉎牛冲走了，于是便有了“两只鉎牛一只溜”的民 谣。 In addition to the eighteen shuttle boats on the bridge and the twenty-fourth floor of the Xiangzi Bridge, there are hidden mysteries under the bridge. During the Yongzheng period of the Qing Dynasty, in order to prevent floods, two bullocks were placed on the eighth pier of the West Bridge and the twelfth pier of the East Bridge at the bottom of the Xiangzi Bridge. Each of the bullocks craved with Zhen Qiao Yu Shui four Chinese characters on the head, which means to protect the bridge and prevent it from the flood. Afterwards, Hanjiang River was in flood and washed away the bullocks in the east, so there is a ballad “two bullocks but one slipped away”. “潮州湘桥好风流，十八梭船廿四洲。廿四楼台廿四样，两只鉎 牛一只溜。”这首粤东地区广为传唱的民谣高度概括了湘子桥的主要 风景与特色。 " Xiangzi Bridge in Chaozhou is fantastic, with 18 shuttle boats and 24 piers. The 24 piers boast 24 types. There were Two bullocks but one slipped away." This ballad widely sung in eastern Guangdong highly summarizes the main scenery and features of Xiangzi Bridge. 编译 黎嘉琪 杨玉华 黄苗桩</p>

<p><strong>4 营老爷</strong></p>

<p><strong>Ying Lao Ye- Worshipping Activity in Chaoshan Region</strong></p>

<p>Ying Lao Ye- Worshipping Activity in Chaoshan Region 潮汕人很喜欢拜神明，而神明的另一个尊称也便是"老爷"，在潮 汕的各个乡镇都可以看到有村民自资建立起来的神庙，这些神庙供奉 着老爷。每逢一个特殊的节日，乡里人总会进庙去拜神，庙里总是香 火不断。以前拜神大多数是为了求风调雨顺，现今拜神的目的也各有 千秋。总之，神明在他们迷茫时给予他们一定的精神支持。 People in Chaoshan are keen on worshiping Shenming (it refers to a variety of Gods), which are also named "Lao Ye “. In Chaoshan, you can find temples that are fund and built by villagers to worship Lao Ye in every town. When it comes to special days, the villagers will go to the temple to worship Lao Ye and an endless stream of pilgrims keep flowing in the temple. In the past, people mostly prayed for good weather. But now, there are various purposes to worship Lao Ye. In short, Lao Ye can comfort people when people are confused. 潮汕地区早在5000 年前就有人类居住。当时的原住民为大闽越 族，自秦汉以后，中原汉族后裔辗转南至潮汕，与当地闽越族人交融 共生，经过上千年演变形成了今天的潮汕族群。移民至潮汕的居民把 他们当地的神明带过来，而原住民也有自己的神明。经过时间的融合， 两类不同的神明演变成今天潮州民俗文化里所存在的“老爷”。 As early as 5000 years ago, Chaoshan region was inhabited. At that time, the indigenous people were the Min-Yue nationality. Since Qin and Han Dynasties, the descendants of Han nationality from the central Plains migrated from the south to Chaoshan region integrating with the local, which formed into Chaoshan ethnic group. On one hand, the immigrants brought their Shenming with them. On the other hand, the indigenous people had their own Shenming. With the time went by, these two different Shenming combined into Lao Ye of Chaozhou's folk culture. 某种程度上讲潮汕话是最难学的方言之一，也一度被认为是古汉 语的活化石。其原因是潮汕话保留了许多古汉字的用法。比如说“营 老爷”的“营”字，“营”字在古汉语里面是指来回走动、飞来飞去 的意思。《诗经》中“营营青蝇”，也就是说这个苍蝇飞回飞去。 那么“营老爷”就是指抬着这个神像在村子里面兜几圈走来走去。 To some degree, Chaoshan dialect is considered as one of the most difficult dialects to learn and is regarded as a living fossil of ancient Chinese because it retains many usages of ancient Chinese characters. For example, the word "ying" from " Ying Lao Ye" means walking or flying around. For example, in the Book of Poetry, there is a phrase "Yingying Qingying", it means the fly flies back and forth. So"Ying Lao Ye " refers that the Lao Ye’s josses are carried to parade around the village.</p>

<p>听老一辈的人说，为感谢"老爷"的保佑，每年的某一个特别日子， 由自乡人以各种不同的形式将"老爷"请出庙，并在乡中主要街道的游 行。人们会在那一天早早地在街道等候着，烧香迎接"老爷"的到来， 营老爷的名字由此诞生并流传开来。每个村营老爷时，负责营老爷的 大多是村里年轻力壮的青年，刚刚结婚的年轻人优先。 It is said by the elder that there is a special day of a year when the villagers invite Lao Ye to go outside the temple in various forms and carry their josses to parade on the street so as to thank them. People on that day will wait on the street early, and burn incense to welcome the arrival of Lao Ye. The meaning of the word “welcome” in Chinese is pronounced “Huan Ying”, so the name of this worshipping activity “Ying Lao Ye” comes into being and passes on from year to year. When "Ying Lao Ye" is held in every village, it is the strong young man, especially the men who got married not long ago that has the priority to lift the josses. 营老爷所祭拜的最主要神明是“三山国王”。三山国王源自广东 潮汕一带，建于隋朝的广东揭西县河婆镇的霖田祖庙，就是"三山国 王"祖庙，距今已有1400 多年历史。 The most important deity to worship in Ying Lao Ye is the "King of The Three Mountains". Originated from Chaoshan region of Guangdong, it was constructed at the Lintian Ancestral Temple, Hepo town, Jiexi county, Guangdong province during Sui Dynasty with a history of more than 1,400 years. 营老爷期间最重要的活动是游行。由几百人组成游行队伍，有敲 锣打鼓的、有英歌锣鼓表演的，间有唱潮剧角色的。整条队伍沿着本 乡镇、临近乡镇的主要干道以及村内集体产业的建筑进行巡演。村民 手持纸钱和香烛迎接老爷，表示敬重和欢迎。</p>

<p>The most important event during Ying Lao Ye is parade. There are hundreds of people with drums and gongs, performing Yingge dancing and Chao Opera. The whole team will tour along the township, the main roads nearby and the village collective industry buildings. The villagers will greete Lao Ye with joss paper and incense to show their respect and welcome. 编译何世晶李玥潼林润铧</p>

<p><strong>5 卖身节</strong></p>

<p><strong>Selling Yourself Festival</strong></p>

<p>Selling Yourself Festival 云南傣族的泼水节颇负盛名，而在东莞市东坑镇也有一个特殊的 民间传统节日---卖身节。卖身节，亦称遇仙节，翻身节，起源于明 末清初，距今已有四百余年历史。每年农历二月初二，当地人们和游 客就会涌向东坑，欢度庆典，祈求“卖身遇仙”。 The Water-Sprinkling Festival of the Dai people in Yunnan is quite famous, and there is also a special traditional folk festival in Dongkeng Town, Dongguan City --- Selling Yourself Festival, also known as Meeting-an-immortal Festival. It originated in the late Ming and early Qing dynasties and has a history of more than 400 years. Every year on the second day of the second lunar month, local people and tourists flock to Dongkeng Town to celebrate the festival, hoping to “meeting an immortal when selling yourself” (have good luck). “卖身”充满农耕时代色彩。相传400 年前，在东坑塘唇村有位 卢姓大户，为了能赶在清明之前开耕，选在每年农历二月初二这个农 产品交易集市日，在村前贴出请农耕长工的启示。自此之后，相沿成 习，无业无田的青年，都在二月初二这天，坐在村前的围篱上，头戴 斗笠，身披粗布以示“卖身”，等待财主雇请。卖身节因此得名和流 传。 “Selling yourself” is a product of the agrarian age. It is said that 400 years ago, in Tangchun village of Dongkeng, a landlord surnamed Lu posted a notice of hiring long-term farm laborers in the village on the second day of the second lunar month, the local trading day of agricultural products, in order to catch up with the plowing before the Qingming Festival. Since then, young people who had no land and job sat on the fence of the village on that day, wearing bamboo hats and coarse cloths to show that they were selling themselves, which means selling their labor, and waited for the hire of the rich landlord. Therefore, the name of Selling Yourself becomes popular. 随着时间的推移，也有传说称，天仙下凡，到东坑观看“卖身”， 并行善事，普救众生，因此，卖身节也有人叫遇仙节。流传甚广的传 说如《曲磨臂》、《直鱼钩》、《金色的锄头》、《“东仔”故事》、 《糖不甩》、《连天阴雨，天必半日晴》等，皆与“遇仙”有关。于 是乎，二月初二这一天，百姓就会到街上行走以求遇见神仙。临归家 之时，人人都要买一件物品带回去，以示遇到了仙人，带回去好运。</p>

<p>As time goes by, there are also legends that celestial immortals come down to the earth to watch laborers selling themselves in Dongkeng, and do good deeds to save all living beings. Therefore, Selling Yourself Festival is also called Meeting-an-immortal Festival. Popular legends such as Bending and Grinding Arms, Straight Fishhook, Golden Hoe and Story of Dongzai, are all related to immortals. On that day, people will go to the street hoping to meet the immortals. When leaving, everyone will buy and bring back an item, meaning that they have met the immortals, and will have good luck. 历年来节日当天必定半晴半雨。水者财也，故近年来，每逢卖身 节，来自四面八方的游人成群结队，肩挂水枪，在东坑指定区域内射 水作乐，把节日的福气带回家。这是延续多年、游人自发、“以水为 财、湿身为乐”的一项民间特色娱乐活动。“射水”已经演变成为卖 身节的代名词，是节庆必不可少的主项目。前来射水狂欢的游客，都 希望在这一天，让东坑之水洒一身吉祥，带回一身好运。当然，节日 当天不止有射水，还有舞狮表演、各种各样的特色小吃。 Over the years, on the day of the festival, it must be half sunny and half rainy. Water means making money, so in recent years, groups of tourists from far and wide, hanging water guns on their shoulders and arms, shoot water in the designated area of Dongkeng to bring home the blessings of the festival. Water for money, and wet for pleasure. This folk characteristic entertainment activity has lasted for many years and is spontaneous by tourists. Water shooting has evolved into a symbol for Selling Yourself Festival, and it is indispensable for that tourists all hope the water can bring back good luck. Of course, there is not only water shooting, but also lion dancing and a variety of special snacks.</p>

<p>古时农耕卖身，今日创业兴邦。如今，卖身节已逐渐演变成展示 “坑土农耕文化”与“中华大地民俗风情”相融相通的文化盛典，成 为一年一度的“莞邑文化大节”。这一民间传统节日带动了当地经济 发展，焕发出勃勃生机。2007 年，卖身节成功被列为广东省非物质 文化遗产保护名录，申报过程中更被历史学家美誉为中国岭南民间流 传最早的“劳务集市”。这是东坑传承和守护历史文化的一个里程碑。 In ancient agrarian age, there was selling oneself to make a living. Today we start a business to prosper our country. Selling Yourself Festival has gradually become a grand cultural integration of Dongkeng farming culture and Chinese folk customs, and also the annual Dongguan Cultural Festival. It has driven the development of local economy, glowing with vitality. In 2007, Selling Yourself Festival has been listed in Intangible Cultural Heritage Protection of Guangdong Province. And in the process of declaration, it has been praised by historians as the earliest “labor market” in Lingnan area. This is a milestone in the inheritance and preservation of history and culture in Dongkeng. 编译陈劲松安妍颖赖晓丹吴秋蕾</p>

<p><strong>6 七月七水</strong></p>

<p><strong>Taishan’s Water on July 7th</strong></p>

<p>Taishan’s Water on July 7th 农历七月初七，俗称七夕节。在广东台山民间，有取七月七水贮 藏的习俗，七月初七在太阳升起前，各家即到山坑或河边取水储藏。 July 7th on the Chinese calendar is Chinese Valentine's Day. In China we call it Qixi Festival. In Taishan, Guangdong province, there is another folk custom of storing the water on that day. On July 7th, each family goes to the mountain pit or river for water storage before the sun rises. 在台山民间传说中，每年农历七月七日这一天，七个仙女脱光衣 服在河里裸泳，这时凡间的河水和井水因沾了仙气，水不仅不会变质， 还可辟邪治病延寿。因此，人们纷纷到河边、山坑或者水井将水挑回 家，用罐子贮存起来，这挑回来的水叫七月七水。又听闻台山人说道， 农历七月七日是七仙女下凡日，七仙女下凡救济凡人洒仙水，只要七 月七日那天人们将井水或山间水装进容器保存起来，这天的水经过多 年也不会变质，并且不用煮就可以喝。 According to Taishan folklore, on the 7th day of the 7th lunar month every year, seven fairies strip off their clothes and swim naked in the river. With fairy breath, the river and well water on earth will not only not deteriorate, but also can ward off evil spirits, cure diseases and prolong life. Therefore, people carry water home from rivers, pits, or wells and store it in jars. This water is called the water on July 7th. Taishan people also said that the 7th day of the 7th lunar month was the day when the seven fairies went down to earth to help the mortals and sprinkle fairy water on them. As long as people put well water or mountain water into containers on that day and keep it, the water would not deteriorate for many years and they could drink it without boiling. 传说七月七水功效神奇，洗头能醒脑，擦眼能明目，搓澡能壮阳， 饮用能健胃。七月七水可以用来治疗中暑、感冒、痱子等多种疾病。 因而，台山人汲七月七水为药饵，用来和药，还用来酿酒。此外，在 台山民间传统习俗中，冬瓜放入七月七水罐中储存，并放在阴凉处， 3 年后开埕饮用可清热解暑，去热清毒。 It is said that the effect of the water on July 7th is magical. It can refresh the brain by washing the hair, brighten the eyes by wiping, tonify the kidney by rubbing the body, and strengthen the stomach by drinking. It can be used to treat heat stroke, cold, prickly heat and other diseases. Therefore, Taishan people draw the water of July</p>

<p>7th as bait for medicine and wine.What is more, in Taishan folk custom, store the wax gourds in jars of water on July 7th and place it in a cool place for three years, and then drink it can clear away heat and detoxify the body. 七月七水在民间有史书记载。清道光年间《苍梧县志》：(七夕) 取河水、井水贮瓮，经久不变味，谓之“银河水”。民国年间《阳江 县志》：(七夕)正午时，取新汲井水贮之，以备和药，经岁不腐，谓 之“神仙水”。民国二十年《罗定志》亦记七夕水云：是日汲水，谓 之“天孙圣水”，以备醯酱、药饵之用。民国二十四年《贵县志》: (七 夕)汲河水贮藏瓮中，名曰“七月七水”，中热毒者每以之调药。 The water of July 7th is recorded in the folk history. Cangwu County Annals in the year of Daoguang in Qing Dynasty says that store the river and well water in a urn during Qixi Festival, we called that water “Yinhe Water”(means water from the Galaxy), and after a long time it’s taste will not change; Yangjiang County Annals in the Republic of China says that at noon on the Qixi Festival, people store new water to knead pharmaceuticals, after the age is not rotten, known as “the immortal water”. Luoding Annals(1931) also says that the water extracted on this day is called “Divine holy Water” and is used to prepare sauces and pharmaceutical baits. Gui County Annals(1935) says that the water stored in urn on Qixi Festival is known as “the water of July 7th”, and use it to adjust the heat poison. 过去台山隆文村曾经广泛流传一句话“七月七入河洗邪气”。台 山人普遍认为农历七月七这天河溪的水特别清凉，父母都会叫孩子去 河里洗身，寓意七月七水冲去小孩子身上的污浊。更有传说，七月七</p>

<p>傍晚在河里洗澡，人们可以看到七仙女在河里洗澡的影子。 In the past, Longwen village which located at Taishan, has been widely circulated a saying, “Wash away evil spirits by bathing in the river on the 7th of July”. It is generally believed in Taishan that on the 7th day of the 7th lunar month, the water in the rivers and streams is so cool that parents will ask their children to wash themselves in the rivers, which means the water will wash away the dirt from their children. It is also said that in the evening of July 7th, people can see the seven fairies bathing in the river. 台山民间七夕节取七月七水虽然带点神话色彩，但也反映了人们 对幸福追求的善良愿望，也不失为一道独特的民俗风景。 Though the custom of storing water on the 7th day of the 7th lunar month in Taishan is a bit mythological, it also reflects people's good wishes for the pursuit of happiness, and can be regarded as a unique folk scenery. 编译李思恩</p>

<p><strong>7 潮汕“闹热”</strong></p>

<p><strong>Naore——A Folk Custom of Chaoshan</strong></p>

<p>Naore——A Folk Custom of Chaoshan “闹热”，也叫“劳热”。这令每个潮汕人民都倍感亲切的词语， 是他们对一种节日的表达。“劳热”在潮汕话里是“热闹”的意思， “闹热”便是其正字。闹热也称“营老爷”，是潮汕人民最重视的游 神祭祀活动，也是潮州的非物质文化遗产之一。它庄严又喜庆，严肃 又热闹，这样的活动对于潮汕人民来说往往比过年还要重要。 "Naore" is also called "Laore". These words which make every Chaoshan people feel cordial, is an expression of a festival. "Lao re" means "lively" in Chaoshan dialect, and "Nao re" is its proper character. It is also called "Ying Laoye", which is the most important sacrificial activity of Chaoshan people and one of the intangible cultural heritages of Chaozhou. It is solemn and festive, serious and lively. To Chaoshan people, such activities are even more important than the Chinese New Year. 春节前后，一般在农历正月至二月期间，潮州乃至临近的汕头、 揭阳等地区的各个乡村都会举办这个民俗庆典活动，且不同村子的庆 祝时间不同。人们用游神赛会的形式庆祝丰收年，表达了对新年新气 象，国泰民安的美好愿望，祈求来年风调雨顺。 Around the Spring Festival, usually from the first month to the second month of the lunar calendar, Chaozhou and other villages in neighboring areas such as Shantou and Jieyang will hold this folk celebration, and the celebration time of different villages is varied. People celebrate the harvest year in the form of Youshen(god pageant ceremony) to express their good wishes for the new year,the country and the people, and pray for good weather and good harvest in the upcoming year. “闹热”民俗起源于潮州人民对土地的无比崇拜，在潮汕地区的 传承已有上千年的历史。每逢“闹热”活动，村民们会自发地将村子 装饰打扮漂亮，沿路彩缎灯笼高挂，家家户户张灯结彩，并在祠堂前 搭梁悬柱，构造一个放置神像的“神前”，用饰物装饰得满堂喜庆。 人们还会在神像前摆放“八仙桌”，家家户户将五牲、红桃粿等各色 祭品盛放于一个个红盘里，再整齐地供奉于神像前。村子中预先挑选 出来的“壮丁”将“老爷”（神像）请上神轿，再以标旗、仪仗队、 醒狮、大锣鼓、潮乐队等为前导，由本村村民自发组成的游神队伍喜 庆地穿梭在村子里的各个小巷，男女老少齐上阵，吹唢呐的、打鼓的、 敲锣的、扛大旗的、推游神车的等等，走遍乡镇的各条主要道路，最 后回到“神前”，祭拜仪式就开始了。</p>

<p>The folk custom of “Naore” originated from Chaozhou people's worship of land, which has been passed down in Chaoshan area for thousands of years. During this activities, villagers will spontaneously decorate the village, hang colorful satin lanterns along the road, decorate every household with colorful lights. In front of the ancestral temple, beams and pillars are put up to construct a "Shenqian(god front)" where gods are placed, and ornaments are used to make the house full of joy. People will also put the "Eight Immortals Table" in front of the statue, and every family will put the five sacrifices, red peach and other kinds of offerings in a red plate, and then consecrate them neatly in front of the statue.The pre-selected "strong men" invited the "Laoye" (Joss) to a sedan, and then led by the flag, honor guard, lion, gongs and drums, tide band, etc., a group of wandering spirits formed by villagers of the village happily shuttled through the alleys of the village. Men and women, old and young all joined in it by playing suona horn and drum, gonging , carrying the flag and carting sedan. People go all over the main roads of the town, and finally back to the ancestral hall, then the worship ceremony began. 在这一天里，每个村子从白天到黑夜都是锣鼓喧天、烟雾缭绕的， 祠堂前更是人山人海！村民们搭起好几个戏台，唱起潮剧，玩起木偶 戏，老少村民都沉浸在这份祥和喜庆的氛围中。“闹热”当天的午餐 也是相当重要的。每家每户会请大厨到自家制办宴席，邀请亲朋好友 一起来参加自己村子的这个活动并且在主人家用餐，在这一天，许多 远在他乡的潮汕人，都赶回自己的家乡参加这个活动，也就是人们口</p>

<p>中的“食劳热”。“闹热”，这富含潮州文化韵味的活动，将潮州千 年历史民俗文化演绎得淋漓尽致。 On this day, every villages from day to night is full of gongs, drums and smoke. At the same time, the front of the ancestral hall is full of people. The villagers set up several stages, sang Chao opera and played puppet shows. All the villagers, no matter old and young, were immersed in this peaceful and festive atmosphere. The lunch on this day is also very important. Every family will invite the chef to hold a banquet in their own home, and invite relatives and friends to participate in this activity in their own village and have dinner at the host's house. On this day, many Chaoshan people who are far away from home will come back to their hometown to participate in this activity, which is known as "Shi Laore". This activity, which is very Chaozhou style, fully interprets thousands of years of Chaozhou folk culture. 编译黄汶</p>

<p><strong>8 石龙木屐</strong></p>

<p><strong>Clogs in Shilong</strong></p>

<p>Clogs in Shilong 据史料记载，东莞尚绣花屐，以轻为贵。其中东莞石龙镇的传统 手工红漆描花木屐，选料精，颜色艳，图案美，有着步步高升、一帆 风顺、花开富贵、吉祥长寿等好意头，深受人们喜爱。不仅是日常行 走、乘凉的必需品，更是东莞人办结婚、乔迁、外出谋生活求学时必 不可少的行头。而且岭南地区湿热多雨，贫乏年代，人们经常赤脚行 走，很少能穿着鞋袜出行。而鞋底较高的木屐非常适合岭南地区梅雨 天气较多的气候特点，人们穿着木屐上街不湿鞋不湿脚，通风方便， 比草鞋、布鞋和皮鞋都实用，走在青石板上还会发出清脆的响声，让 人心情舒畅。 According to historical records, Dongguan is still embroidering, and light is more important. Among them, the traditional hand-painted clogs in Shilong Town, Dongguan, with fine selection of materials, bright colors and beautiful patterns, are well-intentioned and well-liked, such as rising step by step, smooth sailing, blooming and prosperous, and good luck and longevity. It is not only a necessity for daily walking and enjoying the cool, but also an essential outfit for Dongguan people to get married, move, and go out for a living and study. Moreover, the Lingnan area is humid, hot and rainy. In poor times, people often walk barefoot, and rarely travel in shoes and socks. The clogs with higher soles are very suitable for the climatic characteristics of rainy weather in Lingnan area. People wear clogs without wet shoes and feet, which is more practical than straw sandals, cloth shoes and leather shoes. Walking on the bluestone board will make a crisp sound and make people feel Jennifer. 说起木屐，不得不说起春秋五霸之一的晋文公与介子推的故事。 晋文公为逼隐居绵山的介子推回来，放火烧山，谁料孝子介子推并没 有背母下山，反而抱树而死。晋文公后悔莫及，命工匠用那树根做成 一双“木屐”，不时套在脚上，呼为“足下”以示敬之。从此，木屐 和清明寒食开始走进了人们的生活中，“足下”也成为一个敬辞，运 用至今。 Speaking of clogs, we have to tell the story of Jin Wengong and Jie Zitui. Duke Wen of Jin is one of the five tyrants in the Spring and Autumn Period. In order to force Jie Zitui who lived in mian mountain to return, Duke Wen of Jin set fire to the mountain. Unexpectedly, the filial son Jie Zitui did not carry his mother down the mountain, but he died holding a tree. Duke Wen of Jin was too late to regret it, and ordered the craftsman to use the tree roots to make a pair of clogs, from time to time on the feet, called "under the foot" to show respect. From then on, clogs and cold food on Tomb-sweeping Day began to enter people's life, and "under the foot" has also</p>

<p>become a wordy and is still in use today. 东莞石龙镇的传统手工红漆描花木屐，选料要精，颜色要鲜艳， 图案精美，非常喜庆，加上木屐（底）比较高，有着步步高升的好意 头而深受东莞人喜欢。尤其在过去，它可是东莞人办结婚、乔迁、外 出谋生活求学时必不可少的行头。每当有新人要成婚，按照东莞旧习 俗，天还未亮，姑娘早已梳妆打扮完毕，等待来接亲的丈夫。浩浩荡 荡的接亲队伍行至门口，姑娘穿着红色木屐缓缓走出家门，从此成为 人妻。新婚满一个月，新人的房间内又多了两对小木屐，意为求子求 福。纯手工做一双好看的木屐并非易事，从制板到最后完工，需要近 20 个工序，而石龙全手工红漆描花木屐制作更难，需要在木屐上绘 制松鹤、太阳、龙凤等传统山水花鸟花样元素，相互组合为寓意“一 帆风顺”“花开富贵”“吉祥长寿”等好意头的国画作品，需要有一 定的美术功底和美学修养。 In Shilong Town, Dongguan, the traditional hand-painted clogs painted with red paint are very festive, with bright colors and beautiful patterns. In addition, the clogs (bottom) are relatively high, and they are well-intentioned and popular among Dongguan people. Especially in the past, clogs are the essential things for Dongguan people before wedding, housewarming and going out for earn a living and study. Whenever a new person wants to get married, according to the old custom in Dongguan, before dawn, the girl has already finished dressing up and waiting for her husband to meet her relatives. The mighty wedding procession went to the door, and the girl walked out of the house wearing red clogs and became a wife from now on. One month after the wedding, two pairs of small clogs were added to the couple's room, meaning seeking happiness for their children. It is not easy to make a pair of beautiful clogs by hand. It takes nearly 20 working procedures from board making to final completion, but it is more difficult for Shilong to make wooden clogs painted with red paint by hand. It is necessary to draw traditional landscape flower-and-bird</p>

<p>pattern elements such as pine crane, sun, dragon and phoenix on the clogs, and combine them into Chinese paintings with good intentions such as "smooth sailing", "blooming wealth" and "good luck and longevity" 入行近30 年、与木屐为伴，与油漆为伍，辛苦了半生的梁锦泉， 虽然一如往昔，每天重复着打磨、画样、钉屐面等木屐制作步骤，但 作为东莞唯一会这门技艺的人，他对其技艺的传承忧心忡忡：再过几 年就不做了，也做不动了，随着年龄的增长，我的制作技艺如果还是 后继无人，以后也许就再也看不到这种木屐了。 Liang jingquan, who has been in this business for nearly 30 years, has worked hard for half his life with wooden clogs and paint. Although he repeats the steps of making clogs such as grinding, painting and nailing every day, as the only person in Dongguan who knows this skill, he is worried about the inheritance of his skills. He said, “I won’t do it in a few years, and I won’t be able to do it anymore. As I grow older,，if my production skills still have no successors, you may never see this kind of clogs again.” 为了把这种传统文化保存下来，并让更多人认识它，梁锦泉在材 料、绘画内容、包装等做了诸多新尝试，近年来，更是时常出入各类 课堂教学，频繁亮相各大“非遗”活动传艺。 In order to keep this traditional culture, and let more people know it, Liang Jingquan had tried many new attempts in materials, painting content, packaging, ect. In recent years, he has frequently visited various classroom teaching and frequently appeared in major “intangible cultural heritage” activities to convey art. 编译胡雯心</p>

<p><strong>9 巫氏传说</strong></p>

<p><strong>Surname-----Wu</strong></p>

<p>Surname-----Wu 巫氏是一个多民族、多源流的姓氏群体。从上古开始的巫氏家族， 几千年来，主要在平阳繁衍，古之平阳是巫氏族人的发源地。虽然历 史上称为平阳的地方有许多处，但是巫氏族人的原始源地平阳，是指 今山东邹县。 Wu (a surname) is a multi-ethnic group with multi origins. For thousands of years, the Wu family has mainly multiplied in Pingyang County, which is the birthplace of the Wu. Although there are many places called Pingyang in history, the original place of the Wu family is Pingyang County, which refers to today's Zou County, Shandong Province. 从《巫氏族谱》记载，巫氏之由来与其所司之职巫师、卜筮之官 有关。巫氏是古代的名门贵族，与中华几千年历史同流同源，是中国 古老的姓氏。在上古时代，巫族曾有过辉煌灿烂的年代，其影响极大、 流传甚广、历史之长。古代巫氏的地位是很尊贵的，巫氏和政治分不 开的，巫族从三皇五帝到商朝，社会地位一直都是很高的。在商朝有 巫贤父子宰相主持国家政务，大权在握，还有一些大夫级别的官员。 这些巫氏先辈们博通各艺，辐相国家，此乃巫氏的鼎盛时期。 According to Wu’s Genealogy, the origin of the Wu is related to the sorcerer or divinatory official. It is an ancient Chinese noble family with the same origin as the Chinese history of thousands of years. In ancient times, the Wu had a glorious period, which had a great and spreading influence and a long history. The positions of the Wu were very noble, which was inseparable from politics. From the Three Emperors and Five Emperors to the Shang Dynasty, the Wu ranked high on the social scale. In Shang Dynasty, there were two prime ministers, Wu Xian and his son, who were in charge of the state affairs, and there were also some scholar-bureaucrats of Shang Dynasty. These ancestors of the Wu had a wide range of skills and influenced the country, which was the heyday of the Wu. 巫氏的发源地主要有四个：“山西平郡县”，巫乾为平阳始祖； 福建省宁化县，巫罗俊为宁化始祖；福建省永定县，巫祈为始祖；广 东省兴宁县，巫禧为兴宁始祖。不论是哪里的巫氏，都是从这四个地 方迁出的，所以这四个地方称为巫氏的发祥地。而在巫氏族人的第二 次兴旺期，即南宋绍兴年间，十七世巫大郎的七个儿子分别从福建永 定县迁居广东韶关（今曲江县）杨梅，七子后裔散居在福建、广东各 地。至今，广东的肇庆、中山、阳江、台山等多地都有几百到几千的 巫氏。而肇庆的高要、怀集、广宁、四会等县都分布有巫氏族人。而</p>

<p>我就是定居在怀集县的巫氏族人之一。 There are four main birthplaces of the Wu: Pingjun County Shanxi Province, Wu Gan is the ancestor; Ninghua County Fujian Province, Wu Luojun; Yongding County Fujian Province, Wu Qi; Xingning County Guangdong Province, Wu Xi. No matter where the Wu is, they all emigrated from these four places, so these four places are called the birthplace of the Wu. In the second prosperous period of the Wu, that is, the Shaoxing Period of Emperor Song Gaozong in Southern Song Dynasty. Seven sons of the Wu XVII –Wu Da Lang moved from Yongding County of Fujian Province to Yangmei County Shaoguan City (today's Qujiang County) of Guangdong Province, and their descendants scattered all over Fujian and Guangdong. Up to now, there are hundreds of thousands of Wu clansmen in Zhaoqing City, Zhongshan City , Yangjiang City, Taishan City and other places in Guangdong Province. What’s more, the descendants of Wu distribute among Gaoyao District, Huaiji County, Guangning County, Sihui District of Zhaoqing City. I am one of Wu descendants who settled down in Huaiji County. 巫姓是客家人的大姓，子孙散布世界各地，各地族人常设家庙祭 祀巫罗俊公。根据客家族谱的系统分析，表明了客家人起源的主体是 北方中原汉人,很多传统大姓，如巫、伍、伊等都是来自北方的。记 忆中，怀集县族人每年的下半年都会有一个固定的时间跟广宁县族人 一起祭拜巫罗俊公等祖先，一般是每一户人家派代表去参加.而我家 中一般都是父亲参加这类型的活动。由于怀集县族人迁居，现在我们 基本上都不怎么讲客家话了，但是在祭祀祖先这一天我们还是会用客 家话问候对方。 Wu is the main surname of the Hakkanese. Their descendants spread all over the world, and the people of different places set up temples to worship ancestor Wu Luojun. According to the systematic analysis of Hakka Genealogy, it is indicated that the origin of Hakkanese is mainly from the Han nationality in the Central Plains of North China and many traditional surnames, such as Wu (high-level tone), Wu</p>

<p>(falling-rising tone) and Yi, came from the north. In my memory, in the second half of each year, descendants of Wu from Huaiji County and those from Guangning County would have a fixed day to worship ancestors such as Wu Luojun. Generally, every family would send representatives to participate in such worshipping activities, while my father usually joins in such activity on behalf of my family. Since descendants of Wu from Huaiji County migrate, we hardly speak Hakka anymore, but we still greet each other in Hakka on the day of ancestor worshipping. 虽然我们分布在不同的地方，但是我们还是会互相挂念，无论是 有什么喜事，都会通过电话等邀请族中兄弟前来庆祝，比如2019 年 我的升学宴。每一年的清明节，怀集县族人会去广宁县那边会合，一 起祭拜各祖先。而定居得稍微远一点的族人，如在广州和惠州等，由 于距离的限制，虽然没有办法那么频繁的会合，但是我们也是会在一 些重大的日子里相约见面、一起叙话家常的。 Although we live in different places, we still miss each other. Whenever there is any happy event, we will invite our clansmen to come to celebrate by phone, such as my entrance banquet in 2019. Every year on Tomb-sweeping Day, descendants of Wu from Huaiji County would meet in Guangning County and worship their ancestors together. However, descendants of Wu who live a little farther away, such as in Guangzhou City and Huizhou City, may not meet one another so frequently due to the limitation of distance, but we will meet and talk with each other on some important days. 编译巫小倩</p>

<p><strong>10 年例寄乡思</strong></p>

<p><strong>Reposing Nostalgia on Nianli Festival</strong></p>

<p>Reposing Nostalgia on Nianli Festival 粤西年例，中国独一无二的民俗，是粤西地区一个独特的传统节 日，所谓年例，即是年年有例。这是广东茂名、湛江地区民间过年最 隆重的一个节日。各地举办年例的时间各不相同，集中在过完春节的 农历正月和二月。 Nianli festival, the Chinese unique custom, is a special transitional festival in the west of Guangdong. As for Nianli, it represses there are festivals every year. It is the most ceremonious festival in the New Year of Maoming and Zhanjiang areas in Guangdong. The time of holding Nianlie is the first and the second month of the lunar calendar after the Spring Festival. However the exact time are varied from place to place. 年例节一般会维持三天，第一天叫“起年例”，第二天叫“正年 例”，第三天叫“年例尾”。农村年例大多以土地庙为中心，周围几 个村子一起举办。少数地方一年中还会举办两次年例。 Nianli festival usually lasts for three days: the first day is called the beginning of Ningli festival, the second day is called the middle of Nianli festival and the third day is called the end of Nianli festival. The Nianli festival is usually held in a temple and villages around the temple will hold the festival together. In a few paces, Nianli festival is held twice a year. 年例的由来历史悠久。据说年例和冼夫人有关联，史料中记载年 例是由冼氏家族所兴起的长期演变成为今天的年例。冼夫人在茂名地 区具有很大的影响力。她为国家统一、民族团结做出了巨大贡献。所 以在年例的游神活动中都会有冼夫人的神像，意在希望冼夫人能够保 佑当地村民幸福安康，风调雨顺。 Nianli festival has a long history. It is said that Nianli is connected with lady Xian. Historical records shows that Nianli festival was started by the Xian’s family and evolved into today’s Ninali. Lady Xian has a great influence in Maoming region. She has made a great contribution to the nation and ethnic unity. Therefore, the statue of the Goddess of lady Xian will be present on the god pageant, which means that lady Xian can bless local villages with happiness, good healthy and good weather. 在粤西地区有这样一个说法“年例大过年”。一年一度的年例期 间，在外工作、生活的人在年例时都会赶回来团聚。同操一种语言，</p>

<p>乡音乡情交融，气氛热烈，著实让常年在外、难得相见的家乡人别有 一番享，很大程度促进了人们对家乡的情怀。 There is a saying in western Guangdong that “Nianli festival is more important than the spring festival”. During the annual Nianli festival, people who work and live outside will come back for a reunion. The same language with the same local accent, the atmosphere is warm, which really gives those who are away from home all the year round and rarely meet with each other a unique experience of feeling their hometown. 著名的年例活动有在大街小巷游行的“飘色”，信宜镇隆、吴川 黄坡的飘色是民间艺术的珍宝。飘色是由两三个小孩化着妆，站在固 定的板上扮演神话故事和历史传奇人物。另外还有“贺丁灯”，“贺 丁灯”也俗称“点灯”。指的是如果某村有男丁出生，该户必须在村 里的庙前点一盏花灯，且在年例期间，灯内必须一直亮着长寿灯灯芯。 该户还需在年例的前一天摆“点灯酒”宴请亲朋好友。其次还有“睇 大戏”（粤剧），是各地年例必备的表演节目。 The famous Nianli activities including “Piaose”, “Heding Deng” and “Ti Daxi”. Piaose means two or three children in makeup parading on the street while standing on the settled board to impersonate mythical and historical figures. Piaose of Zhenlong(a town of Xinyi) and Piaose of Huangpo (a town of Wuchuan) are the treasures of folk art. Heding Deng us also commonly known as “Dian Deng”(He means congratulate, Ding or Dian means light, Deng means lamp). If a boy was born, this household must keep the longevity wick in a festive lantern light during the whole</p>

<p>Nianli festival in the front of the temple. The household also need to invite friends and relatives to “lighting feast” in the day before Nianli festival. Besides, Ti Daxi(means watching Guangdong opera), is the necessary performance on various region during Nianli. 每到年例各个乡镇都会搭好戏台，张灯结彩，请粤剧团来演出。 大戏一般都会从年例开始前演出一直到年例结束后，深受人们喜欢。 年例的活动除了上述外还有跳花棚、八音、花龙船等。 During Nianli festival, every town will set a stage, decorating with lanterns and streamers, and invite Guangdong opera troupe to perform. Opera is usually performed from the beginning of Nianli festival to the end of the Nianli festival, and are very popular with people. Nianli activities also including: Huapeng Dance,Bayin Sing, Flower Dragon Boat and so on. 对年例的庆祝和重视，寄予了人们美好的夙愿。人们祈祷这一年 能够风调雨顺，幸福安康。更使得人们牢记着传统文化习俗，也让更 多的年轻人认识和接触传统文化，围绕年例的冼夫人文化、潘茂名文 化、“好心文化”，都逐渐被人们所了解，促进了繁荣新农村文化的 发展。年例打开了粤西的大门，成为了粤西地区的明信片。年例使茂 名在广东的知名度越来越高。 The celebration and attention of Nianli festival, expresses people’s long-cherished wish. People pray for good weather, healthy and happy. It reminds people of traditional cultural customs and lets more young people to know and touch the traditional cultures. Madam Xian's culture, Pan Maoming culture, “Good-hearted culture” that related to Nianli festival are gradually understood by people, which promotes the development of a prosperous new rural culture. Nianli festival has introduced the western region of Guangdong to the other places, becoming the postcard of the western Guangdong area. Nianli festival also makes Maoming more and more famous in Guangdong. 编译莫晓君李怡</p>

