<h2>二、民间戏剧与歌舞</h2>

<p><strong>1 潮剧</strong></p>

<p><strong>Teochew Opera</strong></p>

<p>Teochew Opera 潮剧又被人们叫做潮调、潮州戏、白字戏等，是以方言为媒介， 对传统故事进行演唱的传统戏剧。主要是在潮汕地区以及在讲潮汕方 言的华侨、华裔聚居地区流行。据史料记载，潮剧在明朝时期已经形 成并且完善，流传至今已有400 余年的历史。 Teochew Opera is also called Chaodiao, Chaozhou Opera and Baizi opera which is a traditional opera with dialect as the medium to tell traditional stories. It is mainly spread in Chaoshan area and the places inhabited by Chinese speakers of Chaoshan dialect. According to historical documents, with a history of more than 400 years, Teochew Opera has been formed and perfected in the Ming Dynasty. 潮剧是文化碰撞与融合之后的产物。在元明时期，宋元南戏传入 潮汕地区后，盛行一时。于是，潮汕艺术家在汲取了宋元南戏精华的 基础上，结合了潮汕本土的优秀传统文化后创造出独具潮汕韵味的戏 剧——潮剧。而流传于海外的《班曲荔镜戏文》、《新刻增补全像乡 谈荔枝记大全》等的明代刻本以及《琵琶记》和和《刘希必金钗记》 这2 本手抄剧本的出土证明了这一点。 Teochew Opera is the product of culture collision and fusion. During the Yuan and Ming Dynasties, Southern Opera of Song and Yuan Dynasties became current after being introduced to Chaoshan area. Absorbing the cream of it and combining the excellent traditional culture of Chaoshan, the artists created the charms of Chaoshan opera——Teochew Opera. This can be proved by the Ming Dynasty editions of Banqu Lijing Opera and A Complete Collection of Litchi Stories in Xiangtan spreading overseas and the unearthed hand copied scripts such as the Tale of Pipa and the Story of LIU Xibi. 潮剧的表演内容主要取材于两部分。一部分是来自于宋元南戏里 的剧本，如:《刘希必金钗记》、《琵琶记》等，另一个则是基于潮 汕民间传说或世俗实事进行改编的故事。如:在潮汕地区非常有名的 一部戏《陈三五娘》，便是根据陈伯卿和黄五娘的爱情故事改编的。 There are principally two sources for the contents of Teochew Opera. Some are originated from the Southern Opera of the Song and Yuan Dynasties, such as the Story of LIU Xibi, the Tale of Pipa, etc. Others are based on Chaoshan folklore or adapted from secular matters. For example, Chen San and Wu Niang is adapted from the love story between Chen Boqing and Huang Wuniang which is an extraordinary famous</p>

<p>opera in Chaoshan area. 潮剧是以真声进行表演的，它的用调多样。主要有轻松愉快的轻 三六调，悲伤哀怨的活三五调，庄严肃穆的重三六调，凄惨哀伤的斗 鹌鹑调，曲调沉闷的锁南枝调。还有轻三六调的变体调—反线调，它 所适用的情景也是和轻三六调一样的。而由轻三六调，活三五调，重 三六调与反线调4 个调混用而成的犯腔犯调，则被俗称为四斗臭 （凑）。 Teochew Opera is singing with real voice and has various tunes. It mainly consists of relaxed and happy soft three or six tune, sorrowful and plaintive vibrating five tunes, dignified and solemn heavy three or six tune, sad quail tune and dull south branch of the lock tune. It also has variant of the soft three or six tune---the variant tune which is used in the same scenarios. The four tunes that are composed of soft three or six tune, vibrating five tunes, heavy three or six tune and variant tune are commonly known as Sidouchou (Cou). 但现在潮剧也面临着没落的局面。在现代，人们讲究的是高效率， 潮剧的慢节奏已不能符合人们的需求。且潮剧是以潮汕方言进行表演 的，局限于听得懂潮汕方言的人，所以要推广潮剧是特别难的。此外， 潮剧的内容仍停留在古时候的故事，与时代脱钩，相较于其他新颖的 有趣的娱乐方式，显然潮剧不能满足年轻人的胃口。而年轻人正是文 化继承的主力军，潮剧受众群体局限于中老年人，现状堪忧。因此， 对潮剧的改革势在必行。潮剧所具备的是古典的功能，而改革是要在 保留原有的精华的基础上为其注入新的元素。比如潮剧的曲调可保 留，但内容不能老生常谈，要注入一些现代的理念。既要重视中老年 人的诉求，也要挖掘具有发展潜力的年轻团体。除此之外，我们还要</p>

<p>挖掘潮剧的社会功能。潮剧是连接海外潮籍华侨与潮人之间的沟通桥 梁，潮剧对于华侨的影响还是举足轻重的，它能够慰藉华侨们的思乡 之情。因而我们要发扬潮剧的世界功能，将潮剧推广到海外。 But now Teochew Opera is also confronted with a declining situation. In modern time, people are particular about high efficiency and the slow rhythm of Teochew Opera cannot accord with the needs of people. Moreover, Teochew Opera is performed in Chaoshan dialect, which is limited to those who understand Chaoshan dialect. Therefore, it is very difficult to popularize Teochew opera. In addition, the content of Teochew Opera remains stories of ancient times, which is out of style. Compared with other novel and interesting forms of entertainment, Teochew Opera cannot satisfy the appetites of young people. Young people are the principal force of cultural inheritance. The present situation of the Teochew Opera is worrying since its audience is limited to the middle aged and elderly people. Therefore, the reform of Teochew Opera must be enforced. Teochew Opera has classical functions, and the reform is to retain the original essence based on its injection of new elements. For example, the tune of Teochew Opera can be retained, but the content should not be platitude, and some modern ideas should be poured into. We should not only attach importance to the aspirations of middle-aged and elderly people, but also tap young groups with development potential. Besides, we must excavate the social functions of Teochew Opera. Teochew Opera is a bridge between Chaozhou overseas Chinese and Chaoshan people, and its influence on overseas Chinese is still very important. It can comfort overseas Chinese's homesickness. Therefore, we should carry forward the world function of Teochew Opera and extend it overseas. 编译陈钰敏赖林忆</p>

<p><strong>2 紫金花朝戏</strong></p>

<p><strong>Zijin Hua-Chao Opera</strong></p>

<p>Zijin Hua-Chao Opera 花朝戏是河源市紫金山区成长起来的地方戏剧，2006 年5 月20 日，经中华人民共和国国务院入选第一批国家级非物质文化遗产名 录，成为了国家级非物质文化遗产之一。 The Hua-Chao Opera is a local opera that has grown up in The Zijin mountains of Heyuan city. On May 20, 2006, it was included by the State Council of the People's Republic of China in the first batch of national intangible cultural heritage list and became one of the national non-material cultural heritage. 据紫金的史料康熙二十六年的《永安县次志·永安县四十四图》 记载，花朝戏萌芽地永安县（今紫金），那时当地爆发病疫，人们纷 纷祭拜神佛，以保平安。因而有许多民间巫师会在祭祀时以边歌边舞 的形式请神遣将，这种活动形式被人们称作“神朝”。由此可见，紫金 花朝戏至少有300 多年历史。 According to the historical artefact of Zijin, the forty-fourth Chart of Yong’an County, in the twenty-sixth year of Kangxi's reign, there was an outbreak of epidemic in Yong’an County (today's Zijin), where the Hua-Chao opera originated. People worshipped the gods and buddhas in order to keep safe. Therefore, an increasing number of folk witches and wizards would invite the gods to dispatch their generals by singing and dancing during the ceremony, which was called the "a ceremony of worshiping gods". It is thought that the Zijin Hua-Chao opera has a history of at least 300 years. 花朝戏的传统剧目约有一百五十多出，代表剧目有《卖杂货》、 《秋丽采花》、《苏丹》等，花朝戏创作取材多种多样但主题特征较 为突出，主要取材于人们生活、广为人知的民间传说故事或者耳熟能 详的历史题材以此去表现当地人民的民俗风情、生产生活和内在的精 神追求，极具生活气息。 There are about 150 Hua-Chao plays, including Sell Groceries, Autumn Beautiful Flower Picking, Sudan and so on, created with various materials but distinctive characteristics, mainly based on people's life, well-known folklore stories or familiar history subject in order to show the local people's customs, production and living, and the inner spiritual pursuit, life extremely.</p>

<p>花朝戏在粤东客家地区广为流传，且在后来不断发展壮大曾有万 人争看的盛况。从最开始只是以简单的当地的小曲和说唱音乐相结合 方式，到后来花朝戏唱腔曲牌发展到100 多种，其中主要以神朝腔和 民间小调和客家山歌为主。唱调朴素健朗、抒情流畅，旋律优美。主 要以一人开腔领唱，众人帮腔和唱，唱念相间结合的演唱方式，花朝 戏具有强烈的表演性，在演唱过程中用高胡、二胡、扬琴、昆、喷呐 等乐器为其伴奏，载歌载舞使之营造出既喜庆又欢快的舞台氛围。 The Hua-Chao Opera was widely spread in the Hakka region of eastern Guangdong, and in later development, there were ten thousand people to see the grand spectacle. At the very beginning, it was a simple combination of local ditty and talking-and-singing music. Later, Hua-Chao Opera developed to more than 100 types of ditty, mainly composed of Shenchao tunes, folk ditty, and Hakka folk songs. Singing tone is simple and light, lyrical and fluid, and beautiful melody. In addition, it is a combination of singing and reading where one person leads the singing, and all join the chorus. Hua-Chao Opera is characterized by strong performance because Gao Hu, Erhu, Dulcinea, Kun, Pinna and other instruments are used to accompany it during the singing and the performance of singing and dancing makes it create a festive and cheerful atmosphere on the stage. 上个世纪，花朝戏以它独特的民俗性、通俗性，朴实优美唱腔， 诙谐幽默唱词，和大量客家语言的俚语、歇后语、双关语等口头语运 用深受乡村民众喜爱，从而催生出一大批流动的戏班子。但是后来由</p>

<p>于花朝戏为集镇赌场服务增多被认为有伤风化了，屡遭禁演，加上战 乱和灾荒，花朝戏一度濒临泯没。直到新中国成立后才恢复发展，但 是，在文化大革命初期被当作“四旧”又再次惨遭打压。直到1977 年 后才再度发展且重新出现繁荣景象。后来，1988 年中国戏曲家协会 主席曹禺为花朝戏题书为“山沟里的山茶花”’。 In the last century, Hua-Chao Opera, with its unique folkways and customs, simple and graceful singing, humorous lyrics, and a large number of hakka slang, a two-part allegorical saying, pun and other colloquial language, was deeply loved by the rural people, thus giving birth to a large number of mobile troupe. Later, however, as more and more Hua-Chao Opera served the casinos in the market town, it was considered indecent and was banned repeatedly as well as in times of war and famine, which was once on the brink of extinction. Until the founding of the People’s Republic of China, but it was suppressed again at the beginning of the Cultural Revolution for it was regarded as the "four olds". It was not until 1977 that it developed again and flourished again. Later, in 1988, Cao Yu, the chairman of the Chinese Opera Association, wrote a book entitled "Camellia in the Valley" for the Hua-Chao Opera. 花朝戏作为中国独一无二的稀有剧种，是紫金山区流传下来的古 老民间表演艺术，不仅只是一种戏曲，而且还是一种文化，它承载传 播了早期紫金人民的生活方式，在表演中融入了许多民间文化元素， 将舞蹈与音乐完美结合。如今，在响应习近平总书记提出的文化自信， 推进社会主义文化繁荣兴盛的口号下，紫金花朝戏已经正担负起引领 文化振兴的历史使命，积极在粤港澳城市巡演，成为紫金文化融湾的 靓丽文化名片。 As a unique and rare type of opera in China, Hua-Chao Opera is an ancient folk performing art handed down from the Zijin mountains. It is not only a kind of opera, but also a kind of culture. It carries and spreads the life style of the early Zijin people, blends many folk cultural elements into the performance, and perfectly combines dance and music. Now, in response to the slogan of promoting socialist culture prosperity and cultural confidence put forward by General Secretary Xi Jinping, Zijin Hua-Chao Opera has undertaken the historical mission of leading the cultural revitalization. It has been actively touring in Guangdong, Hong Kong and Macao cities, and has become a beautiful cultural card that Zijin Culture integrates into the Greater Bay Area. 编译钟文铃</p>

<p><strong>3《正字戏》——南戏的“活化石”</strong></p>

<p><strong>Zhengzi Opera -- "Living Fossil" of Southern Opera</strong></p>

<p>Zhengzi Opera -- "Living Fossil" of Southern Opera 正字戏是广东省汕尾市陆丰市地方传统戏剧，2006 年5 月20 日， 正字戏经中华人民共和国国务院批准列入第一批国家级非物质文化 遗产名录。 Zhengzi Opera is a local traditional opera in Lufeng District, Shanwei City, Guangdong Province. On May 20, 2006, Zhengzi Opera was approved by the State Council of the People's Republic of China to be included in the first batch of national intangible cultural heritage list. 正字戏，本名正音戏，用“中州官话”唱念，是一个多声腔古老稀 有剧种。明初南戏的一支流入粤东，后扎根海陆丰。并曾在港澳、台 湾、东南亚等地传播、演出。 Zhengzi Opera, whose real name is Zhengyin Opera, was performed in "Zhongzhou Mandarin". It is an ancient and rare opera with various tunes. In the early Ming Dynasty, a branch of southern opera spread to eastern Guangdong and took root in the Hailufeng area. It has spread and been performed in Hong Kong, Macao, Taiwan, Southeast Asia and other places. 正字戏有传统剧目2600 多个，分文戏和武戏两类。文戏有唱腔， 以正音曲和昆腔（唱牌子）两种唱腔为主、杂以乱弹、小调等。正音 曲以“奚琴”（别称二胡）领奏，昆腔以笛子、大小唢呐伴奏。武戏以 做工尤其是打斗为主，没有或少有唱腔，用吹打牌子伴奏，渲染气氛。 Zhengzi Drama has more than 2,600 traditional repertoire. It can be divided into the military plays and the singing plays. Wenxi (Chinese operas characterized by singing and acting) has vocal music, consists largely of Zhengyin opera and tunes of Kunqu opera, two types of singing mainly, mixing with strumming, ditty and so on. Zhengzi opera is led by "Xilinx" (also known as the Erhu fiddle), and the tunes of Kunqu opera is accompanied by flute and suona horn. Military plays consist largely of action and expression of opera, especially fighting action, have no or little vocal music, with the accompaniment of beating plank, rendering the atmosphere. 正字戏传统有红面、乌面、白面、正生、武生、白扇、正旦、花 旦、帅主、公末、婆、丑等十二行当。 The tradition of Zhengzi opera includes Red pattern of the make-up (a symbol of loyalty, integrity, and the hot-blooded), Black pattern of the make-up (the expression</p>

<p>character is serious，is a neutral role, represents the courage and wisdom）, White pattern of the make-up (show suspicious, containing derogatory sense, representing fierce fraud）, Zhengsheng (the hero in Chinese operas), Wusheng (an actor playing a martial role in Chinese operas), Baishan（the military counselor in a clique), Zhengdan (main female role in Chinese operas), Huadan (female role in Chinese opera), Shuaizhu (General), Gongmo (duke）, Po（an old female character type in Chinese operas), Chou (funny characters in Chinese opera) and so on. 正字戏脸谱有毛面、水龟目、鹰咀、虎目等200 多种图案。 The painted faces concerned include more than 200 patterns including hairy face, terrapin eye, eagle beak, and tiger eye. 文戏剧目，明代有宣德七年《正字刘希必金钗记》、嘉靖年间《蔡 伯皆》出土的南戏抄本。另外，今仍保存着一批较完整的清代、民国 抄本，以及20 世纪50 年代的记录本。有“四大喜戏”《三元记》、《五 桂记》、《满床笏》、《月华缘》，“四大苦戏” 《荆钗记》、《葵 花记》、《琵琶记》、《白兔记》，“四大弓马戏”《义忠烈》、《千 里驹》、《铁弓缘》、《马陵道》，统称十二真本戏。 In the Ming Dynasty, there are transcript of Southern Opera: the remarriage of Liuxibi in the seventh year of the reign of Ming Emperor Xuande, and Caibojie in the reign of Ming Emperor Jiajing. In addition, a number of relatively complete</p>

<p>transcripts of the Qing Dynasty and the Republic of China are still preserved today, and records from the 1950s. The four comic operas: "Won Three Trophies", "the five guangxi", "full bed wat", and "stripe edge". The "four tragic operas: "the Romance of A Hairpin", "Sunflower", "The Story of Pipa", and "White Rabbit". The "four big bow circus": "the Valiant Ones of Righteousness", “Stallion", “Romance of the Iron Bow " and " Malingdao ", generally referred to as the twelve intact operas. 其他传统剧目中，正音曲戏属弋阳腔、青阳腔系统，其中有《封 神榜》、《古城记》等史传戏和《目连救母》、《金印记》等传奇。 Among the other traditional operas, Zhengyin opera belongs to the system of Yi-yang and Qing-yang cavity. There are the historical operas: the Legend of Deification and the Tale of The Ancient City, the legendary drama: Deliverance of Mulian’s Mother, and the Mark of Gold. 牌子以大锣、大鼓、大唢呐演奏，应用于武戏，善于制造气势磅 礴的古战场气氛。 The Kunqu opera plays on big gongs, big drums and big suona, which is good at creating the magnificent atmosphere of the ancient battlefield, used in military plays. 正字戏表演风格古朴、气派宏大，特别擅演“三国”连台本戏。武 戏气氛热烈火爆，有独特、精彩的抖靠旗、抖肌肉、抖髯口、追赶以 及古老的跑布马、独特的南派武功等表演程式，和逼真的对阵、开打 形式。各种排场运用自如，善于表现各种历史、军事场景。 Zhengzi Opera performance style is simple, grand, especially good at "Three Kingdoms" series. Military opera has warm atmosphere, and has a unique and excellent performing form, like shake KaoQi, shaking muscles, shake RanKou, pursuit and horse that made of cloth, and has realistic encounter and perform fighting. can use all kinds of ostentatious freely, good at showing a variety of historical, military scenes. 在我的家乡陆丰，每逢春节，中元和中秋等佳节，村里人都会“捡 丁钱”（一种筹钱的方式）到戏团里请戏班子过来唱上整夜的戏。春 节期间，常在正月初八设戏，人们管它叫“开丁戏”，寓意祝贺添丁。 正字戏分两场：上半夜和下半夜，上半夜晚上8 点到12 点，主要唱 的是武戏。下半夜为凌晨1 点到5 点，唱文戏。每逢佳节，戏坛那块 区域便是最为热闹喜庆的地方，大人小孩酣赏一场戏曲盛宴，遇上重 头戏时常常拍腿叫绝，场下座无虚席。</p>

<p>In my hometown, Lufeng, at every Spring Festival, Ghost festival, Mid-Autumn Festival and other festivals, the villagers will "collect Ding Qian" (a way to raise money) to the troupe invited the them to sing the play all night. During the Spring Festival, they are often operas on the eighth day of the first lunar month. People call it "Kaiding Opera", which means congratulations on the birth of a child. There are two scenes: “before midnight”, which is from 8 p.m. to 12 p.m., mainly play military operas. “and the “after midnight” is from one to five in the morning. Every festival, drama altar that area is the most lively and jubilant place, adults and children heartily appreciate a drama feast, the highlight of opera is stunning, all seats are occupied. 正字戏历史悠久，风格古朴，具有浓厚的岭南特色和丰富的遗产 价值；同时，正字戏是古老南戏的变体，为戏曲声腔的流变和地方文 化对戏曲的影响等研究提供了珍贵的材料。具有很大的传承价值。 Zhengzi Opera has a long history, primitive style, strong Lingnan characteristics and rich heritage value; at the same time, Zhengzi opera is a variant of the old Southern opera, which provides precious materials for the study of the changes of the opera tune and the influence of local culture on the opera. It has great inheritance value. 编译林倩婷</p>

<p><strong>4 揭阳“皮猴戏”</strong></p>

<p><strong>Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show</strong></p>

<p>Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show 揭阳铁枝木偶俗称“皮猴戏”，又称“纸影戏”，是中国汉族木 偶艺术的稀有品种，系由南宋时期随中原移民传入的皮影戏演变而 来。木偶戏（揭阳铁枝木偶戏）已于2011 年入选第三批国家级非物 质文化遗产代表性项目名录。揭阳铁枝木偶戏因其剧目、唱腔与表演 都具有潮剧的特色，故有“微型潮剧”之称。 Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show, commonly known as "Monkeys Play", or "Paper Shadow Theatre ", is one of the rare puppet arts of Chinese Han nationality. It evolved from the shadow play introduced by immigrants from the Central Plains in the Southern Song Dynasty. Puppet Show (Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show) has been included in the third batch of national intangible cultural heritage representative projects list in 2011. It is called "mini-Chao Opera" as well, since it features the Chao Opera in terms of list of operas, types of singing and performance. 清代以后，为满足观众视觉欣赏需要，纸影戏台也改“现影”为 “现形”——艺人们把舞台蒙上的白纸去掉，把皮影人物改为皮手木 足，头部由细泥塑成，面部用油彩绘成潮剧各种角色的脸谱，躯干用 稻草扎成，腿臂用布帛裹连，身着戏服。木偶体高为24cm-45cm，两 手及背后均连有铁线及部分为细竹所包裹的“皮猴筷”，供幕后艺人 操纵。在当时称为“圆身纸影”。戏班演出时先要搭建舞台，台上铺 着草席，操纵木偶的人盘膝而坐。这一重大改变，纸影戏已变化为铁 枝木偶戏。 After the Qing Dynasty, to satisfy the visual appreciation of audience, the station for Puppet Show was changed not to "show the shadow" but to "show the appearance" ——Artists removed the paper-made white backdrop from the stage and changed the paper figures into the ones with leather hands and wooden feet. Their heads are made of fine clay, their faces are painted into masks of various characters in Chao opera, their trunks are bounded with straw, and their legs and arms are wrapped in cloth and costumes. At about 24cm to 45cm high, those figures’ hands and back are connected with iron wire, except for some bamboo-legged "Monkeys Chopsticks" being operated by backstage artists. Due to these features, it was called "Round Body Paper Shadow". Prior to the show, a stage should be built up with straw mats where performers can sit, cross-legged, to make performances. These major changes have turned the Paper Shadow into Iron-stick Puppet Show. 铁枝木偶偶像由连在后面的三枝铁枝操纵，保留了皮影操纵特 点；剧目、表演动作、音乐唱腔与潮剧相同；表演时，台内仅有五、 七个人，包揽了生、旦、净、丑各行角色的表演唱和鼓乐，故潮俗有</p>

<p>“手打鼓、脚打锣、口唱歌、头壳撞深波”；基本表演手法有：推、 拉、提、拨、抖等，表演过程根据人物行当和剧情需要表演飞天、入 地、点火、射箭、骑马、张扇、划船、武打等动作，呈现独特的操纵 技艺。 The Iron-stick Puppet, braced by three iron sticks in the back, has the same operation as the Paper Shadow, and similar list of operas, types of singing and performance as the Chao Opera. While playing, only five to seven people sing or play drums in the stage, covering all the roles of Sheng, Dan, Jing and Chou. Therefore, there was a popular saying that "beating drums by hands, beating gongs by feet, singing by mouth, hitting gong by head (to describe someone who is very busy with his hands, feet, mouth and head.)". Pushing, pulling, lifting, plucking and shaking are the basic performance techniques. But these can be evolved into flying in the sky, coming down to the ground, firing, archery, horseback riding, fanning, rowing, martial arts and other movements based on characters and plots. All of these are of high skills. 揭阳铁枝木偶在明代中期以前，是唱正音的，即以中州音为标准， 所以叫“正音戏”或“正字戏”。明代中期，潮音戏开始形成。清代 中期潮音戏已很普及，但很多纸影戏仍保留唱正音戏。清末“竹窗纸 影”改为“阳窗纸影”以后，才大多改唱潮音戏。民国初年至本世纪 三、四十年代，揭阳铁枝木偶戏班虽已唱潮音戏（潮剧）了，但还保 留眉幕上绣上“正音班”三个大字，以表示他们对正音戏的怀念和尊 崇，向观众说明他们的剧种是来自梨园正宗的。</p>

<p>Before the mid Ming Dynasty, Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show was also called "standard pronunciation opera" or "standard words opera" as its pronunciation was based on the Zhongzhou accent. In the middle of Ming Dynasty, Chao Opera came into being. In the middle of Qing Dynasty, though Chao Opera was very popular, many Paper Shadow Operas still retained the standard pronunciation opera. At the end of the Qing Dynasty, especially when "bamboo window paper shadow" was changed to "balcony window paper shadow", Chao pronunciation opera was mostly adopted. From the early years of the Republic of China to the 1930s and 1940s, though Chao opera was integrated into the Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show, the characters of " standard pronunciation class" were still embroidered on the grand valance, showing their memory and respect for standard pronunciation opera and also showing the audience that their opera was from the orthodox school of Liyuan. 民国时期，揭阳铁枝木偶剧更为兴盛。1945 年，仅渔湖一乡就 有纸影戏班22 班。可以说村村有纸影戏班，多的还有二至四个班。 新中国成立后，揭阳铁枝木偶戏班和铁枝木偶戏的演出，显著减少。 现在只有在一些重大祭神期间会请戏班来演出，但也是越来越少。 During the Republic of China, Jieyang Iron-stick Puppet Show was more prosperous. In 1945, Yuhu town alone boasted 22 paper shadow play classes. It was no exaggeration to say that every village has at least one paper shadow play class and each of some has even two to four classes. However, after the founding of People’s Republic of China, Iron-stick Puppet troupes and the performance of Iron-stick Puppet Show in Jieyang have seen a significant decrease. Now a troupe is only hired to play during major festivals, but it’s getting less and less. 随着人们艺术欣赏时尚的改变，演出市场日益萎缩；木偶戏班大 多为半农半艺，是松散形业余艺术团体，对木偶戏的研究传承具有一 定难度，特别是一些高难表演技艺面临失传，必须采取有效措施加以 保护、传承。 As people have been changing their artistic tastes in fashion, the market for puppet performance has been shrinking accordingly. Most of the puppet show performers are loosely organized amateur art groups, because they usually play aside from farming. It, therefore, is difficult to carry on the research of puppetry, let alone the dying highly-skilled performance skills, which should be protected and carried on more effectively. 编译陈依雯</p>

<p><strong>5 龙川手擎木偶戏</strong></p>

<p><strong>Longchuan Hand Puppet Show</strong></p>

<p>Longchuan Hand Puppet Show 木偶戏具有悠久的历史。根据史料记载，木偶戏始于汉代，唐代 时盛行，在两宋时期快速发展，到了明清时期木偶戏在全国普及。随 着木偶戏的发展，不断出现了晋江布袋木偶戏、漳州布袋木偶戏、临 高木偶戏、龙川手擎木偶戏等具有地方特色的传统木偶戏。龙川手擎 木偶戏的表演生动形象，故事精彩有趣，很受龙川人民的喜爱。 The puppet show has a long history. According to historical records, the puppet show derived from the Han Dynasty, prevailed in Tang Dynasty, developed in the Song Dynasty and popularized throughout the country in the Ming and Qing Dynasties. With the development of the puppet show, there appeared various traditional puppet shows with local characteristics, such as Jinjiang glove puppet show, Zhangzhou glove puppet show, Lingao Puppet show, and Longchuan hand puppet show. Longchuan hand puppet show is particularly favored by its locals due to the vivid performance and the fascinating stories. 龙川手擎木偶戏是龙川县的民间传统戏剧。1914 年，木偶戏由 骆七和骆三从福建泉州传入龙川，传入时是提线木偶、杖头木偶的形 式，经过一百多年的不断创新发展，形成了现在龙川特有的手擎木偶 戏。在发展初期，出现了许多木偶班。其中，黎咀虎口村的两个提线 木偶班—“兆丰年”和“贺丰年”最为出名。 Longchuan hand puppet show is a traditional folk drama of Longchuan county. It was introduced by Luo Qi and Luo San in 1914 to Longchuan from Quanzhou, Fujian Province. Back then, it was stringed puppet and stick puppet. Through hundred years of development and innovation, the show has gradually evolved into what we now know “ Longchuan hand puppet show” . At the initial stage of its development, many troupes appeared, among which "Zhao Fengnian" and "He Fengnian" are the best known puppet troupes in Hukou village, Lizui. 龙川手擎木偶戏的表演具有丰富的地方特色。木偶戏有很多不同 的角色，例如生、旦、丑、公、婆等。其伴奏音乐也有多种形式，例 如民间小调、采茶调等，而唱腔一般以客家山歌唱腔为主，所唱之词 及对白多采用客家方言，表演风格极具地方特色。表演的剧目也有很 多，但主要传统剧目有：《苏小妹三难新郎》、《夜打登州》、《梁 山伯与祝英台》、《孙悟空大闹天宫》等。 The performance of Longchuan hand puppet show has rich local characteristics. Puppet shows have many different roles, such as Sheng, Dan, Chou, Gong and po. Its accompaniment music also has many forms, such as folk ditty, tea picking tune and so on. Generally speaking, the singing is mainly Hakka folk song, and the words and</p>

<p>dialogues are mostly in Hakka dialect, so the performance style has local characteristics. There are many operas performed, but the main traditional operas are: Su Xiaomei's Three Difficulties with the Bridegroom, night fighting in Dengzhou, Liang Shanbo and Zhu Yingtai, Monkey King's havoc in Heaven, etc. 手擎木偶戏在龙川的发展是曲折的。1955 年，“龙川县线剧团” 被广西收编后，曾经风靡一时的手擎木偶戏在龙川销声匿迹。直到骆 锦标从广西回来，组建了“龙川黎咀木偶剧团”，龙川木偶戏才逐渐 回到龙川人民的视野。但后来又因为编制的问题，剧团解散，木偶戏 的声音再一次消失在龙川的街头。直到2004 年，龙川黎咀木偶剧团 才再次成立。 The development of Longchuan hand puppet show has seen many twists and turns. Since "Longchuan County line Opera Troupe" was incorporated by Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region in 1955, the hand puppet show, once extremely popular in Longchuan, disappeared. It was not brought back to Longchuan only until Luo Jinbiao came back from Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region to organize the "Longchuan Lizui Puppet Troupe". But later the hand puppet show disappeared here once again due to the troupe’s improper running and disorganization. Until 2004, the Longchuan Lizui Puppet Troupe was finally established again. 龙川木偶戏传承到现在已经有四代人的历史。骆锦标是手擎木偶 戏的第三代传人，他不仅延续了传统木偶艺术，而且促进了地方戏剧 的发展，丰富了地方的文化特色。在2017 年时，他的儿子骆志鸿也 被评为广东省第五批非物质文化遗产代表性传人。为了传承和发扬木 偶戏这个传统艺术，骆氏传承人做出了巨大的贡献。</p>

<p>Longchuan puppet show has, by far, been witnessed by four generations. As the inheritor for the third generation, Luo Jinbiao not only passed down the traditional puppet arts, but also promotes the development of local drama, enriching the characteristics of the local culture. In 2017, Luo Zhihong, the son of Luo Jinbiao, was also rated as the fifth batch of representative inheritors of intangible cultural heritage in Guangdong Province. In order to enrich the traditional art of puppet show, the Luos have devoted all their lives. 龙川手擎木偶戏的发展是传统戏剧的传承，更是文明的进步，它 对反映当地人民生活和丰富当地文化起着积极的作用。同时，手擎木 偶戏的发展与龙川木偶戏的发展息息相关，对岭南文化的发展也有重 要意义。 The development of Longchuan hand puppet show not only represents for the inheritance of traditional drama, but also the progressiveness of civilization. It plays an active role in reflecting local people’s lives and enriching their culture. At the same time, it is also of great significance to the development of Longchuan puppet show as well as Lingnan culture. 编译黄蓉</p>

<p><strong>6 潮汕社戏</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chaoshan Village Opera</strong></p>

<p>Chaoshan Village Opera 《三国志》记述“祭南北郊”，南城郊外祭天，北城郊外祭地。 这边以酒肉祭神，同时，另一边以演戏祭社，这样的戏就叫“社戏”。 显而易见，这就是人办给神看的戏，神明一高兴，村里风调雨顺，村 民也自然安居乐业。人们将自己喜欢的事物投射到神明的崇拜中，也 是祈求美好的一种愿望。 According to the Annals of Three Kingdoms Records, "the southern and northern suburbs of the city were places for worship". While the god of heaven was sacrificed in the southern suburbs with the Chinese spirit and meat, the god of land was worshiped in the northern suburbs with opera. And such opera is called "village opera". It apparently was designed for pleasing the gods. If the gods are pleased, everything in the village would go on well and villagers there would live and work in peace and contentment. It is also people’s wishes for happiness to add their favorites into worship. 潮汕社戏一般被认为兴盛于唐宋时期，几乎每个村庄、寨子或社 区都立有“土地庙”、“土谷祠”或祖宗的祠堂。潮汕民间以祭社为 中心形成了居民社会组织逐步形成村落或社区。社戏就是这些村落或 社区中每年所演的“年度大戏”。“社戏”一般有庙会戏、祠堂戏、 喜庆戏等，大部分以庙会戏为主。每逢如关帝、妈祖、城隍、土地等 的诞辰，神庙所在的乡村会举办祭祀活动，请来剧团演戏。 Chaoshan village opera has been believed to be flourished during the Tang and Song dynasties, when almost every village or community had "Temple of the land god", "Tugu ancestral Hall" or ancestral temple. Around these places, social organizations for residents were established by Chaoshan folks and they gradually turned into villages or communities. There, village opera was performed annually as the “Opera of the Year”. It generally contains temple opera, ancestral temple opera, festival opera, etc., most of which are temple fair operas. On each and every birthdays of Guan Di, Mazu, Cheng-Huang and The earth, the villages which boast these temples will hold sacrificial activities and invite theatrical troupes to perform. 社戏除了潮剧之外，还有木偶戏和皮影戏，现在还会放一些现代 电影等，为了让神明看了高兴，大多是些吉利戏。值得一提的是，随 着时代的变化，潮剧不但有了现代新编的剧，在艺术形式也上与时俱 进，受到一些年轻人的喜爱。 In addition to Chaozhou opera, village opera also came with puppet shows and shadow puppet shows. Nowadays, some modern movies, mostly auspicious movies,</p>

<p>are shown to make the gods happy. Most of all, Chaozhou opera not only renews with modern scripts, but also adopted the latest art forms. It therefore is favored by youngsters. 比较盛大的社戏是农历三月廿三日庆祝祭妈祖生辰的日子。传说 妈祖曾经多次解救海上遇难的渔民，帝王也多次赐匾颂扬，沿海渔民 祈盼出海一帆风顺，渔业兴旺，商贸发达，为了纪念这个民间道教的 奇女，于是将其奉为神明崇拜。戏台上，穿着光鲜华丽戏服的女子或 凄凉或轻巧的唱着潮音，戏台旁隐去的潮乐跟随着主角的情绪奏出摧 情的旋律，戏台下的老人用心倾听着主角的故事，时而眉头紧锁，时 而拍手叫绝，戏台上主人公的一举一动都牵动着他们的心。 The grand village opera falls on March 23rd of the lunar calendar to celebrate the birthday of Mazu. Legend has it that Mazu has rescued fishermen from distress on the sea many times and thus received plaques awarded by the emperor. Coastal fishermen prayed to her for smooth sailing, prosperous fisheries and flourishing trade and commerce. In order to commemorate this legendary Taoist girl, people worshiped her as a god. Theretofore, a glamorously-dressed women sang the tide sounds desolately or lightly on the stage with changing background melodies to create similar atmosphere, while the elders under the stage listened to it with rapt admiration. They sometimes frown, sometimes clap and exclaim, and was affected by every move of the actor.</p>

<p>戏台之上，有的是善良美好的化身，也有保境安民，为国家作出 贡献的忠臣良将、民族英雄。潮汕人以庙会祭祀的方式寄托着对忠勇 正义的先圣前贤的敬仰之情。有人说，举办庙会演唱社戏浪费人力财 力，庆祝庙会时点燃的鞭炮更是污染空气，这种没有科学依据的迷信 活动应该消失。 On the stage, some roles are embodiment of goodness and beauty, some are loyal ministers and others are national heroes. The people of Chaoshan pay tribute to saints and sages for their loyalty, bravery and justice by offering sacrifices to the temple fair. Some people claim that such superstitious activities should be discarded as holding temple fairs and singing social operas is a waste of manpower and financial resources and the firecrackers lit during the celebration of temple fairs pollute the air. 潮汕社戏不能只看到迷信的一面，还应该理解其漾溢着文化生活 和联谊的良性一面。这是人们庆祝农业、渔业、商贸的丰收，祈盼风 调雨顺，安居乐业的美好愿望；是人们辛勤劳作商暇后的心灵慰籍， 也是农村、社区的文化生活享受。应该好好的传承下去。 People shouldn’t just fixate on superstition of Chaoshan village opera. Instead, they should understand that it also reflects the benefits of culture, life and friendship. It is a good wish for people to celebrate the bumper harvest of agriculture, fishery, commerce and trade, and to live and work in peace and contentment. It is both the spiritual comfort for people after tedious labor work or trade affairs, and the enjoyment of cultural life in rural areas and communities. All these make it critical to be passed down. 编译黄泳思罗丽珊余泽娜</p>

<p><strong>7 潮州歌册</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chaozhou Folk Songs</strong></p>

<p>Chaozhou Folk Songs 潮汕歌册，也称为歌仔、笑歌（呱），是用潮汕方言说唱的歌词 本子，为潮州俗文学中最流行的说唱文学。主要流行于潮汕、闽南地 区以及东南亚的潮人群体中。曾是潮汕地区街头巷尾随处可见的演 唱，如今却不见踪迹。 The Chaozhou folk songs, also known as the Song or Laughing Song (quack), is a book of lyrics singing in Chaoshan dialect. It was the most popular pros metric and verse narrative in Chaozhou and Shantou, (abbreviated to Chaoshan), Southeastern Guangdong Province. It enjoyed great peculiarities among Minnan and Southeast Asian communities. It used to be seen everywhere in Chaoshan, but now it is traceless. 据学者考究，歌册形成于明代，盛行于清乾嘉年间，由唐朝的潮 州弹词演变而来。歌册大多是七个字一句，以潮汕话押韵，古风古韵。 潮州歌册的题材大致可分为四大类：一、由历史演义小说改编，如《隋 唐演义》；二、由历史知名公案编写，如《七尸八命》；三、由才子 佳人的故事编写，如《西厢记》；四、由地方故事民间传说编写，如 《苏六娘》。这四类题材都属于一种传奇故事体的体裁，还有一种体 裁是歌行体，有些碎片化，以介绍某一事物或以某一社会现象为题材， 如《戒赌歌》、《百花名》等。 Scholars in this regard reported that the folk song, evolved from the Chaozhou storytelling in the Tang Dynasty (618-907), was formed in the Ming Dynasty (from 1368 to 1644) and prevailed during the ruling of Emperor Qianlong and Emperor Jiaqing in the Qing Dynasty (about 1736 to 1796). The folk songs boast ancient charm as each line of most songs contains seven words and rhymes with the Chaoshan dialect. Chaozhou Folk Songs can be classified into four categories: firstly, songs adapted from historical novels, such as The Romance of the Sui and Tang Dynasties; secondly, songs compiled from famous historical cases, such as Seven Corpses and Eight Lives; thirdly, songs from stories of gifted men and elegant ladies, such as the Romance of the Western Chamber; fourthly, songs compiled according to local stories and folklore, such as Su Liuniang. All these belong to the legendary int terms of its types. Another genre is fragmented song form and it often themed on things or social phoneme like the Song of Quiting Gambling and The Name of a Hundred Flowers. 潮州歌册对潮州妇女的精神熏陶、普及文化教育起到无法估量的 作用。由于古代私塾只陪养预备考取功名的学生，潮汕人便创造出歌 册来弥补女性的教育缺失。歌册的传唱者多数是女性，不仅主唱者是 女性，听唱的群体也是妇女儿童。从学唱歌册的年龄来看，大多数女</p>

<p>性是在20 岁时候开始的，而且其唱歌册最痴迷的时期大都是在15-22 岁之间。民国时期是潮州歌册发展最兴盛的时代，出版业的发展加上 新学堂招收女学生，认识字的女孩自发充当老师，教同辈认字，没机 会读书的女孩儿则在歌册里面了解历史，接受文化，歌册的教育功能 更加彰显。历史学家称其为“潮汕历史上独有的女子文化”。 Chaozhou Folk Songs play an inestimable role in popularizing general knowledge for women and enriching their spirits. As private schools were exclusively established for competent male talents devoted to emperor in ancient times, Chaozhou Folk Songs was created by Chaozhou people for women to acquire knowledge. These songs were largely passed on by women, both singers and listeners. Most women began to learn Chaozhou Folk Songs at the age of 20 and most of them were fascinated by the songs from age15 to 22. Due to the rapid development of publishing industry and the permission to admit female students into schools, folk songs came to its full radiance during the period of Republic of China and played increasingly important role in education. The literate female voluntarily teach their peers and those female who had no chance to go to school could also learn the history and other knowledge from the songs. As such, historians regarded it as “the unique female culture in the history of Chaoshan.”</p>

<p>歌册的流行也促进了经济的发展。人们传阅歌册带动了书店开展 出租歌册的业务；媒婆在婚礼上也要来上几句，甚至是乞丐若能唱上 几句，那天的伙食可能会改进；抗日革命的年代，它们也用来当作宣 传工具。 The popularity of folk songs has also boosted the economy. Book rental popped up in bookstores. Matchmakers were hired to sing a few words at the weddings and even beggars could have a better meals if they can sing several lines. People fought against the enemies during Anti-Japanese Revolution through these songs. 不幸的是，文革时期，歌册被打为“四旧”，被完全禁止。歌册 不比通俗小说，它是一种小众文化，潮汕外的地区难以寻觅，烧一本 少一本。歌册实体被彻底消灭之后，几乎以肉眼可见的速度在潮汕地 区消亡。同时，新生活方式的冲击下，古旧潮汕传统文化瓦解，歌册 的生存土壤也不复存在了。 Unfortunately, the folk songs was alleged to be one of the "Four Olds"—— old ideas, old culture, old customs and old habits during the Cultural Revolution (May in 1966 to October in 1976) an was thus banned completely. Unlike novels , folk songs, a minority culture, exclusive in Chaoshan region were getting less and less if burned. After the books of folk songs was completely wiped out, folk songs vanished at a uncontrollable speed. And the introduce of new life style only added fuel to the collapse of traditional Chaoshan culture, which made it impossible for folk songs to be recovered. 2008 年，潮汕歌册被列入第一批国家级非物质文化遗产扩展录 项目名单。幸存的歌册被小心翼翼放进博物馆、图书馆古籍库里保护 起来。 In 2008, Chaoshan folk song was included in the first batch of national intangible cultural heritage expansion list. The folk songs survived protected in museums and stockroom for rare books of libraries. 编译 许诗婷 朱芬 曾庆双陈伊桐</p>

<p><strong>8 惠东渔歌</strong></p>

<p><strong>The Song of Huidong’s Fishermen</strong></p>

<p>The Song of Huidong’s Fishermen 惠东县位于广东省东南部，惠州市东部，东临汕尾市海丰，北临 河源市紫金，西临惠阳区，南临南海的大亚湾和红海湾。惠东有着丰 富的文化底蕴，其中渔歌尤为著名，是广东传统民间艺术之一，具有 大海般的韵味和南方滨海文化特色。惠东当地人沿海而居,靠打鱼为 生，他们独特的的方言和音律节奏形成独特的渔歌文化，歌词深入浅 出地表达出渔民的生活与情感。 Huidong County is located in the southeast of Guangdong Province and the east of Huizhou City, bordering Haifeng of Shanwei City in the east, Zijin of Heyuan City in the north, Huiyang District in the west, and Daya Bay and Honghai Bay of the South China Sea in the south. Huidong has affluent cultural deposits, among which the fisherman’s song is particularly renowned. As one of the traditional folk arts of Guangdong, the fisherman’s song embodies the charm of the sea and the cultural characteristics of the southern coastal area. The local people in Huidong live along the coast and make a living by fishing. Therefore, they form a unique fishing song culture with their distinct dialect and singing rhythm. And the lyrics express the fishermen’s life and feelings in simple words. 据《惠东县志》记载，惠东渔民的远祖又称“后船疍民”，宋代 迁居福建、潮州一带。渔歌也随疍民迁徙而来，并逐渐衍变为具有独 特的曲调、风格和表演形式的惠东渔歌。惠东沿海一带的渔村风俗， 是疍家渔民流传千年的文化模式和行为习惯，与我国其他民间风俗比 较，既有相似的一面，也有不同的地方。比如，与端午吃粽、春节对 联等静态风俗不同，与划龙舟、赛马等动态传统相似，惠东疍家渔村 风俗大多是仪式性的群体动作场合，像“祭妈祖”“平海鲤鱼灯舞” 等，其仪式性、集体性、动作性、观赏性、参与性是疍家风俗的基本 特征。 According to Huidong County Annals, the ancestors of Huidong’s fishermen were also known as “people living in the back boat”. In the Song Dynasty, they moved to Fujian and Chaozhou. Their song also came with them and gradually formed the Huidong song of fisherman with unique tune, style and performance. The fishing customs along the coast of Huidong are the cultural mode and behaviour habits that has remained for thousands of years, which has differences as well as similarities compared with other Chinese traditional folk customs. For instance, being different from those static customs like eating Zongzi on the Dragon Boat Festival or</p>

<p>pasting Spring Festival couplets, their customs are similar to those dynamic traditions like rowing dragon boats or racing horse. Most of them are ceremonial group activities, such as “commemorating Matsu” and “Lantern Dance of Pinghai carp”, whose ritual, collectivity, movement, appreciation-deserving and participation are the basic characteristics of the customs of Huidong’s fisherman. 据记载，在旧社会，惠东渔民受尽欺压和凌辱，他们生活在极度 艰难的环境之中，因而只能写歌表达内心的忧伤。中秋夜晚，他们对 月而歌；在婚嫁时也有唱歌、斗歌的习俗；亲人分离、相聚，或是老 人与世长辞等时候都是以歌代言。新中国成立后，渔民翻了身，生活 一天天好起来。随着渔民生活水平的提高，惠东渔歌也在不断更新和 发展，内容不断丰富，旋律日臻优美。 According to the records, in the old days, the fishermen in Huidong suffered unlimitedly oppression and abuse and lived in an extremely tough environment, and they could do nothing but express their inward anguish by writing songs. On the mid-autumn night, they sing to the moon. When holding a wedding ceremony, they sing and compete with others in singing. When the family members are separated and reunited or the elders passed away, they also sing songs to show their deep feelings. After the founding of new China, the fishermen were liberated and their lives got better day by day. With the development of their living standard, their songs are also constantly developed and updated, with richer contents and more beautiful melodies. 惠东渔歌因曲调品种多样，旋律韵味独特，为音乐创作提供了丰 厚而珍贵的素材。许多词曲作家先后来到惠东渔村采风，创作了大量</p>

<p>渔歌题材的作品。惠东渔歌是我国地域文化中的一份珍贵遗产，但面 临着失传的危险。以前耳熟能详、人人会唱的渔歌渐渐只有在渔村祭 祀、节庆等场合上才能听到。现如今，渔歌已被惠东县政府重视并实 施拯救对策。在许多音乐人的重视下，惠东渔歌得到了发展，一度享 誉全国。如今，在惠东巽寮湾一带，每年的重要节日，当地的渔民便 唱起渔歌浩浩荡荡地庆祝、祈福。这样万人空巷的场面，谁看到都会 感到震撼。作为土生土长的惠东人，我认为当我们对西方的交响乐和 钢琴顶礼膜拜的时候，不妨回首去品位那一首首经典的渔歌——这些 流传已久的歌曲犹如一颗颗散落于民间的珍珠，拂去岁月的轻尘，它 们依然摇曳生辉。 The song of Huidong’s fisherman offers rich and precious materials for music creation owing to a variety of tunes and unique melodies. Many songwriters have come to Huidong’s fishing villages to collect folk songs and create a large number of fishing songs. Huidong fishing song is a valuable heritage of regional culture in China, but it is in danger of being lost. Those renowned fishing songs that everyone can sing gradually can only be heard in commemorative ceremonies, festivals and other special occasions. Now, the Huidong County government has attached importance to it and implemented protection measures. With the attention of many musicians, Huidong fishing song has developed and became famous all over the country. Today, in the Xunliao Bay area of Huidong, local fishermen sing fishing songs to celebrate and pray for blessings every year on important festivals. No one is not shocked by the sight of the spectacular. As a native of Huidong, I think when we worship western symphonies and pianos, we might as well look back and taste the classic fishing songs. Those songs are like pearls scattered among the people for a long time, which will still sway and shine when the dust of the years is shaken off. 编译周绮倩李运娣杨梓樱</p>

<p><strong>9 四会民歌</strong></p>

<p><strong>Sihui Folk Songs</strong></p>

<p>Sihui Folk Songs 《四会民歌》是流传于肇庆市四会市客家人的抒情民歌。民歌具 有客家人民歌特色，因此《四会民歌》也被称之为客家山歌。这些客 家山歌由于受到四会白话的影响，发音和声调与传统的客家话有所不 同，加上长时期的与地方民歌的交融，形成了浓郁的四会市地方特色， 民歌与梅州、惠州，以及江西和广西等地的客家山歌也就有了明显的 区别，形成了有地方特色的《四会民歌》。 Sihui Folk Songs are spread in Sihui City, Zhaoqing Area, which belongs to a kind of lyrical ballads. As Sihui Folk Songs have the features of the Hakka’s characteristics, so they are also called Hakka folk songs. Time on and time over, these Hakka folk songs influenced by the Sihui’s colloquialism,which has differences in the pronunciation and intonation of the traditional Hakka tone. After a long period of time of folk songs integrating, Sihui Folk Songs have formed folk songs with distinctive local characteristics, making it has significant difference among the folk songs of Mei Zhou City, Hui Zhou City, Jiang Xi Province and Guang Xi Province. 据四会市史料记载；南宋淳熙年间（1174 年至1189 年），四会 知县苏建邦修建县衙时，掘得一古碑，乃鹿鸣燕士诗，有“龙岭行歌 龙以化，凤头将见凤齐鸣”之句。由这句诗歌可见，在南宋淳熙年之 前，《四会民歌》已经在当地十分盛行。由此可见，四会民歌至少已 经有800 多年历史了。2015 年经广东省人民政府批准；《四会民歌》 被确定为第六批省级非物质文化遗产。 According to the historical records of Sihui, during the Chunxi period of the late Song Dynasty (1174-1189), it was told when Su Jianbanghe, a magistrate of Sihui, was building the county government , he fond an ancient monument with a poem caved on it, " the singing style of Longling has the dragon’s spirit, if a phoenix heard it, it will also sing. ". From this poem, we can learn that before the Chunxi year of the late Song Dynasty, the folk songs of Sihui had been very popular in the local area. It can be seen that Sihui Folk Songs has a history of more than 800 years. Sihui Folk Songs has been identified as the sixth batch of provincial intangible cultural heritage by the People's Government of Guangdong Province in 2015. 受到南朝民歌和唐诗的影响《四会民歌》继承了诗歌的比兴传， 基本上是四句七字体，每首山歌采用各种修辞手法，音乐上押韵合拍，</p>

<p>唱起来朗朗上口，高亢嘹亮。民歌题材广泛，歌词淳朴生动，主要通 过“口传心授，上辈传下辈的方式，在民间广泛传唱，演唱者多触景 生情、歌由心生、问字拿腔，是客家人抒发情感、交流情谊、鼓舞志 气、教育后辈的表现形式，具有浓郁的地方特色。《四会民歌》中的 白话民歌最有名的是“啼哭歌”。“啼哭歌的代表曲目是《哭嫁歌》、 《哭丧歌》，它们主要在婚礼和葬礼上传唱，演唱的时候还伴有哭泣。 这与许多地方民歌有共同性。 Sihui Folk Songs inherits the traditional buesching style, it is influenced by the folk songs of the Southern Dynasty and Tang’s poetry form. Basically, it is a four-sentence seven font and various rhetorical devices are used. Every folk song embodies rhyme in tune, which is catchy, loud and clear. Folk songs cover a wide range of themes and the lyrics are simple and vivid, which are widely sung among the people by oral teaching from the heart and passed on from one generation to the next. The singers are often moved by the scenery, the songs are born from the heart, and use the words in rhyme and take them in cavity. It is a form of expression for Hakkas to express feelings, exchange friendship, inspire ambition and educate future generations with strong local characteristics. Among Sihui Folk Songs, the most famous one is "Crying Song". The representative repertoire of the Crying Songs are "The Marriage Song" and "The Funeral Song", which are mainly sung at weddings and funerals, accompanied by crying.This has something in common with folk songs in many other places. 《四会民歌》是一种传承演唱形式，其中传承谱系最为明显、最 有代表性的是四会市迳口镇元龙岭的李氏家族，云龙岭的客家山歌被</p>

<p>称之为《四会民歌》中的“元龙调”。据迳口镇元龙岭的《李氏族谱》 记载，李重明家族的祖辈都是当地“客家山歌王”，到李重明这一代， 四会客家山歌元龙调已被传唱了九代人。李重明虽已是78 岁高龄， 但是他唱起山歌时抒情悠扬、委婉动听，流露出极强的声乐功底。出 于对《四会民歌》的热爱，他搜集、整理和创编了100 多首客家山歌， 其中《明日带你转涯家》等曲目入选《广东客家山歌大典》。客家山 歌对唱《玉翠桔红》，获得了广东省旅游文化节民间艺术汇演金奖， 2008 年，由李重明领衔主唱的四会客家民歌，夺得国际广东小曲争 霸赛冠军。 Sihui Folk Songs is a form of inheritance and singing among the numerous heritage performances, Li's family, which is in Yuanlongling, Jingkou Town, Sihui City, has the most outstanding and representative heritage pedigree. The Hakka folk songs in Yunlongling is hailed as the "Yuanlong tune" in "Sihui Folk Songs".The four-club folk song is a form of inheritance and singing Some of the colloquial auxiliary words, such as "Luo", "Ho", "Yu" and so on, have been added to Yuanlong tune, "some of them are added to the beats, which makes the" prolong tune "of Sihui Folk Songs more unique." According to Li's Genealogy in Yuanlongling, Jingkou Town, the ancestors of Li Chongming's family were all the local "king of Hakka folk songs". The generation of Li Chongming is the ninth generation of Sihui Hakka folk singing with Yuanlong tune. Although Li Chongming is 78 years old, he is hale and hearty with a silver head and a loud voice. His folk songs is melodious and beautiful, showing that his has a strong vocal skill. Because of his love for Sihui Folk Songs, he has been collecting more than 100 Hakka folk songs in his spare time, among which Tomorrow Takes You to My Home and other tracks have been selected into "Guangdong Hakka Folk Song Classic. The antiphonal style of Hakka folk song--- The Green Emerald and Red Orange won the gold medal of folk art performance of Guangdong Tourism and Culture Festival in 2008. 编译何愉桦王泽熙</p>

<p><strong>10 咸水歌</strong></p>

<p><strong>Salty Water Song</strong></p>

<p>Salty Water Song 咸水歌是珠三角洲渔民（又称为“疍家”）用粤语演唱的一种渔 歌，又称为“白话渔歌”“中山民歌”。咸水歌是疍家文化的精华之 一，与惠东渔歌、客家山歌统称为广东民歌的三颗璀璨明珠。 Salty Water Song is a kind of fishing song in Cantonese by fishermen from the Pearl River Delta (also known as Tanka), also known as “Cantonese Fishing Song” and “Zhongshan Folk Song”. Salty Water Song is one of the finest products of Tanka culture, also being regarded as the three shining pearls of Canton folk songs together with Huidong fishing songs and Hakka hill songs. 为什么要称作“咸水歌”？一般认为这与疍家人的生活地域有关。 疍家人生活在珠三角沿海地区，他们常年捕鱼谋生，所唱之歌也与大 海脱离不了关系，在咸水边所唱的歌便叫“咸水歌”。唱咸水歌是疍 家不可缺少的日常乐趣，表现出疍家渔民对劳动生活的热爱与积极的 生活态度，形成了鲜明独特的艺术特色。 Why is it called “Salty Water Song”? It is related to the living area of the Tanka. The Tanka people live in the coastal area of the Pearl River Delta and make a living by fishing through years. What they sing is inseparable from the sea, which also known as Salty Water, and therefore is called “Salty Water Song”. Singing songs is an important part of Tanka people’s daily life, which shows their enthusiasm and positive attitudes towards their labor working, thus providing Salty Water Song with a distinctive artistic characteristic. 咸水歌种类繁多，不同的场合有不同形式的咸水歌。其中“高堂 歌”是在结婚、满月等喜庆的场合所唱，其轻松的旋律、婉转的音调 为节日增添了氛围。而“大板歌”则是在渔民休息期间为寻乐趣所唱， 因为其每句的末尾都有“姑呀妹”的押韵点缀，也被称为“姑妹歌”， 展现出独具一格的方言特色和语言文化。 According to a variety of occasions, Salty Water Song comes in many forms. For example, Gaotang songs appear on festive days, such as wedding ceremony and a baby’s completion of its first month. Its light melodies and tones add festival atmosphere. And Daban songs are sung for fun during the fishermen’s rest time, which is also known as “Gumei songs” because it is punctuated with the rhyme “Gu Ya Mei” (local dialect) at the end of each lyric, showing their unique dialect and local</p>

<p>culture. 根据相关史料记载，咸水歌流传至今已经有三百余年的历史。明 代文学家屈大均所写的《广东新语诗语》中记载，“疍人亦喜歌，婚 夕两舟结合。男歌胜则牵女衣过舟也。”由此可见，咸水歌早在明末 清初时期就已经很流行了。 According to relevant historical records, Salty Water Song boasts a history of more than 300 years. In The New Canton Dialect written by Qu Dajun, a writer of the Ming Dynasty, it is recorded that “Tanka folks are fond of singing songs. If the bride sings better than the groom when their boats are met on the wedding day, he can bring his wife home.” As can be seen, Salty Water Song was very popular in the late Ming and early Qing dynasties. 不同时代的疍家人所演唱的咸水歌有不同的形式，节奏也有快有 慢，从而反映了他们当时的生活状况。疍家人择水而居，历史上他们 曾长期受到歧视，甚至在民国时期有严格规定疍家人不能在岸上居 住，只能以海为家。海上生活环境恶劣，他们只能以唱歌的形式去传 递信息、相互鼓励，所以当时咸水歌的节奏与速度相对缓慢，绵长悲 切。而新中国解放之后，疍家人被允许上岸生活，日子开始稳定起来， 所以这时咸水歌的节奏相对轻快，更具丰富的动感及节奏，更具感染 力,由此可见他们当时生活的稳定以及新中国解放后疍家人的喜悦。 In different ages, Salty Water Song is sung in different styles and at different rhythms, reflecting Tanka people’s living conditions at that time. In the past, they have been discriminated for a long time. Even in the Period of the Republic of China, there are strict regulations that the Tanka people were unable to live on the land, but</p>

<p>only to take the sea as their home. They lived in a tough environment in the vast sea, so they could only convey information and encourage each other by singing. Therefore, the rhythm and speed of Salty Water Song are relatively slow, long and full of sorrow. After the liberation of New China, the Tanka folks were allowed to go on shore, and their lives began to be stable. Therefore, the rhythm of Salty Water Song was relatively brisk, with more dynamic and more infectious rhythm, which indicated the stability of their life and their joys of the liberation of New China. 到了改革开放的现代，随着社会的发展、当代文化思潮的影响， 以及咸水歌老艺人的相继去世，咸水歌却面临着后继无人的窘境。面 临濒危的状况，如何传承和保护咸水歌成了重中之重的问题。2006 年5 月20 日，中山咸水歌被国务院批准纳入第一批国家级文化遗产 名录，不仅使当代年轻人认识了咸水歌，还推动了其世界知名度。 In the modern era of reform and opening up, under the influence of social development and contemporary cultural trends, Salty Water Song faces the situation of no one to spread and no one to sing, especially after the old artists of Salty Water Song passed away one after another. Under the circumstances, how to inherit and protect Salty Water Song is our top priority. On May 20, 2006, Zhongshan Salty Water Song has been approved by the State Council into the first batch of national cultural heritage list, which making it known not only to contemporary young people, but also to promote its worldwide popularity. 咸水歌是岭南文化的艺术精髓之一，更是我国非物质文化遗产的 重要部分。我们不仅要继续传承与发展咸水歌，更需要在这一过程中 有所创新、有所突破，结合当代的精神和时代的发展，在咸水歌中加 入新元素，让人们更好地理解和接受。如此一来，才会有更多的歌者 喜欢和传唱咸水歌，咸水歌才能得到真正意义的传承和发展。 Salty Water Song is one of the artistic essence of Lingnan culture and an important part of China’s intangible cultural heritage. We should not only continue to inherit and develop Salty Water Song, but also make innovations and breakthroughs during this process. What’s more, we should also add new elements to Salty Water Song and combine it with modern spirits and social development, thus enabling it to be better accepted by people. Only in this way can more singers enjoy and spread Salty Water Song and can it be truly inherited and developed. 编译 卢千烁梁禧铧刘彬灏 黄嘉仪莫小婷冯安琪</p>

<p><strong>11 汝湖渔歌</strong></p>

<p><strong>The Song of Ruhu’s Fisherman</strong></p>

<p>The Song of Ruhu’s Fisherman 汝湖,民间传说是七位仙女下凡来游玩，到此地被景色所吸引忘 记返回天庭，故命名仙女湖，再到后来变成汝湖。在汝湖传唱着一种 民间歌谣，那就是汝湖渔歌。汝湖渔歌是惠州传统民间艺术之一，它 是汝湖镇水上社区渔民以惠州方言演唱的淡水渔歌。渔歌历史悠久, 在清代中期就已开始传唱，民国至上世纪60 年代，渔歌仍盛行于汝 湖一带，但现今只有少部分中老年人会唱。 Ruhu is located in Huizhou. According to a folk tale, seven fairies visited Ruhu and were attracted by the scenery that forgot to return to the paradise. So the place was named Fairy Lake and later became Ruhu Lake. There is a kind of folk song by fisherman in Ruhu and that is Ruhu Fishing Song. As one of Huizhou’s traditional folk arts, it is a freshwater fishing song in Huizhou dialect by fishermen in the aquatic community of Ruhu Town. Fishing songs boast a long history, which began to take shape and became popular in the mid-Qing Dynasty. During the period of the Republic of China to the 1960s, fishing songs were still popular in the Ruhu area. But today only a few middle-aged and elderly people know how to sing. 汝湖位于气候温和的东江上游，生活氛围悠然自得，造就了渔民 逍遥自得的轻吟浅唱，渔歌轻盈欢快的旋律附和着船桨拍打水面的声 音舒缓地漂流于云水间。温和的惠州方言使得汝湖渔歌不同于沿海渔 歌般刚烈和雄壮。穿梭在东江河上的汝湖渔歌用歌声描绘着一方水 土，一地风情，一份心绪，从容地释放，委婉地倾诉。 Ruhu is located in the upper reaches of the Dongjiang River, where the climate is comfortable and the living atmosphere is leisurely. As a result, the fishermen sing in a relax and happy way. The light and cheerful melody of fishing songs is accompanied by the sound of the paddles slapping on the water and drifting slowly among the river. The Huizhou dialect is very gentle, thus making Ruhu fishing songs be different from other fishing songs that are powerful and majestic. The songs spread across the East River area, gentlely and euphemistically showing the features of this land, the local customs and a leisure mood. 不同于客家山歌、闽南歌和粤语歌，汝湖渔歌是惠州方言语系唯 一的淡水歌，且主要在东江水域传唱。汝湖渔歌主要由词、曲、儿歌 组成,演唱形式丰富多样，包括独唱、对唱、斗歌等。曲调简单易唱， 朗朗上口。歌词内容广泛，多与渔民的日常生活相关，主要分为九类，</p>

<p>分别是劳作歌、生活歌、风景地名歌、婚嫁歌、白事歌(农村办丧事 时的歌曲）、情歌、乐唱歌、儿歌、杂歌。由于是在小船上临时创作 的歌曲，所以歌唱时无乐器伴奏。 Being different from Hakka folk songs (folk songs in Hakka language by the Hakka people), Minnan folk songs (folk songs developed in southern Fujian Province) and Cantonese folk songs, Ruhu fishing song is the only freshwater song in Huizhou dialect, which is mainly developed in the Dongjiang River area. Mainly composed of lyrics, tunes and children’s songs, it boasts various forms, such as solo, antiphonal singing and competing with others in singing. Its melody is simple and easy to sing. Its lyrics are wide-ranging, mostly related to the daily lives of fishermen, which can be divided into nine catagories: labor working songs, daily life songs, landscape songs, wedding songs, funeral songs, love songs, tunes, children’s songs and miscellaneous songs. There is no accompaniment of musical instrument when singing because those songs are temporarily composed on the boat. 汝湖渔歌产生和发展的原因主要有三，首先是清政府对渔民的限 制十分苛刻：不允许他们识字读书、不允许他们参加科举考试。渔民 不能像岸上人家那样享受同等的文化生活与教育的权利。从出生到离 世，渔民每天都在一条狭窄的船上，过着漂无定所的生活。在精神与 物质生活压力的双重挤压下，渔歌自然产生并盛行，成为渔民精神生 活的重要寄托，成为他们艰难打渔生活的调味剂。与此同时，按渔家 风俗，渔民家的女儿嫁作人妇时一定要唱渔歌哭嫁，不唱哭嫁歌就意 味着对父母不恭不孝。此外，有亲人离世，后辈也要以唱歌的形式送 行。</p>

<p>There are three main reasons for the emergence and development of the fishing songs in Ruhu. At first, the government of the Qing Dynasty has very strict restrictions on fishermen: they are not allowed to accept education and take imperial examinations (a civil service examination system in Imperial China to select candidates for the state bureaucracy.) Fishermen cannot enjoy the same cultural life and education as the people living on the land. From birth to death, they live a wandering life on a narrow boat every day. Under the double pressure of spiritual and material life, fishing songs are naturally produced and prevailed, becoming an important sustenance of the spiritual life of fishermen and the entertainment of their difficult fishing life. Furthermore, according to the local customs, the daughter of fisherman’s family must sing fishing songs and cry when she gets married. If not singing the songs, she will be regarded as not showing filial piety to her parents. In addition, when family members passed away, the younger generations must see them off by singing. 汝湖渔歌对于研究惠州方言、惠州人生活生产史、惠州民间文学 与民间音乐、惠州文化史、惠州民俗等方面有重要的鉴赏价值。如今， 汝湖渔歌成为了内河渔民的一种集体记忆，他们虽然改变了以前水上 漂泊的生活方式，但他们仍然传唱着渔歌。每一个音符每一个词汇， 都在重构这段凝结先民水上生活的历史，填补了惠州方言语系渔歌史 的空白，一定程度上更是弥补了惠州历史的缺失。现在渔民们都上了 岸，扛起了锄头，五谷杂粮，布衣华服，裹挟在烟火人情中，感受着 花开四季，春夏秋冬节气的变化。 The song of Ruhu’s fisherman possesses extremely high appreciation value for the research on the dialect, people’s life and production history, folk literature and music, cultural history and local customs of Huizhou. Nowadays, those songs have become a kind of collective memory of the fishermen in inland river. Though they had changed the way they used to lived over the lake, their songs were still very popular. Every note and lyric of those songs is reconstructing the history of their ancestors used to live on boats, filling in the blank of the history of fishing songs in Huizhou dialect and, to some extent, making up for the lost of Huizhou’s history. Now the fishermen have returned to the land, working in the fields and eating grains. They are in fine clothes, living a comfortable life, feeling the changing seasons and appreciating flowers blossoming all the year round. 编译梁静林妍津黄丽</p>

<p><strong>12 余音绕梁之广东汉乐</strong></p>

<p><strong>The Tune Lingers in the Mind</strong></p>

<p>The Tune Lingers in the Mind —Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music 广东汉乐有过许多称谓，例如客家音乐、外江弦、儒家乐、汉调 音乐等，是流行于广东省梅州市一带的传统音乐。它历史悠久，有“中 州古乐”之称，是一千多年前由客家先民南迁时带来的中原古乐，在 梅州大埔至少有五百年以上的历史。而且，大埔县于2004 年被广东 省文化厅授予“汉乐之乡”荣誉称号。 As a traditional music being popular in Meizhou City, Guangdong Province, Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music has many appellations, such as Hakka Music, Waijiang Strings, Confucian Music, Music with Han Melody, etc. It has a long history and is called “Zhongzhou Ancient Music”. It is also an ancient music brought to the south by Hakka ancestors more than one thousand years ago, which has a history of at least five hundred years in Dabu County, Meizhou City. In addition, Dabu County was awarded the title of “Hometown of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music” by the Cultural Department of Guangdong Province in 2004. 回顾历史，我们不难发现——自秦始皇时期开始，汉族就发生过 多次大规模南迁，到粤东、闽西、赣南等地定居，而这些南迁的汉族 称自己为“客家人”。并且，历史上汉族南迁的主要原因是躲避战乱。 客家人的到来不仅给南方带来了异乡习俗，还带来了《中州古调》、 《汉皋旧谱》等中原古汉乐乐谱。这些古汉乐与当地的民间音乐、庙 堂音乐等乐种融会贯通，形成极具地方特色的音乐流派——广东汉 乐。根据传统的演奏形式、长期沿革的演奏习惯和用途的不同，广东 汉乐可以分成五个类别，它们分别是丝弦乐、清乐、汉乐大锣鼓、中 军班音乐、庙堂音乐。 Looking back at history, it is not difficult to find that since the time of Qin Shihuang (the first emperor in Chinese history who unified China in 221 BC), the Han nationality has moved to the south on a large scale for many times and settled in the eastern part of Guangdong, the western part of Fujian and the southern part of Jiangxi. They call themselves “Hakkas”. Moreover, in history, the main reason for the Han people to move to the south is to escape from the war. The arrival of the Hakka brought both the customs of foreign lands to the south and the music scores of the ancient Han music in the Central Plains, such as Zhongzhou Ancient Melody and Hangao Ancient Music Score. These ancient Han music assimilated local folk music,</p>

<p>temple music and other types of music and then formed a music genre with distinctive local characteristics — Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music. According to the traditional form of playing, the long-term evolution of playing habits and different uses, Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music can be divided into five categories, which are String Music, Music for Literati Activities, Music for Traditional Festivals, Ceremonial Music and Temple Music. 广东汉乐是一种移民文化，它不仅具有深厚的民族文化底蕴，而 且还蕴含弥足珍贵的历史价值。在长期的继承与发展中，广东汉乐既 继承了中原地区的宫廷音乐和民间音乐的精华，又吸收融合了客家地 区传统的民间音乐。同时，它还吸纳了另外一种传统音乐——潮州音 乐的某些成份，形成了既独特又完整的音乐体系，在中国民间音乐史 上的研究价值极大。 Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music emerges from immigrant culture, which not only has profound national cultural deposits, but also contains an extremely precious historical value. In the long-term inheritance and development, it not only inherited the essence of court music and folk music of the Central Plains, but also absorbed and integrated the traditional folk music of the Hakka region. At the same time, it also assimilated some elements of another traditional music — Chaozhou Music, forming a unique and complete music system. Therefore, Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music is of great research value in the history of Chinese folk music. 但是现如今，广东汉乐面临着不容乐观的发展与生存状况。造成 这种现状的原因有四个：一是社会基础发生变革导致广东汉乐失去了</p>

<p>赖以生存和发展的基础。二是现代娱乐产业发展变化快、娱乐形式呈 现多元化发展，导致学习广东汉乐的人愈来愈少。而且，老一辈乐手 已然年迈或相继谢世，有些绝技后继无人。三是广东汉乐中的庙堂音 乐活动锐减，导致能演奏此类乐曲的乐手相对较少。而且，它与平时 乐手们自娱自乐的愉快气氛不符合，所以能演奏庙堂音乐的人就更屈 指可数了。四是大部分广东汉乐资料都散落在社会和个人手中，有关 部门没有建立一个完整的资料库，导致缺乏广东汉乐的系统资料。通 过以上分析，我们可以发现广东汉乐人才队伍青黄不接，面临濒危。 因此，广东汉乐亟待加强传承与保护。 However, Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music is confronted with a discouraging situation of survival and development at present. There are four reasons for this situation. First, the social foundation has been reformed, which has led to the loss of the foundation on which Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music has relied for its survival and development. Second, the rapid progress of modern entertainment industry and diversified development of entertainment forms have resulted in fewer and fewer people learning it. Moreover, due to advanced years and demise of the older generation of musicians, some unique skills of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music have no successor. Third, the sharp decrease of Temple Music activities of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music gives rise to relatively few musicians capable of playing this kind of music. Furthermore, it does not match the ordinary pleasant atmosphere of entertainment by musicians, so there are less people who can play Temple Music. Fourth, the majority of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music data have been scattered in the hands of the society and individuals, and the relevant departments have not established a complete database about it, resulting in the lack of systematic data of it. Through the above analysis, it can be seen that the talent team of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music is in short supply and in danger of extinction. Therefore, it is urgent to strengthen the inheritance and protection of Guangdong Traditional Chinese Music. 编译蔡茹娴莫琪琪郭海凤</p>

<p><strong>13 傩舞—岭南地区民间舞蹈的奇葩</strong></p>

<p><strong>Nuo Dance -- A Wonder Folk Dance in Lingnan Area</strong></p>

<p>Nuo Dance -- A Wonder Folk Dance in Lingnan Area 广东岭南地区是一个民间艺术丰富多彩的地区，据统计全区共有 各种传统民间舞蹈60 余种。傩舞—又称（湛江傩舞）是流行在湛江 地区的一种古老的民间传统舞蹈。古代人利用舞蹈的表演形式去祭雷 遣灾、祷神求安。傩舞经历了上千年历史沉淀，不断地融入了湛江当 地的民俗民风，发展至今，形成了独特的湛江地区民间舞蹈风格，具 有宗教、民俗、历史文化等多方面的价值，被称为“舞蹈活化石”。 2008 年经国务院批准傩舞（湛江傩舞）列入第二批国家级非物质文 化遗产。 The Lingnan Prefecture of Guangdong Province is a district with rich and colorful folk art. According to statistics, there are more than 60 kinds of traditional folk dances in various parts of the area. Nuo Dance -- also known as (Zhanjiang Nuo Dance), is an ancient folk traditional dance popular in Zhanjiang. The ancient Chinese used the folk dance to offer sacrifices to Thunder God, to ward off evil and epidemics and to pray for peace. Nuo Dance has experienced thousands of years of historical precipitation, and has been continuously integrated into the local folk customs of Zhanjiang. It has developed into a unique style of folk dance in Zhanjiang area with religious, folk, historical and cultural values, which is called "living fossil” of Chinese dance. In 2008, Nuo Dance (Zhanjiang Nuo Dance) was approved by the State Council to be included in the second batch of national intangible cultural heritage. 据相关记载：（湛江傩舞）每年从正月十三开始连续表演十五夜， 每夜大街小巷张灯结彩，表演者三五百为一队，放爆竹，烧烟火，锣 鼓声声，游人熙熙攘攘。传统的傩舞主要进行祭雷遣灾保平安表演， 表现内容以雷公与五方雷神活动为主。傩舞的表演形式大至分为奏 请、誓师、遣灾、押灾与庆功五个内容： According to relevant records: Nuo Dance will be shown in most parts in Zhanjiang, and the performances continuous for 15 nights every year from the thirteenth of the first lunar month. Every night, the streets and alleys are decorated with lights and colors. The performers form a team of three to five hundred to set off firecrackers and fireworks, and to strike gongs and drums. Everywhere, tourists are bustling. The traditional Nuo Dance is mainly performed to offer sacrifices to thunder gods and to drive away the evils for peace, and the content of the performance mainly focused on the activities of Thunder God and the five thunder gods. Nuo Dance can be divided into five procedures: petitions, oaths, evil elimination, disaster relief, and</p>

<p>celebrations. 表演者们手执宝剑舞动自己的身体，跟着锣鼓音乐的节奏移动着 脚步：右左，上下，侧身，转身，上跳下跳、指挥五雷公将、艄公婆、 土地公婆往村点将坛前集中，各路将神的表演者绕坛走3 圈后高呼 “尽职尽力”后就奔各家各户驱除邪恶,各家各户设供桌迎接。五雷 公将驱除邪恶在船上由艄公婆押走，烧纸和放炮，并将纸船点燃放入 河中，预示着厄运的离去。随后土地公婆进入送子孙送财宝，以求平 安。 The performers dance their bodies with swords in their hands, and move in accordance with the rhythm of the gongs and drums: right and left, up and down, and sideways. They turn around, jump up and down, and command the five thunder gods, Boat God, and Earth God to gather in front of the altar in the village. The performers of the gods walk around the altar three times before shouting "endeavour and responsibility" and rush to each house to dispel evil. Each household will set up a table to greet them. The five thunder gods will drive away the evil and Boat God will take it away on the boat. They will burn papers, set off firecrackers, and fire the paper boats into the river, indicating the departure of bad luck. Then, Earth God will enter to give away treasures to children and grandchildren for safety. 具有雷州民俗艺术特色的湛江傩舞是一种带着面具表演舞蹈。现 有的保存完好的雷傩面已有600 年了。表演者带上象征着各路神灵彩 绘脸谱，有木质的、有牛皮及一些其他材料的。跳傩舞的人根据自己 的想象，及对雷公和祖先的崇拜、对自然的敬畏和对雷图腾文化融合 在一起，模拟他们心目中的五方雷将，并用青、赤、白、黑、黄五种 颜色来绘制人物面具，完美的表现了舞蹈者的人物形态。湛江傩舞具</p>

<p>有强烈的表演性，在舞蹈过程中可以用锣鼓、堂鼓、高边锣、大钹、 小锣、小铃及古老的陶鼓等为其伴奏。保留了古代的“击鼓逐疫”， “以乐送神”的古礼乐制，呈现了强烈的原始粗犷神秘的氛围。 Zhanjiang Nuo Dance is a dance performed with masks. The Lei Nuo Masks have been preserved for almost 600 years.The performers wear painted masks made of wood, leather and other materials, which symbolize various gods. Nuo Dance performers imitate the five thunder gods in their minds with the combination of their own imagination, the worship of the thunder gods and ancestors, the reverence for nature, and the culture of thunder totem. Usually, they use green, red, white, black and yellow colors to draw their masks, perfectly representing the dancer's character,and showing us a perfect performance. The performers are accompanied on gongs, drums, high-side gongs, big cymbals, small gongs, small bells, and ancient pottery drums during the dance. It retains the ancient ritual music system of "beating the drum to drive away the epidemics" and "praying to gods with music", presenting a strong primitive, wild and mysterious atmosphere. 湛江傩舞是湛江地区流传下来的古老的民间表演艺术，它反映了 各个历史时期湛江地区及雷洲半岛的人民敬雷崇雷的宗教活动、民 俗、民间文化及表演艺术手法。傩舞不仅是一种舞蹈，还是一种文化， 它承载传播了早期人类的社会生活方式，在表演中又嵌入了许多的民 间元素，将舞蹈与音乐完美相结合，是岭南地区民间舞蹈的奇葩。 Zhanjiang Nuo Dance is an ancient folk performance art throughout countless generation in Zhanjiang area. It reflects the religious activities, folk customs, folk culture and performing arts techniques of people in Zhanjiang area and Leizhou Peninsula in various historical periods. Nuo Dance is not only a kind of dance, but also a kind of culture. It carries and spreads the social lifestyle of early humans and also embeds many folk elements in the performance, which perfectly combines dance and music. It is a wonder folk dance in Lingnan area. 编译潘利锋赵小莉</p>

<p><strong>14 春牛舞</strong></p>

<p><strong>Spring Cattle Dance</strong></p>

<p>Spring Cattle Dance 春牛舞在河源市紫金县东部及瓦溪镇一带较为流行。1974 年瓦 溪乡的《春牛歌舞》参加惠阳地区业余文艺汇演获优秀节目奖。春牛 舞曾多次参加河源市和本县民间艺术巡游表演活动。1997 年县花朝 戏剧团排练春牛舞赴香港屯门、大埔、元朗等地演出，获得好评。2007 年，春牛舞列入第一批河源市非物质文化遗产名录。2015 年春节期 间，龙窝镇春牛舞除了在本镇各村演出外，还应邀五华、惠东、揭西 等地演出。 Spring Cattle Dance is popular in the eastern part of Zijin County and Waxi Town, Heyuan City. In 1974, "Spring Cattle Singing and Dance" in Waxi Town won the Excellent Program Award in the amateur art performance in Huiyang area. Spring Cattle Dance has participated in folk art parades in Heyuan City and this county many times. In 1997, the County Huachao Drama Troupe rehearsed the Spring Cattle Dance and performed in Tuen Mun, Tai Po, Yuen Long and other places in Hong Kong, which was favorably reviewed. In 2007, Spring Cattle Dance was included in the first batch of Heyuan City Intangible Cultural Heritage List. During the Spring Festival in 2015, in addition to performing in the villages of the town, the Spring Cattle Dance in Longwo Town was also invited to perform in Wuhua, Huidong, Jiexi and other places. 春牛舞是以打击乐为伴奏乐的民间舞蹈。其表演形式，是双人钻 进竹扎的春牛肚子里合舞，由牧童牵牛上场，表演骑牛、逗牛等滑稽 动作戏耍春牛。歌词内容以二十四节气和相关农事活动为主，唱腔是 紫金特色的春牛调音乐主要是打击乐，由唢呐、笛子伴奏。 Spring Bull Dance is a folk dance accompanied by percussion. Its performance form is that two people get into the belly of spring cattle tied in bamboo to dance together, and the shepherd boy leads the cattle to play, performing funny actions such as riding cattle and teasing cattle to play the spring cattle. The lyrics are mainly composed of twenty-four solar terms and related farming activities, and the singing is spring cattle tune with Zijin characteristics, mainly percussion, accompanied by Suona and flute. 春牛舞是一种运用采茶舞的表演形式，借鉴师公的唱赞形式的综 合表演。舞春牛旧时为官方举办的春耕春播仪式，县衙举办这个活动， 寓意是春耕即开始，并预祝当年风调雨顺，农家取得大丰收。旧时县 官每逢开春，便带僚属和县民，肩挑祭品，牵着牛到五谷庙祭祀神农， 祈求风调雨顺，五谷丰登。祭祀后，县官下田扶犁驱牛，谓之“示耕”。 后来，舞春牛活动成为一种民间的娱乐活动，演化为春牛舞。每当丰</p>

<p>收年景，村民们便与牛共舞，与牛同乐，期望开春又有好收成。 Spring Cattle Dance is a comprehensive performance that uses tea things' performance form and draws lessons from the singing and praising form of Shigong. In the old days, Dancing Spring Cattle was an official spring ploughing and sowing ceremony. The county government held this activity, which meant that the spring’s ploughing began, and wished the farmers good weather and a bumper harvest. Every spring, county officials took their relatives and county people, shouldered sacrifices, and led cattle to the Wugu Temple to worship Shennong, praying for good weather and good harvest. After the sacrifice, the county officials went to the fields to plow and drive cattle, which is called "showing cultivation". Later, spring cattle dance became a kind of folk entertainment and evolved into Spring Cattle Dance. Whenever the harvest is good, the villagers dance with the cows and have fun with them, expecting a good harvest in spring. 如今表演形式和道具又有新变化，春牛则用竹扎、纸糊牛头，布 身，双人钻进牛的肚子里合舞，表演默契。开场时，春牛锣鼓响起后， 由牧童牵牛上场，表演骑牛、逗牛等滑稽动作戏耍春牛，春牛则从艺 术上加以塑造，模仿牛的形态、神态、动作，活灵活现地表演，使它 更具人性化，憨厚、可爱。牧童用喂草、洗刷、抚背等表演动作，表 现对牛的呵护。牧童表演完后，男队头裹毛巾，肩扛锄头，女队戴凉 帽，肩挑花蓝分别从两边舞上。表演时，两队边跳边舞转一个圆圈后。 男女对唱，绕圆场后，每舞一圈唱一段。唱词内容以二十四节气和相 关农事活动为主，是三句式，第三句是第二句的重复。唱腔是紫金特</p>

<p>色的春牛调，如《脚踏泥水春耕忙》、《贺新年十大恭喜》等。音乐 主要是打击乐，由唢呐、笛子伴奏。春牛舞属自娱性表演，既可在村 寨进行联谊活动，也可在门坪、广场、街道表演或舞台上演出。 Nowadays, there are new changes in the performance form and props. Spring cattle tie their heads with bamboo and paper, and then cloth their bodies. Two people get into the belly of cattle and dance together, thus performing tacitly. At the beginning, after the gongs and drums of Spring Cattle sounded, the shepherd boy led the cattle to play the Spring Cattle, performing funny actions such as riding and teasing cattle. The Spring Cattle was shaped in art, imitating the shape, manner and movements of cattle, and performing vividly, making it more humane, simple and lovely. Shepherd boys show their care for cattle by feeding grass, washing and caressing their backs. After the shepherd boy's performance, the men's team wore a towel on their heads and a hoe on their shoulders, while the women's team wore a cool hat and a blue flower on their shoulders. During the performance, the two teams danced and turned around in a circle. Men and women sing in pairs. After circling the circus, sing one paragraph for each dance. The lyrics are mainly composed of twenty-four solar terms and related farming activities, which are three sentences, and the third sentence is the repetition of the second sentence. Singing is a unique spring style of Zijin, such as Busy Spring Farming with Mud Feet and Ten Congratulations on the New Year. Music is mainly percussion, accompanied by Suona and flute. Spring Cattle Dance is a self-entertainment performance, which can be used for social activities in villages, as well as performances in gates, squares, streets or on the stage. 编译黄嘉莹赖易安吴泳斯</p>

<p><strong>15 杯花舞</strong></p>

<p><strong>The Beihua Dance</strong></p>

<p>The Beihua Dance “客家妹子客情长，情甜甜过冬蜜糖。杯花声声迎客来，欢天喜 地乐洋洋。”几十个美丽的姑娘身着客家传统服饰，双手敲打着两个 改良后的白色“伯公杯”，在优美的音乐中翩翩起舞。人们都知道茶 杯是用来泡茶的，却没想到茶杯竟还被编成舞蹈元素，这样的舞蹈是 不是很有特色？这说的就是我们家乡独有的一种舞蹈——杯花舞。 “The girls of Hakka people are fond of each other, and their love is sweet as honey in winter. The sound of Beihua dance greets the guests, and they are filled with joy. ” Dozens of beautiful girls dressed in traditional hakka costumes, her hands beat the two improved white “Bogong Cup”, dancing in the beautiful music. People know that the teacup is used to make tea, but they do not expect that the teacup has been wovend into dance elements. Isn’t this dance unique? This is a dance unique in our homeland – Cup Flower Dance. 杯花舞,是广东省兴宁市的传统舞蹈，广东省级非物质文化遗产 之一。杯花舞是道教一类的传统舞蹈艺术，表演时原是用五句板说唱 的竹板进行拍的，后来经人改革以兴宁产的白色瓷质“伯公杯”替代 了。在清朝年间，杯花舞始于兴宁流行，经过长期、反复地创新、演 练和发展，如今已有100 多年的历史，也成为了兴宁文化事业的象征。 2007 年，杯花舞被列入广东省第二批省级非物质文化遗产名录，是 兴宁颇具客家风情的传统节目。2008 年12 月，兴宁被中国文化部命 名为"中国民间艺术杯花舞之乡"。 Cup Flower Dance, a traditional dance in Xingning city, Guangdong Province, is one of the intangible cultural heritages in Guangdong Province. Cup Flower Dance, a traditional Taoist dance, was originally shot with a bamboo board made of five-sentence board. It was later reformed and replaced with white porcelain “Bogong Cup” made in Xingning. During the Qing Dynasty, Cup Flower Dance began to be popular in Xingning. After long-term and repeated innovation, practice and development, it has a history of more than 100 years and has become a symbol of Xingning's cultural undertakings. In 2007, Cup Flower Dance was listed in the second batch of provincial intangible cultural heritage list in Guangdong Province, which is a traditional program with Hakka customs in Xingning. In December 2008, Xingning was named "Hometown of Flower Dance in Chinese Folk Art Cup" by Chinese Ministry of Culture. 杯花舞是以客家山歌为基调，通过客家民俗舞蹈“杯花舞”来展 现客家人劳动和生活的情景，极具客家文化特色。它那优美婀娜的舞 蹈动作，欢乐明快的音乐节奏，加上杯花相撞击时清脆悦耳的声音，</p>

<p>配上浓郁客家特色的山歌，使得杯花舞成为民间舞蹈艺术的一朵奇 葩，经久不衰，令人百听不腻。 Cup Flower Dance is based on the folk song of Hakka people, through the folk dance to show the working and living scenes of the Hakka people, which is characteristic of Hakka people’s culture. With its graceful dance movements, cheerful and lively musical rhythm, the clear and melodious sound of cup-flowers colliding with each other, and the rich and distinctive folk songs of Hakka people, Cup Flower Dance has become a wonder of the folk dance art, lasting for a long time, and people never get tired of hearing it. 杯花舞中无论是它的表演动作还是舞步种类都令人眼花缭乱— —杯花舞的表演动作有杯花出手、转杯、摇杯等；而舞步有云步、横 步、跪步、下板腰等。表演时在独特的曲调和锣鼓点的伴奏下，用流 畅的舞步、多变的节奏和“摇、甩、打、磨、转”等敲击舞杯的技艺， 相互赛杯、献艺，给人们带来一种艺术的享受。 In Cup Flower Dance, there are dazzling performances such as cup flower throwing, cup turning and shaking, as well as cloud step, cross step, kneeling step and bending waist. The dance performs in the unique melody and gongs and drums of the accompaniment, with smooth dance steps, variable rhythm and “shake, shake, beat, grinding, turn” and other percussion cup skills, cup competition, dedication, which brings people a kind of artistic enjoyment. 杯花舞自改革以来就没有停止过创新的脚步，不断推陈出新。无 论是歌曲以青年男女的爱情到反映兴宁人民欢乐生活为主题，还是对 “伯公杯”道具的改进，使杯花舞更富有技巧性，表演更加灵活，甚 而之，舞曲饱含的情绪变得更加热烈，旋律变得更为欢快。这归功于 杯花舞的传承人潜心挖掘，收集客家民间舞蹈素材，吸收杯花舞的创 新型表演技巧，进行大胆地创新。最终，为人们呈现出高尚的视听盛 宴。</p>

<p>Cup Flower Dance has not stopped the innovation step since the reform, unceasingly pushing the old to bring out the new. Whether it is the theme of young men and women’s love to reflecting the happy life of the people of Xingning, or the improvement of the props of the “Bogong Cup”, which makes the dance more skillful, more flexible and even more, the mood of the dance become more intense and the melody become more cheerful. This is due to the efforts of the inheritors of Cup Flower Dance, who have made bold innovations by collecting materials from the Hakka people folk dance and absorbing the innovative performing techniques. At last, it presents a noble audio-visual feast for the people. 在夜深人静的夜晚里，梦里似是渐渐浮现出女子手执小巧“伯公 杯”，伴随着悠扬的音乐，轻轻摇晃、敲杯，杯子清脆的声音响起， 弯下双膝、仰起头来，执杯的人迈着轻快的步子翩翩起舞…… In the dead of night, the people’s dream seems to emerge gradually a girl holding a small “Bogong Cup”, accompanied by melodious music, gently shaking, knocking the cup. With the sound of the cup ringing, the girl with holding the cup, bent knees, head up, and dances with a light step. 编译黎翠翠王颖林少珍</p>

<p><strong>16 鹤起翩翩舞</strong></p>

<p><strong>A Crane Dancing Trippingly</strong></p>

<p>A Crane Dancing Trippingly 广东省中山市沙溪镇的申明亭村是鹤舞的诞生地。以前，申明亭 村是一个山清水秀、淙淙流水、鱼虾成群的地方。这里景色优美，具 有丰富的鱼虾资源，十分适合白鹤在此生活。因为申明村有很多白鹤， 村民便将此地称为“鹤地”。有趣的是，当地方言的“鹤”字与“学” 字同音，而且为了发扬先祖的勤奋好学之风，村民便创作了独具特色 的鹤舞来祝贺学有所成的乡民。 The village of Shen Mingting located in Shaxi Town, Zhongshan City, Guangdong Province, is considered to be the birthplace of Crane Dance. In the past, the village was a place with beautiful scenery, murmuring water and flocks of fish and shrimps. Therefore, it was very suitable for the cranes to live here. The villagers called it "Crane Land" since there are many cranes in Shen Mingting. Interestingly, the word "crane" in the local dialect has the same pronunciation as the word "learning". And in order to carry forward the diligence and studiousness of the ancestors, the locals created a unique crane dance to congratulate the villagers on their success in learning. 鹤舞是根据白鹤的动作姿势和生活习惯所创作的一种动物道具 的舞蹈，含有祈福之意和好学向上之意。它起源于明朝，盛行于清朝 和民国。在明清时代每十年举办一次舞蹈大会，名为“出鹤”。 The Crane Dance is a dance of animal props created according to the movements, postures and living habits of the cranes, which contains the meaning of blessing and studious upward. It originated in the Ming Dynasty and flourished in the Qing Dynasty and the period of the Republic of China. This dance was held every ten years in the Ming and Qing dynasties in a convention called "Out of the Crane". 鹤舞所用的道具是用竹篾编织的一只大型的白鹤。村民用竹条制 作了白鹤的骨架，用白布包裹着骨架，再以彩墨点缀眼睛，在头顶插 上红花。已制作完成的大型白鹤需要到村里的寺庙进行祭祀，祈求神 灵保佑。最后，找舞者来演绎出白鹤活动的优美姿态。 The prop used for the Crane Dance is a large white crane woven from bamboo strips. The locals make the crane's skeleton out of bamboo strips, wrap it in white cloth, decorate its eyes with colored ink and put red flowers on its head. The large crane which has been made needs to be worshiped at the village temple in order to pray for the blessing of the gods. Finally, dancers are asked to perform the postures of the cranes in motion.</p>

<p>一开始，鹤舞的形式和伴奏音乐是相对单一的，只有一只白鹤跟 随着鹤歌在跳舞。经过后来人们的不断改善，到如今，鹤舞形式多样， 丰富多彩，更具有独特的民间文化魅力，展示了特有的表演艺术形式。 其主要有14 个动作，如：走圆场、展翅高飞、鹤蚌同嬉等。在过去， 出鹤时，是以鹤歌和传统的敲击节奏作为伴奏。鹤歌是当地特有的民 间歌曲，用当地方言演唱，主要以七言绝句为基础，不受平仄韵律限 制。而现在，出鹤不仅有鹤歌，还增加了大锣、大鼓等敲击乐器和广 东传统音乐为其伴奏。 In the early days, the form of the Crane Dance and background music were relatively simple. Only one crane dances to a crane song. Nowadays, with continuous improvement by people, the Crane Dance has a variety of forms and a unique charm of folk culture, showing a distinctive form of performing arts. There are 14 main movements, such as walking in a circle, flying with wings and playing with clams. In the past, the dance was performed to the accompaniment of crane songs and traditional percussion rhythms. The crane song is a unique local folk song, sung in the local dialect, mainly based on the seven-word stanza, with no restrictions on the rhythm of the level and obliquity. Now, not only the crane song but also percussion instruments such as gongs and drums, and traditional Cantonese music are added to accompany the cranes dancing. 鹤舞出巡，在申明亭被当作是最隆重的盛事。在过去，鹤舞出巡 时，有明珠引路，由村中有名望的人开路，再让几个人扮演角色配合 出巡。其中一个人打扮成紫薇星君，表示驱除妖魔；另一个人拿着木 盒，木盒里放着书本，表示村民崇尚学习；还有古代人物扮相的文巡</p>

<p>和武巡相随两边。鹤舞出巡时，歌者歌唱鹤歌，有八音锣鼓队吹奏音 乐，场面十分壮观。鹤舞巡游队伍经过时，村民都要在自己家门口备 上茶水、茶果等迎接巡游队伍的到来。 The Crane Dance's parading is regarded as the grandest event in the village of Shen Mingting. In the past, when the crane went on parading, a person holding a pearl would guide the way, a person of renown in the village would lead the way and some people would play roles in the parade. One dressed as the Deity Zi Wei, which means to drive away demons; another person carried a wooden box with books in it, indicating that the villagers were devoted to learning; and some ancient figures dressed as Wen Xun, a civil office and as Wu Xun, a military officer followed on either side. Both past and nowadays, when the Crane Dancing is on parading, singers will sing crane songs, and there is a team playing music with eight categories of musical instrument in ancient orchestra, which is a spectacular scene. When the crane dance parade passes by, the villagers have to prepare tea and fruits at their own doorstep to welcome the parade's arrival. 可惜的是，现在的鹤舞濒临失传。由于受到现代文化和商品经济 的冲击，年轻人热衷于外来舞蹈，如：街舞、韩舞、拉丁舞等。同时， 企业缺乏热情，觉得鹤舞无利可图，便没有对鹤舞进行太多投资。目 前，在沙溪镇内，表演传统鹤舞的艺人越来越少，并且大都是年事已 高的老人了，年轻人对鹤舞毫无兴趣，所以很少主动了解学习鹤舞。 如果越来越少年轻人不积极了解和传承鹤舞，或许在未来的某一天， 鹤舞这一民俗舞蹈便会被人遗忘，彻底失传。 It is a pity that the Crane Dance is on the verge of extinction now. Due to the impact of modern culture and the commodity economy, young people are more interested in foreign dances, such as street dance, Korean dance, and Latin dance and so on. In the meantime, enterprises do not invest much in it because they lack of enthusiasm for it and find it unprofitable. At present, there are fewer and fewer performers to do the traditional Crane Dance in Shaxi, and most of them are old. Young people have no interest in the Crane Dance and rarely take the initiative to understand and learn it. It is likely that one day this folk dance will be forgotten and completely extinct if fewer and fewer young people do not learn and pass on the dance. 编译林锶琪刘洁华唐媚凤</p>

<p><strong>17 塘厦舞麒麟</strong></p>

<p><strong>Tangxia Kylin Dance</strong></p>

<p>Tangxia Kylin Dance 2013 年11 月22 日，广东省人民政府批准并公布了省文化厅确 定的第五批省级非物质文化遗产代表性项目名录（共计39 项）和省 级非物质文化遗产代表性项目扩展名录（共计28 项），东莞市一项 名为麒麟舞（又名塘厦舞麒麟）的传统舞蹈入选扩展名录。 On November 22, 2013, the People’s Government of Guangdong Province authorized and published the Fifth Representative List of Provincial Intangible Cultural Heritage determined by the Provincial Department of Culture, which includes 39 programs and 28 extended programs. Kylin Dance (also Tangxia Kylin Dance), as one of the traditional dances of Dongguan City, was listed in the extended programs. 民国《东莞县志》记载：“元旦至晦，结队鸣征鼓，以纸糊麒麟 头，画五采。缝绵被为麟身，两人舞之，舞罢，各演拳棒，曰舞麒麟。” 历史上，珠江三角洲麒麟舞以东莞最为鼎盛。塘厦镇位于东莞市东南 部，毗邻港澳，塘厦舞麒麟至今已有三百多年历史，兴盛于20 世纪 初。主要流传于镇内石潭埔、石马、清湖头、石鼓、横塘、林村、莲 湖等多个村落。 According to Dongguan County Annals in the Republic of China (1916), from the New Year’s day to the end of the month, the dance teams would gang together, beat the drum, paste Kylin heads with paper and paint them with five colors, and quilt their body. There are two performers for each Kylin. After performing Kylin, the performers would perform martial arts, which is called dance the Kylin. In history, the Kylin Dance of Dongguan City is the most prosperous one in the Pearl River Delta. Tangxia Town is located in the southeast of Dongguan City, adjacent to Hong Kong and Macao. The Tangxia Kylin Dance, flourished in the early 20th century, has a history of more than 300 years, and mainly spread in many villages in the town, such as Shitan, Shima, Qinghutou, Shigu, Hengtang, Lincun, Lianhu, etc. 塘厦镇传统的麒麟队通常只有一只麒麟、一套锣鼓、一根队旗， 队旗上面都标有队伍的姓氏或堂号，每支队伍有二十多人。表演时乐 队站在队旗前面，舞麒麟随音乐节奏而动，一人舞麒麟头，一人舞麒 麟尾。麒麟舞动时又结合特色基本武术，分为上下两大套路，上套主 要是表现麒麟玩耍动作，包括：舔脚，舔身、耍尾等，下套主要以表 现麒麟寻青、惊青、闻青、试青、采青、找青、逗青为表演主题，动 作上即兴发挥、风趣幽默、谐趣横生；上下套路配合，演绎着麒麟晃 头、张望、舔脚、舔尾、搔痒、滚地、嬉戏、见青、抢青、嚼青、吞</p>

<p>青,活灵活现的表达出麒麟的喜、怒、哀、乐、惊、疑、思等神态。 麒麟舞之后有武术表演，一般包括莫家拳、南拳和龙拳，又辅以刀、 剑、棍、盾板、戟、藤牌、大钹等十八武器。塘厦舞麒麟的场面热烈， 深受当地群众喜爱。 Usually, in a traditional Kylin team in Tangxia Town, there is only one Kylin, a set of gongs and drums, and a team flag, on which the team’s family name or hall name was marked. Each team has more than 20 members. During performing, the Kylin performers dance to the music of the percussion playing in front of the team flag, one performing Kylin’s head and another Kylin’s tail, and also perform some basic martial arts with characteristics. Two routines, upper and lower, are included in the martial arts. The upper routine mainly shows Kylin’s playing, which consists of such movements as licking feet and body, shaking tail, etc.. The lower routine mainly shows such themes through improvised and humorous movements as xunqing (looking for the greens), jingqing (being afraid of the greens), wenqing (smelling the greens), shiqing (feeling the greens), caiqing (plucking the greens), zhaoqing (seeking the greens), douqing( playing with the greens). The two routines coordinately interpret a series of Kylin’s behavior: shaking head, looking around, licking feet and tail, scratching, rolling, playing, jianqing (seeing the greens), qiangqing (grabing the greens), jiaoqing (chewing the greens), tunqing (swallowing the greens) and bearing: being happy or angry, sad or joyous, surprised, suspicious, thinking etc.. Generally, other martial arts like Mojia Quan (Mo’s Boxing), Nan Quan (Southern Style Boxing), Long Quan (Dragon Style Boxing) would follow the Kylin Dance, which are performed with the help of 18 weapons: sabre, sword, staff, shield, halberd, cane shied, Da Bo(a kind of cymbals used as weapons), etc.. 麒麟舞融音乐、舞蹈、工艺美术、武术、杂技于一体，既有美学 的欣赏价值，又有艺术、宗教、民俗、历史的研究价值，是节庆喜庆 活动的重要民间习俗。塘厦舞麒麟是当地逢年过节的传统节目之一，</p>

<p>其代表性传承人黄汉光先生认为，要将这项传统技艺传承下去，必须 要与时俱进，让年轻人接受和喜爱。“传统的舞麒麟只有一条麒麟， 视觉效果单调，节奏也比较缓慢，年轻人不喜欢”，他将一条麒麟独 舞改为2 条、4 条、6 条甚至9 条，提速表演节奏，增加动作，制造 冲突看点等等，还吸取舞狮舞龙的一些元素，提升表演难度。同时， 黄汉光先生通过整理和归纳，将锣、鼓、唢呐、麒麟等舞麒麟涉及到 的东西用不同符号代表，以通俗易懂的形式把上一辈只能口口相传的 乐谱“写”下来。 Kylin Dance, as an important festive folk custom, combining music, dance, arts and crafts, martial arts, acrobatics, has the aesthetic value as well as research value of art, religion, folkways and history. Tangxia Kylin Dance is one of the local traditional festival programs, whose representative inheritor, Mr. Huang Hanguang, believes that inheriting this feat must advance with the times and make it being acceptable and enjoyable among the young people. “Traditionally, there is only one Kylin. The monotonous visual effect and slow rhythm make Kylin Dance less popular among young people”, he says. Therefore, the solo dance to were changed to 2,4,6 or even 9 Kylins dancing together; the rhythm sped up; the motions added; conflicts created etc.. Some elements of Lion Dance and Dragon Dance were also assimilated to increase the performing level. Besides, Mr. Huang Hanguang collates and concludes the notations in the former generation and changes them into score by using different simple symbols of gongs, drums, suona, Kylin and other tools. 舞麒麟从最初的不起眼到现在所拥有的荣誉，这背后也经历了很 多的艰辛。除了政府大力支持等因素外，最重要的是这些传承人的坚 持，让气势磅礴的舞麒麟走到现在。 A lot of hardships had seen the process of the Kylin Dance from a noteless program to a famous one. In addition to the government’s support and other factors , the inheritors’ persistence is the key to today’s majestic Kylin Dance. 编译陈宇珊杨雯雯倪煜琪</p>

<p><strong>18 惠州龙门—舞火狗中的期盼</strong></p>

<p><strong>Longmen, Huizhou— the Expectation in Fire Dog Dance</strong></p>

<p>Longmen, Huizhou— the Expectation in Fire Dog Dance 蓝田瑶族乡位于广东省惠州市龙门县北部，有龙门县“北大门” 之称，东南与龙田镇连接，西南与天堂山交界。蓝田瑶族乡群山环抱， 历史悠久，许多传统的民俗都经历住了时间的考验，没有在历史长河 中淹没。由于地理环境，瑶族呈现出了与其他民族不同的风格，更有 着独具一格的民俗习惯。在群山围绕的环境下，蓝田瑶族展现出了不 同于中原文化的民族风格，保存度良好的民族风俗和节目，让信息交 流便利的世人耳目一新。 Located in the north of Longmen County, Huizhou City, Guangdong Province, the Lantian county of Yao nationality is taken as the “North Gate” of Longmen County, on the southeast of which lies Longtian town and southwest Mount Heaven. Surrounded by mountains, it is long-standing and many traditional customs have stood the test of time. The special geographical location makes the Yao nationality distinctive from others in style as well as customs. The well-kept customs and programs leave an refreshing impression on people, which display a distinguished ethnic style from that of the Yellow River culture. 中秋节，一个团圆的节日，每个民族都有不相同的庆祝方式，而 蓝田瑶族为这个节日赋予了一层新的意义，最大的体现便是舞火狗这 个传统民间习俗。相传，很久之前，外族来犯，皇帝多次派兵迎战， 都被打败。于是，皇帝出榜招贤御敌，宣布：“能退敌者，无论是谁， 可任选三位公主中的一位为妻。”两天过去了，无人敢揭榜。到了第 三天晚上，有一条毛发俊逸，龙腰虎背的狗来到皇帝前面。敌军来袭， 皇帝就命令这条狗去迎战。狗口中喷出火，大败敌军。但皇帝不愿意 将自己女儿嫁给一条狗，但那最小的女儿被这神犬折服，执意要嫁给 神犬。在农历八月十五晚上，神犬与公主举行了盛大的婚礼。婚后他 们有了四个孩子，但是奶水不够孩子喝，于是就挤狗奶给孩子喝，四 个孩子平安长大，一代一代地繁衍下去。 Each of the nationalities has its own way to celebrate the Mid-autumn Festival, a festival of reunion, while the Yao give a new significance to it mainly by performing the traditional Fire Dog Dance. It is said that before long, the emperor sent troops to fight against invaders, but ended in defeat. So the emperor ordered a proclamation to summon skillful men to fight against the enemy and announced whoever repelling the enemy can marry one of the three princesses. Two days passed, no one came forwad. On the third day night, a dog, with supple and elegant bright hair and strong body, came to the emperor. The dog was ordered to fight against the striking enemy and crushed them all by spitting fire. However, the emperor did not want to marry his</p>

<p>daughter to a dog while his youngest daughter was convinced by the dog and insisted on marrying the dog. On the fifteenth night of the eighth lunar month, the dog and the princess held a grand wedding. After marriage, they had four children, but there was no enough mother’s milk, they feed the children with the dog’s milk instead. The four children grew up safely and multiplied from generation to generation. 据说这神犬便是蓝田瑶族的始祖。为了纪念祖先，要瑶民永远记 住狗作为“再生之母”的恩德，规定每年农历八月十五团圆节（中秋 节）之夜，举行舞火狗活动。每个少女要参加2 到3 次的“舞火狗” 方能向族人宣示自己已经成年，进入谈婚论嫁的行列。由此在特定的 “团圆节”上，以少女为主体形成了社会性的群体活动，从而形成了 蓝田瑶族独具特色的“舞火狗”民间舞蹈。 It is said that the dog is the ancestor of the Lantian Yao nationality. In order to commemorate their ancestors and the grace of rebirth, the Yao stipulated to perform Fire Dog Dance on the night of Reunion Festival (Mid-Autumn Festival) on the 15th day of the 8th lunar month. Each of the Yao’s girls must take part in this performance two or three times to show her qualification to be an adult and talk about marriage. Thus, in the special Reunion Festival, the social group are mainly formed by young girls, then formed the unique folk dance of Lantian Yao nationality — Fire Dog Dance. “舞火狗”在瑶族文化中是独一无二的，它只属于蓝田瑶族。“舞 火狗”是为少女成人而举行的活动，是少女的成人礼。少女长到16 岁，就要举行成人礼了，一年一次，举办到18 岁。成人礼上，母亲 要给少女盛装打扮，头上要戴斗笠，斗笠上插满了香；手、腰、脚3 个部位包满了黄姜叶。拜祠堂、拜菜地，到各家各户拜灶神，之后来 到已架起篝火的开阔地上，举行仪式，做代代沿袭下来的传统动作，</p>

<p>然后举着火把，围着篝火跳起舞，唱起歌。围着火跳舞，叫“舞火狗”， 舞中唱的歌叫火狗歌。最后瑶族少女们汇集到溪河边，把卸下的香火 和黄姜叶抛入河中，并与对岸的瑶族少年进行情歌对唱。 Fire Dog Dance is unique in the Yao culture, it only belongs to the Lantian Yao nationalty. It is an event for young girls’ adult ceremony. It is annually performed for the 16-year old girls until 18-year old. Mothers would dress up their girls for the adult ceremony with a bamboo hat full of incenses and ginger leaves covering hands waist and feet. Then the girls would worship at the ancestral temple and vegetable field and pay obeisance to the Kitchen God of each family. Next, they come to the open ground where the bonfire has been set up to attend the adult ceremony and do the inherited traditional actions. After that, they would dance around the bonfire holding torches and sing songs. The dance is called Fire Dog Dance the song Fire Dog Song. At last, the Yao girls gathered by the river, threw the incense and ginger leaves into the river, and antiphonally sing love songs to the Yao boys on the other side. “舞火狗”这种独特的民间艺术蕴含着民间对自然的敬畏和感激 之情，也包含了对古老传说的一种精神传承,让感恩这一良好品质一 直传承下去。这一民族习俗更体现出了长辈对于晚辈的期望，希望晚 辈能好好成长，变得独立；也蕴含老者的敬重。但是，在新思潮的冲 击下，很多瑶族村民淡薄了传统的祖先崇拜观念。同时，旧有的以歌 传情的情感表达方式也慢慢被年轻人摒弃。舞火狗，这门独特的民间 艺术面临着失传的危险。据传承人谭松娣说，如今的瑶族少女只知道</p>

<p>“舞火狗”这个仪式，却不了解其中的文化内涵。现在的年轻人也羞 于在大庭广众之下对歌传情了。年轻人对传统的淡薄加上近年来民间 艺人陆续离世，致使舞火狗处于濒危状态，传唱者越来越少。对于这 种状况，我们需要将保护非物质文化遗产的关注提高。国家政府重视， 现代人有意识地去学习、发扬，那么“舞火狗”这独一无二的民间习 俗就不会消失。 This unique folk art displays not only the awe and gratitude of the people towards nature, but also the spiritual inheritance of ancient legends, that is, to passed on the good quality of paying gratitude. What’s more, it reflects the elders’ expectation for the younger generation that they can be well-developed and independent and also the respect for the old. However, due to the impact of the new trend, the traditional concept of ancestor worship of many Yao villagers have been weakened. Also, the traditional way of expressing emotions by singing is gradually abandoned by the young people. Thus, Fire Dog dance, as a unique art, is in danger of being lost. According to one of the inheritor, Lin Hedi, today’s Yao girls only know the ceremony instead of its meaning. Young people, nowadays, are too shy to express their love through singing to each other in public. Their indifference coupled with the death of folk artists in recent years led to the endangered status of Fire Dog Dance, so there are fewer and fewer singers.In view of this situation, we need to pay more attention to the protection of intangible cultural heritage. Government’s attaching importance and modern people’s conscious learning and promoting will stop Fire Dog Dance fading away. 编译胡佳浩</p>

<p><strong>19 佛山无影脚</strong></p>

<p><strong>Foshan Shadowless Kick</strong></p>

<p>Foshan Shadowless Kick 一说佛山无影脚，很多人第一反应就是黄飞鸿的武功绝技。在南 方，武术绝大多数以腰、手为主，很少运用脚的方面，忽略了脚的功 夫。黄飞鸿多年的卖武生涯，使他学习到了很多南方北方的武术文化， 通过多地交流，黄飞鸿将北方的一些脚法与南方拳术融合，进行创新， 创出了“佛山无影脚”。无影脚强调的是脚法，在以快制敌的同时， 保证脚下方寸不乱，只有脚下沉稳才能出手敏捷，才能抵挡和消解外 来的攻击。因此扎实的马步功底是这项绝技的根本。确切地说，无影 脚是一种声东击西的做法。在武术上这应该不算什么独门绝技，特殊 的地方就是突出了攻击身体下盘的技巧。 When it comes to Foshan Shadowless Kick, Huang Feihong’s martial arts stunt would firstly come into many people’s minds. In the south, martial arts are mostly related to waist and hands and less to feet. Years of making living through martial arts give Huang a lot of chances of learning of martial culture of both the south and the north. Foshan Shadowless Kick was created after communications and his integration of northern footwork and southern boxing. Shadowless Kick emphasizes footwork, which ensures the body balance while attacking the enemy quickly. Only when it is steady at feet can a person make a quick move and defend against the attack. Therefore, solid horse stance is the foundation of this stunt. To be precise, shadowless kick aims at creating a diversion, which is not a normal stunt in martial arts but an outstanding technique of attacking the lower part of the body. 扎马步是“佛山无影脚”的根本,是因为在扎马步过程中，可以 锻炼身体的平衡感，熟悉掌握身体的重心，以达到“盘根”结实，从 而下盘稳如泰山。其次，扎马步还可以锻炼下肢的力量感和肌肉感. 脚的功夫顾名思义是大腿与小腿、脚的较量。扎马步时,身体腰背部 挺直、重心下压、大腿与地面平行等，在这个过程中，身体的全部重 量就下放到了腿上。如果能够坚持下去，腿部肌肉越来越发达，双腿 的力量会不断加强,从而在面对敌人时，腿部力量也有急速上升。最 重要的是练武之人要求心态平和，遇事不慌不乱。扎马步还能稳定情 绪，培养坚强的毅力。当一个人处于一个非常放松、安静的心态时， 时间越久心境会越来越平静，做事也会更加有毅力。因此只有当一个 人下盘稳定，面对敌人时临危不乱才能达到出手快狠准，尽快击倒敌 人的水平。 Horse stance is the foundation Foshan Shadowless Kick because in the process doing that, body balance and gravity would be trained and mastered, and thus the lower part of the body can be as stabilized as the Mount Tai. What’s more, horse</p>

<p>stance can also exercise the lower limbs’ sense of strength and muscle. The footwork, is the trial of strength among thighs, shins and feet. When doing horse stance, the back should be straight, the center of gravity pressed down, and the thighs parallel to the ground, so all the weight is placed on the legs during this period. If persisted, the legs will be more muscular and stronger. In the end, the strength will also be increased rapidly when attacking enemies. The most important thing is that a martial artist should have a peaceful mentality with no rashness, panic or mess. Thus, doing horse stance set one’s mind at rest and cultivate his strong will. When one in a relaxed and calm spirit, the longer the more peaceful and determined he will be. Therefore, only with a stable lower body can one launch fast, aggressive and accurate attacks against the enemy quickly and calmly. 黄飞鸿第三代传人余志伟的师傅曾说：“无影脚是很厉害，但是 如果你没有结实的基本功，就算教给你也没用。根本打不出来，余志 伟扎了12 年的马步才有一个“稳”字才被师傅教予无影脚的基本功。” 除了脚的功夫了得，手上功夫也不可忽视，在无影脚发招前，大多是 先以手出招，让敌人眼花缭乱，等其被上身吸引时，再趁此机会起脚 攻击他的下部，达到一招制敌的效果。 The master of Yu Zhiwei, the third generation successor of Huang Feihong, once said, “shadowless kick is sharp yet useless without solid basic skills. It took Yu Zhiwei 12 years to be in a solid status before being taught the basic skills of shadowless kick.” Strong footwork is needed, sleights of hand cannot be ignored, most of which were used before shadowless kick to confuse the enemy and subdue him by shadowless kick after he was attracted to the hands.</p>

<p>从“佛山无影脚”的练成我悟出了一个道理：“只要功夫深，铁 杵磨成针。”做一件事要有坚定不移的意志和相信成功的信念。只要 有决心，肯下功夫，无论是多大的困难都能克服。在生活和学习中也 一样。成功的彼岸并不遥远，只要相信自己，坚持不懈，坚持的后面 就是成功。 From the practice of Foshan Shadowless Kick, I have realized a truth that constant grinding turns an iron rod into a needle. To do a thing successfully requires an unshakable will and confidence to success. As long as you are determined and willing to work hard, you can overcome any difficulty. So it is in life and study. It is not far from success, as long as you believe in yourself and keep doing, success can be achieved. 编译高紫晴</p>

