<h2>三、民间建筑与文化</h2>

<p><strong>1 隐秘的炮台</strong></p>

<p><strong>A Covered Fort</strong></p>

<p>A Covered Fort 说起崎碌炮台，许多人可能不甚了了；但谈起《天津条约》，人 们可能还颇有些印象。据史册记载，十九世纪中期，第一、二次鸦片 战争爆发，腐败无能的清朝政府战败后与美、英、法等列强签订了丧 权辱国的不平等条约：《天津条约》。其中，《中英天津条约》和《中 法天津条约》均要求清朝政府新增通商口岸，妄图进一步打开中国的 大门。而当时的潮州，也就是现在的汕头，便是当时新增的十大通商 口岸之一。 Speaking of the Qilu Fort, many people may not know much about it; but when it comes to Treaty of Tientsin, one may still have some impression on it. According to the historical records, the First and Second Opium Wars broke out one after another in the mid-19th century, the corrupted and incompetent Qing Government signed the unequal treaty that humiliated the nation and forfeited the sovereignty after being defeated: Treaty of Tientsin, which was signed with the United States, Britain and France and other great powers. Among the treaties, both Treaty of Tientsin between Britain and China and Treaty of Tientsin between French and China required Qing Government to add some new trading ports in an attempt to further open the door of China. At that time Chaozhou which is named as Shantou currently, was one of the ten new trading ports. 当时，外国商船纷至沓来的情景随处可见，海防布局结构松散。 驻潮州总兵方耀为顺应民意，故以“邻分不净，潮海严防”为由，奏 请清廷建筑崎碌炮台，也就是后来我们所称的石炮台。 At that time, influx of foreign merchant ships could be seen everywhere, and layout of coastal defense was unfirming. Fang Yao, the commander-in-chief garrisoned in Chaozhou, pleaded with the Qing Government for building Qilu Fort on the ground of “the tidal sea should be strictly guarded” and so as to comply with the public, which was known as the Stone Fort later. 崎碌炮台于清代同治十三年开始建造，光绪五年竣工（即 1874-1879 年），历时五年，耗资八万银元，这在当时是一笔不小的 财政开支。崎碌炮台位于当时旧汕头（当时称为“潮州”）的东南角。 从上往下俯视，它属于环圆形城堡建筑，与当时隔岸苏安山上的炮台 相呼应，扼住汕头海湾出入口。地理位置十分险要，是清代粤东地区 的主要海防建筑。</p>

<p>The construction of Qilu Fort began in the 13th year of Tongzhi Emperor of Qing Dynasty. The project had lasted for five years and finally completed in the fifth year of Guangxu Emperor of Qing Dynasty (1874-1879), taking 80,000 silver dollars which was a considerable financial expenditure at that moment. Qilu Fort was situated at the southeast corner of Old Shantou (then known as Chaozhou). Looking down from the above, it was a circular castle building, echoing the fort on The Su’an Mountain across the shore at that time, and occupying the vital entrance and exit of Shantou Bay. Its geographical position was very dangerous but crucial, which was the main costal defense building in the eastern Guangdong region in Qing Dynasty. 炮台独具建筑特色，环圆状带形墙体的城堡，墙体以贝灰、沙煮 烂，再以糯米粥、红糖调和夯筑，配以花岗岩石料；台面跑道用贝灰 和糯米浆混合夯筑，炮台底层坑道与十字交叉拱窟窿全部用非风化花 岗岩规格石砌筑，垛口炮位均铺上花岗岩石条，石缝严密，砌筑坚固。 The Qilu Fort’s wall is in the shape of circular cone and its barbette has unique architecture features. The wall is built with overcooked shell ash and sand, and rammed with glutinous rice porridge, brown sugar and granite stones. The counter surface is set up with a mixture of shell ash and rice paste. The bottom pit road of the fort and the cross-arch hole are constructed with non-weathered granite specification stone. The stacking emplacement is covered with granite tightly and firmly.</p>

<p>炮台占地总面积19607 平方米, 有一条宽23 米、水深3 米的护 台河环绕炮台一周。要知道，炮楼过去肯定是没有桥的，内城与外围 隔着这么一条河，即使想游到炮楼里也不是一件容易的事情。炮台 分上下两层，各设18 个炮位和若干枪眼，底层的炮巷4.1 米，长约 300 米深邃迂回。 Covering a total area of 19,607 square meters, the fort is surrounded by a river which is 23 meters wide and 3 meters deep. It is acknowledged that there must have been no bridge in the past, and the inner city and the outside are separated by such a river, it is not easy to swim to the turret. The Fort is divided in to two layers, each with 18 guns positions and a number of gun holes. The gun lane at the bottom is 4.1 meters long and about 300 meters deep and roundabout. 小道上，“崎碌炮台”四个大字内嵌于炮台石壁，异常显眼。进 入炮台内道，几十个通风口，大的小的，或分布于石壁上方，或设立 在石壁两侧，紧密而整齐。从内道穿过洞口来到内城，你会看见内城 有一道27 级波纹型石阶。由于当时正处战争频发之时，波浪型的石 阶设计便于士兵将炮械循级推上台面；台阶较隐蔽，是作战时的快速 通道，便于作战时疏散及向台面运送弹药。台面上，18 个炮塔坚固 严密，对海而设，其上“大清光绪制造”“乙卯年”九个大字清晰可 见。五千斛前膛洋炮属炮台里最大的一座，射程可达十五、六华里， 对入侵者有一定的威慑作用。有趣的是，台面上有72 个通风报话塔， 每三个为一组，呈品字型鼎立，用于炮塔上下报信通话联络及供底层 的通风采光，与炮台内道的几十个大小通风口相得益彰。炮台广场东 北角设有一口淡水井，其水质甘醇清甜，是当时清兵生活饮水的重要 来源。炮台东北面有一月牙型点将台，是当时兵丁们操练、听从指挥 的操场。想象一下，阳光炽烈，照得青铜铠甲泛起一片金黄色的光， 操场上士兵们快速移动的脚步整齐划一，坚定有力。如今这片绿油油 的草场，正是当时战士们体现英雄本色的地方。 On the path, the four characters " Qilu Fort " are embedded in the wall of the fort, which is very conspicuous. Entered the inner tracks of the fort, dozens of air vents, large and small, are distributed on the top of the stone wall, or set up on both sides of the stone wall, close and neat. From the inner passage through the opening to the inner city, you will find a 27-step corrugated stone staircase. It was a time of war that the wavy stone steps made it easier for soldiers to push their cannon machinery on the platform. The stairs are covered, which is a fast track for evacuation and ammunition transportation. On the platform, the 18 turrets are firm, and set against the sea, with nine visible characters “Made in Guangxu Emperor of Qing Dynasty” and “Year of</p>

<p>Yimao”. Wu Qian Hu Qian Tang Western Cannon is the largest one of the forts, with a range of 7.5~6 kilometers, which has a certain deterrent effect on the invaders. What is interesting is that there are 72 ventilation towers on the platform, three in a group, standing in the shape of letters, which are used for communication between the turret and the ground floor, and for ventilation and lighting, which complement the dozens of vents of different sizes in the inner tracks of the fort. There is a freshwater well in the northeast corner of the fort square, whose water is sweet and clean. It is an important source of drinking water for Qing soldiers at that time. There is a crescent - shaped military parade platform in the northeast of the fort, which is the playground for soldiers to drill and obey commands. Just imagine, the sun shines on the bronze armor into golden, the soldiers on the playground move fast with uniform and firm step. And now the green meadow is where the soldiers showed their fortitude and hero character. 崎碌炮台兴建至今已有一百多年，但整座建筑尚未发现裂缝和崩 塌现象，是清末粤东海防设施的代表作。如今，改造后的崎碌炮台， 也称为石炮台公园，是一座环境清幽、古朴的公园。走在那里，你会 领略到古人在建筑方面的“工匠精神”，这在今天，也是让我们难以 望其项背的。 Qilu Fort has been built for more than 100 years, but the whole building has not been found cracks and collapses, which is a representative of the eastern Guangdong coastal defense facilities in the late Qing Dynasty. Presently, after the transformation of the Qilu Fort, also known as the Stone Fort Park, is a quiet and simple park. Walking around there, you will appreciate the ancient people's "craftsman spirit" in architecture, which is hard for us to catch up today. 编译林冬宜</p>

<p><strong>2 古韵顺德，碧江金楼</strong></p>

<p><strong>Bijiang Golden House in Ancient Shunde</strong></p>

<p>Bijiang Golden House in Ancient Shunde 碧江金楼坐落于“中国历史文化名村”北滘碧江。又名赋鹤楼， 于清代嘉庆、道光年间所建，已有几百年历史。金楼古建筑群由泥楼、 职方第、金楼、南山祠、见龙门、亦渔遗塾、慕堂祠、三兴大宅等多 座建筑物组成。集中了宅第、祠堂、书塾、书斋、园林等功能，保留 着干打垒、蚝壳墙、水摸墙、水磨砖、“镬耳山墙”等等岭南特色的 古建筑实物。 Bijiang Golden House is located in Bijiang, Beijiao, a "Chinese Historical and Cultural Village". Also known as Fuhe House. It was built during the Jiaqing and Daoguang reigns of the Qing Dynasty and has a history of several hundred years. The ancient building complex of the Golden House is composed of mud buildings, Zhifangdi, Jinlou, Nanshan Temple, Jianlongmen, Yiyu Ruins, Mutang Temple, Sanxing Mansion and other buildings. Concentrating the functions of the mansion, ancestral hall, school, study, garden, etc., it retains the ancient architectural objects with Lingnan characteristics such as dry base, oyster shell wall, water touch wall, water mill brick, "wok gable" and so on. 晚清时期，慈禧的干女儿、法务大臣戴鸿慈的女儿戴佩琼，下嫁 时任兵部员外郎的碧江人苏丕文的孙子苏伯雨。当时这座金楼还只是 苏家的私人藏书阁，为了迎娶这位“格格”，苏家特意将其贴金改造， 以作结婚之用。苏家大少苏伯雨将戴佩琼安置在金楼之中伴读，夜夜 有美人红袖添香，故传有金屋藏娇的佳话。首层前廊停放的官轿以及 楼内上下所有家具摆设和古董字画，全部是旧时原物，其中精美的八 宝床是金楼稀世珍宝之一。这些景点近年拂尘惊世，被专家和游客总 结出古、博、精、真四大特点。明清时期广府地区的民居结构形式可 以在这里找到活标本，数百年顺德人从耕读文化到儒商文化再到积累 吸收外地文化的轨迹，在这里历历可寻。 In the late Qing Dynasty, Dai Peiqiong, goddaughter of Empress Dowager Cixi and daughter of Minister of Justice Dai Hongci, married Su Boyu, the grandson of Su Piwen from Bijiang who was a member of the military department at the time. At that time, this golden house was only the private library of the Su family. In order to marry this "princess", the Su family specially modified it with gold for marriage. Su Boyu, the first young master of the Su family, placed Dai Peiqiong in the golden building as a companion to read. With a beautiful woman accompany every night, there is a gossip of a beauty hidden in a golden house. The official sedan parked on the front</p>

<p>porch on the first floor, as well as all the furnishings and antique calligraphy and paintings in the upper and lower floors of the building, are all old originals, among which the exquisite eight-treasure bed is one of the rare treasures of the Golden House. These scenic spots have shocked the world in recent years, and experts and tourists have summed up the four characteristics of ancient, rich, refined and true. Living specimens can be found here for the residential structure of the Guangfu area during the Ming and Qing dynasties. For hundreds of years, the people of Shunde have gone from farming and reading culture to Confucian merchant culture to accumulating and absorbing foreign cultures, which can be found here. 清代道光年间，苏家有子苏鹤，号二悟坡道人，作二十四咏，概 括碧江当地的人文自然景观，并以此咏为线索，雕作铜壁，重现历史 上的繁华碧江，被誉名为碧江版清明上河图。这幅碧江版的“清明上 河图”23·8 米长, 1·5 米高，上面所绘风景栩栩如生，是不可多得 的珍品。 During the Daoguang period of the Qing Dynasty, Su He, a son of the Su family, also known as Erwu Slope Taoist, made a twenty-four chant, summarizing the local cultural and natural landscape of Bijiang, and using this chant as a clue, he carved the bronze wall and reproduced the history. The prosperous Bijiang is known as the Bijiang version of the famous painting Riverside Scene at Qingming Festival. This Bijiang version painting is 23.8 meters long and 1.5 meters high. It is a rare treasure with vivid scenery.</p>

<p>金楼所有装饰都取用了中国民间的木雕艺术，并巧妙渗入了外来 的艺术风格，院庭内保留了清末年间名士如刘塘、宋湘等为这个家庭 题写的木、石匾额及题赠的书画翰墨真迹，还陈设着清代的官轿、踱 步床、酸枝制作的家具，可以体会到当时珠三角富庶人家的生活，也 看到岭南文化在建筑艺术的建树。 All decorations of the golden house adopt the Chinese folk woodcarving art, and cleverly infiltrate foreign artistic styles. In the courtyard atrium retained from the late Qing celebrities such as, Liu Tang, Song Xiang etc. inscribed for the family, such as the wood and stone plaques, the original painting and calligraphy, the official sedan chairs, pacing beds, and furniture made of rosewood. You can experience the life of the wealthy families in the Pearl River Delta at that time, and you can also see the achievements of Lingnan culture in architectural art. 如今，碧江村古韵犹存。泥屋背后的蚝壳墙，还排列得非常整齐。 这些具有冬暖夏凉、防风防火功能的蚝壳墙，在古代珠三角富有阶级 甚为流行。泰兴大街的古祠堂群，古宅生辉。傍晚，夕阳铺洒在栉比 的瓦阵上，与金楼的光辉映照，怀古的悠悠情，如诗如画的流光溢彩 晚霞，更能让人忘却尘世中的喧嚣。 Today, the ancient Bijiang Village still exists. The oyster shell wall behind the mud house is also very neatly arranged. These oyster shell walls, which are warm in winter and cool in summer, windproof and fireproof, were very popular in the ancient Pearl River Delta wealthy class. The ancient ancestral halls on Taixing Street are shining. In the evening, the setting sun spreads on the tile array, reflecting the brilliance of the golden house, the leisurely feeling of nostalgia, and the picturesque sunset glow, making people forget the hustle and bustle of the world. 编译钟敏渟</p>

<p><strong>3 肇庆宋城墙</strong></p>

<p><strong>City Wall of Song Dynasty in Zhaoqing</strong></p>

<p>City Wall of Song Dynasty in Zhaoqing 肇庆是历史悠久的岭南名郡，位于广东省中西部，西江流域中下 游，扼两广交通咽喉，控西江干道，历代为兵家必争之地。现如今已 成为当地的旅游胜地。 Zhaoqing is a famous county of Lingnan with a long history. It is located in the middle and lower reaches of Xijiang River basin in the central and western part of Guangdong Province. It dominates the traffic throat of two regions of Guangdong and Guangxi and the main road of Xijiang River. It has been a battleground for military strategists in the past. Now it has become a local tourist attraction. 在宋代以前，肇庆没有城墙，1041 年，广西部落首领侬智高起 兵反宋。1052 年，他率军沿西江挥师连续攻陷南宁、封开、德庆等 州府后直逼端州当时的端州守臣丁宝臣，因无城可守而竟仓惶而逃。 后来，朝廷派大将军狄青才平定了这场叛乱。 Zhaoqing had no city walls before the Song Dynasty. In 1041, Nong Zhigao, a tribal leader from Guangxi, rebelled against the Song. In 1052, he led his troops along the Xijiang River to successively capture Nanning, Fengkai, Deqing and other provincial capitals, and then directly forced Ding Baochen, then governor of Duanzhou, to flee in panic because he had no city to defend.It was only later that the rebellion was put down by the imperial general Di Qing. 鉴于这一历史教训，为抵御敌兵，知州江柬之在宋皇祐三年根据 建城要依山靠水的原则，修筑土城。城池坐北向南，背靠将军岭，面 向西江河。将州衙、县署所在的两个小土岗及南面部分溪塘用城墙围 起来，并在城西三台岗建真君堂、三圣堂等道教寺院，开始了官廨与 道观为主的府城建设，当时土城也叫“子城”，主要目的是为了守护 府衙。 In view of this historical lesson, in order to resist the enemy soldiers, Mayor Jiang Jianzhi built the terra city in the third year of the Song Dynasty according to the principle that the city should be built by mountains and water. The City sitting north to south, back to the General Mountain range, facing the West River. The two small mounds where the Prefectures and county offices were located and the southern part of the river pond were enclosed with city walls. Taoist temples such as The Zhenjun Temple and the Three Saints Temple were built in the west of the city. These marked the beginning of the construction of official halls and Taoist temples. At that time, the</p>

<p>the terra city was also named "Zi City", and its main purpose was to protect the government office. 城墙体上有宋、元、明、清、民国历代的青砖，甚至保留了整段 宋砖筑砌的城墙，宋代青砖有九种不同的规格，是历史上多次修葺的 证据，明清两代历经近20 次修聋，堪称“砖的博物馆”。 There are black bricks from the Song, Yuan, Ming, Qing, and the Republic of China on the city wall, and even a whole section of the Song Dynasty brick wall is preserved. Black bricks in Song Dynasty embody nine different specifications, which is the historical evidence of many repairs. The Ming and Qing Dynasties experienced nearly 20 repairs, which is called a "brick museum". 宋代的城墙开四门：东曰宋崇、西曰镇南、南曰端溪、北曰朝天。 城门之上各有城门楼1 座，四门之外有瓮城，城墙四角各有角楼1 座， 城外还有护城河。端州宋城墙因保留了广东唯一的、全国极少见的主 体及城周基本完整的宋代砖城墙，于2002 年被列为第五批全国重点 保护单位。 The city wall in the Song Dynasty had four gates: Song Chong in the east, Zhen Nan in the west, Duanxi in the south and Chaotian in the north. Above the city gate each has a gate tower, four outside the gate has a weng city, four corners of the city each has a turret, outside the moat. The Duanzhou Song city wall was listed as the fifth batch of national key protection units in 2002, because it retained the only part</p>

<p>rarely seen in Guangdong province and the basically complete brick city wall of Song Dynasty in the whole country. 古城墙在历史上防水患多于御敌，所以从明代开始，便将河堤与 城墙相连，这样对保护城里百姓的人身和财产安全起到了很大的作 用。从筑墙后的777 年间，记载西江洪水为患的有104 次，联围缺口 13 次。特别是在民国四年，西江河水暴涨，城外是汪洋泽国，城内 却安然无恙，可见古城墙的建造不但起到了御敌作用，更显抗击洪水 的功能。 In history, the ancient city walls suffered more from water-proof than against the enemy. Therefore, from the Ming Dynasty, the river bank was connected with the wall, which played a great role in protecting the safety of the people in the city. During the 777 years after the construction of the wall, 104 floods were recorded in the Xijiang River, and 13 times were linked to encircle the gap. Especially in the fourth year of the Republic of China, the river of Xijiang river rose sharply. Outside the city was the flood, but the inside was safe and sound. It can be seen that the construction of the ancient city wall not only played a role in defending the enemy, but also in fighting against floods. 肇庆宋城墙作为肇庆历史文化的重要组成部分,是肇庆历史长河 中的一块瑰宝,在肇庆旅游城市的建设中起到举足轻重的纽带作用. 对宋城墙的保护与开发利用将对肇庆现在和未来的发展有着积极作 用。 As an important part of Zhaoqing's history and culture, the City wall of Zhaoqing in Song Dynasty is a treasure in the long history and plays an important role in its tourist city construction . The protection, development and utilization of the city wall of Song Dynasty will play a positive role in the present and future development of Zhaoqing. 编译 张锦如贾宇新郭译文</p>

<p><strong>4 嵌瓷---镶嵌在屋顶上的一颗明珠</strong></p>

<p><strong>Inlay Porcelain——A Pearl Inlaid on the Roof</strong></p>

<p>Inlay Porcelain——A Pearl Inlaid on the Roof 嵌瓷，又称“贴饶”或“扣饶”，是潮汕特有的一种传统建筑装 饰技艺，与潮州木雕、潮州石雕三者形成最具代表性的潮州民间传统 建筑艺术。主要分为大寮嵌瓷和普宁嵌瓷两类，且有平嵌、浮嵌和立 体嵌等形式。 Inlay Porcelain, also known as "Tie Rao" or "Kou Rao", is a unique traditional architectural decoration technique in Chaoshan, forming the most representative traditional Chaozhou folk architectural art together with Chaozhou wood carving and Chaozhou stone carving. It is mainly composed of two types of porcelain, Daliao embedded porcelain and Puning embedded porcelain, including the flat inlaid form, floating inlaid form and stereoscopic inlaid form. 从明代至今，嵌瓷发展日久岁深，已流传了400 多年。明神宗时 期，勤劳与智慧的潮汕匠人得灵感于雕塑，采用破碎瓷片加以改造塑 型，首创碎瓷制为花卉器品并嵌于屋檐以装饰的方法。清代嵌瓷之风 盛行，据嘉庆《澄海县志》中描述：“望族喜营屋宇，雕梁画栋，池 台竹树，必极工巧。大宗小宗，竞建祠堂，争夸壮丽，不惜资费。” 嵌瓷之发展应用由此可见一斑。 Since the Ming Dynasty, Inlay Porcelain has been developed profoundly with a history of more than 400 years. During the reign of Ming Shenzong, the Chaoshan artisans, who were industrious and intelligent, took inspiration from the sculpture and used broken porcelain pieces to create a new piece of artwork, Inlay Porcelain. They are the first to make broken porcelain pieces into flower ornaments and inlay them on eaves for decoration. In the Qing Dynasty, the trend of Inlay Porcelain prevailed. According to the description of Chenghai county annals in Jiaqing period, “The well-known families like to build houses, carve beams and paint buildings. Pools and gardens must be built and bamboos and other trees must be planted with superb craftmanship. Clans of different sizes compete with each other to build magnificent ancestral halls regardless of the cost.” The development and application of Inlay Porcelain is evident here. 作为潮州建筑的标志，嵌瓷不仅造型各异，且蕴意美好。取材于 民间传说，历史典故，传统戏剧，神话故事等等，按造型嵌瓷可分三 类：瑞兽类，人物类以及动物花草类。瑞兽常为龙凤，麒麟，鹤鹿等 等，寄寓富贵吉祥，福寿安康；人物类则表现人物的品德精神，气势</p>

<p>风貌；而动植物类则为飞鸟走兽、花卉瓜果等，寓意和平美好。妆点 于祠堂，宗庙，或民间屋舍的厝头，屋角，屋脊，或是门壁，墙壁上， 这些色彩缤纷、琳琅满目的嵌瓷以点睛成龙之笔与潮州建筑融为一 体，为之增添颜色，点缀其中。 As a landmark of Chaozhou architecture, Inlay Porcelain is not only diverse in shape, but contains good implications. Based on folklore, historical allusions, traditional dramas, myths and so on, Inlay Porcelain can be divided into three categories according to the shapes: auspicious beasts, figures, animals and plants. Auspicious animals are often dragons and phoenixes, kylins, cranes and deer, etc., meaning wealth and luck, longevity and health; the character category embodies the character's moral spirit and imposing manner; the last kind is for birds, animals, flowers and fruits, implying peace and beauty. Put on the pediments, corners, ridges, doors and walls of ancestral halls, temples, or folk houses, these colorful and dazzling porcelain inlays are integrated with Chaozhou architecture as a finishing touch, adding color and embellishment to it. 嵌瓷可简单的分为构图，塑体，钳剪，和嵌贴几个步骤。根据立 意，师傅预先对作品进行整体的构图设计，从形态结构、特征大小、 再到色彩搭配。塑体时期，用以熟石灰和毛边纸为主要原料制成的纸 灰泥堆砌塑形，决定成品大体。钳剪则指用剪钳将瓷片裁成大小合适， 线条和谐流畅的形状。等各个零碎的瓷片背后涂上纸灰，依序填补， 经细致调整后，一件惊才绝艳的作品便问世了。 In a nutshell, Inlay Porcelain can be divided into composition, molding, shearing, and inlaying. According to the intention, the masters pre-designed the overall composition of the work, from shape and structure, features and size, and then to the</p>

<p>color matching. During the molding process, the paper plaster, which mainly made of hydrated lime and moben paper, is used to shape and determine the overall shape of the finished product. Shearing refers to the cutting of ceramic chips to a proper size and smooth edges with the cutting pliers. Before a stunning work came out, every piece of porcelain must be coated with paper plaster, filled in order, and carefully adjusted. 嵌瓷的流传可归于三大原因：其一，瓷器色彩明丽，历久弥新。 作为室外装饰，饱经风霜而不受侵蚀是嵌瓷得以延续至今的关键因 素。其二，瓷器生产地的底蕴。嵌瓷不可或缺的原料就是瓷片，而潮 州作为瓷都，其运输与生产中产生的大量碎瓷为嵌瓷的诞生和发展奠 定了基础。其三，潮州重视祠堂的态度与匠人爱财惜物和别出心裁创 作思维的结合。在匠人手中，碎瓷变废为宝，具有审美价值，得以重 焕新的生命力。 There are three reasons why Inlay Porcelain can be passed on from generations to generations: firstly, porcelain is characterized by its brilliance and durability. As a kind of outdoor decoration, the key to the continuation of Inlay Porcelain is that it experiences wind and rain without erosion. Secondly, the historical background of the porcelain production place. The essential raw material of Inlay Porcelain is porcelain shards, and in Chaozhou, the capital of porcelain, a large amount of broken porcelain pieces can be collected in the process of transportation and production, which laid a foundation for the birth and development of Inlay Porcelain. Thirdly, the combination of attitude that Chaozhou attaches importance to ancestral temple and thinking that craftsman's cherish wealth and treasure things and creative. Under the craftsman's</p>

<p>skillful hands, broken porcelain is transformed into treasure, which has aesthetic value and glows with a new vitality. “破而后立，晓喻新生！”可谓是嵌瓷的真实写照。从零散的碎 瓷片，到精美的工艺品，嵌瓷已不单是一项传统的民间建筑装饰技艺， 它更是潮人精神信仰的凝聚，是潮州街头巷尾里不可或缺的“一出好 戏”。如今，嵌瓷虽因时代变化导致的建筑文化差异而衰落，但在新 一代潮州匠人的不懈努力下，在每一个传承者的手中，嵌瓷仍散发着 它勃勃的生命气息。 "Break and then stand up, get a new life and breakthrough!" can be described as a true snapshot of Inlay Porcelain. From scattered ceramic chips to exquisite handicrafts, Inlay Porcelain is not only a traditional architectural decoration technique, but also the cohesion of Chaozhou people's spiritual beliefs, and it is an indispensable "good show" in the streets and lanes of Chaozhou. Nowadays, changes taking place in the present era have led to the decline of Inlay Porcelain due to the differences in architectural culture, but with the unremitting efforts of the new generation of Chaozhou crafters, in the hands of every heir, the Inlay Porcelain technique still smells of life. 编译陈艺杨立珊</p>

<p><strong>5 客家“围龙屋”</strong></p>

<p><strong>Hakka Dragon House</strong></p>

<p>Hakka Dragon House 被称为“世界客都”的梅州，群聚着这么一种人：“他们讲着客 家话，住着围龙屋。他们热情好客，他们勤劳能干。” 早在西晋（永 康元年）开始，他们不断地南迁，直至两宋才定居下来。一部分客家 人定居在了广东，以梅州为中心，以放射状向周围扩散。 Meizhou, known as the "Hakka capital of the world," is crowded with people who speak Hakka and live in Hakka Dragon House. They are hospitable, hardworking and capable. As early as the Western Jin Dynasty (the first year of Yongkang), they continued to move south until the Song Dynasty, and then they finally settled down. Some of them stayed in the present Guangdong province and now their descendents’ living area radiates to different places in Guangdong province with Meizhou as the center. “围龙屋”其历史源远流长，始于唐宋，盛于明清。它主要隐蔽 于山区，亦或丘陵，故有“无客不住山，逢山必有客。”由于是客家 人的主要建筑，又有客家楼、客屋等昵称。 "Hakka Dragon House" has a long history, starting from the Tang and Song dynasties, flourished in the Ming and Qing dynasties. It is hidden in the mountains, or hills, when it is built. So it is said that where there are mountains, there are Hakka people. As it is the main building of the Hakka people, it also has the nickname of Hakka building, Hakka house and so on. “围龙屋”用抬梁式与穿斗式相结合的建筑技巧，适合于山区搭 建出“一围二厅三卧”等各具特色的样式。在历史长河中，因战乱频 繁，盗贼盗窃，地域限制等众多原因，“围龙屋”便有着易守难攻（营 垒式风格，楼高墙厚）的特点。 “Hakka Dragon House” combines post and lintel construction technique, and, column and tie construction technique, which is suitable for people living in the mountainous area to construct buildings of "a circle, two halls, three bedrooms" and other distinctive building styles. In the long history, due to frequent wars, burglary, geographical restrictions and many other reasons, "Hakka Dragon House" has the characteristics of being easy to defend and difficult to attack (fortress-style, high buildings and thick walls).</p>

<p>从外部视角看，“围龙屋”以祖堂为中心，环环相套，层层围合， 是一个封闭式外部结构。 From the external perspective, the "Hakka Dragon House" is a closed external structure with ancestral hall as the center, enclosed in circles and surrounded by layers. 从内部结构角度看，其里厢间功能齐全，大厅，卧室，厨房，厕 所，浴室，水井，鸡窝，猪圈，仓库应有尽有，是典型的自给自足， 自得其乐的大本营。 From the internal perspective, its compartments are fully functional, hall, bedroom, kitchen, toilet, bathroom, well, chicken nest, pigsty, warehouse and everything for living. It's a classic stronghold where you can feed yourself and enjoy yourself. 从文化角度看，“围龙屋”呈现一种对称模型，像一个圆，这也 就反衬出了客家人主次分明，尊卑有序的的思想。他们供奉祖先祠堂 就如教徒在教堂忠诚的祈祷一般，神圣而又庄严。 From the cultural perspective, "Hakka Dragon House" presents a symmetrical model, like a circle, which reflects Hakka people's emphasis on the distinction of primary and secondary respects , and hierarchical order. They worship ancestral hall as sacredly and solemnly as a believer of a religion can in the church. “围龙屋”呈现的庞大也映射出客家人的群居性，形成以一个“祠 堂”为中心的一个大家庭，各得其所，优雅舒适。是古人所追求的天 伦之乐，也是团团圆圆的合家团聚。当然，也反映了客家人的性格特</p>

<p>点，热情好客（遇到远方客家，我们都会热情来句“日莱食碧茶”‘客 家话’）、团结互助（遇到邻居有难，都会主动过去“等亿哈，诶莱 帮泥”‘客家话’）、尊老爱幼、知情达理、勤劳能干……等。 The large size of "Hakka Dragon House"also reflects the gregarious nature of hakka people, forming a large family with an "ancestral hall" as the center, each sub-family in its own place, elegant and comfortable. It is the happiness of family and family reunion ancient people pursued. Of course, it also reflects the characteristics of hakka people, such as hospitality, (when encountering a Hakka visitor from afar, we would warmly say "Come in and have a cup of tea." (Hakka dialect)), solidarity (when encountering difficulties with neighbors, we would take the initiative to say " Wait a minute, let me help you" （Hakka dialect）), respect for the elderly and care for the young, being sensible, diligent, capable and so on. “围龙屋”作为客家建筑，随着社会发展，逐渐被高楼大厦取代。 作为一种客家文化，梅州正以“客家围龙屋”申报世界文化遗产。其 伸报，对于提高梅州文化软实力具有重大意义，也是尊重文化多样性 的表现。客家围龙屋，给浓厚的中华文化增添了浓厚的色彩。 As a Hakka architecture, "Hakka Dragon House "was gradually replaced by high-rise buildings with the development of the society. At the same time, as a symbol of Hakka culture, Meizhou is launching the "Hakka Dragon House" declaration for world cultural heritage. It is of great significance to improve the cultural soft power of Meizhou and also shows respect for cultural diversity. The Hakka dragon house has added a strong color to the profound Chinese culture. 编译李灯辉陈靖熙谭泽榆</p>

<p><strong>6 开平灰雕---碉楼上永不凋零的花朵</strong></p>

<p><strong>Kaiping Grey Carving—The Flower that Never Withers on the</strong></p>

<p>Kaiping Grey Carving—The Flower that Never Withers on the Watchtowers 开平灰雕源于清代中叶，已经有将近三百年的历史，首先出现在 建筑讲究的礼堂，庙宇的墙上，作为一种寓意吉祥的装饰物。后来， 随着开平乡村中大批用砂质青砖建造民居的出现，人们将灰雕工艺广 泛地运用于墙上装饰，灰雕也因此成为了民间建房中的一项必备的工 序。 Kaiping Grey Carving originated from the middle of the Qing Dynasty （1728-1820）and have a history of about three hundred years. They first appeared on the walls of architecturally exquisite auditoriums and temples as a kind of decorative object implying auspiciousness. Afterwards, with the appearance of a large number of residential houses built with arenous grey bricks (a kind of stone fired from clay and used for building houses) in Kaiping villages, the technology of Grey Carving was widely used for decoration on residents’ walls and Grey Carving became a necessary procedure in the construction of folk houses. 灰雕又称“灰批”，以经过特别处理的石灰作为主料，用批刀直 接雕贴于墙上或者檐下，干结以后形成的各种图案，如山水、雀鸟、 花草人物画等，具有浮雕的艺术效果。它有操作易，耐久存等特点， 常用于檐宇，楼堂，房屋的装饰中。 Grey Carving is also called “grey modifications”. The raw material for creating Grey Carving is mainly lime. The craftman will affix the basic model to the wall or the eaves and refine it with a carving knife. Various patterns such as landscape, bird, and plant paintings, and, portraits of human beings, etc. can be seen after the the Grey Carving gets dry, which can present the effect of embossment art. It is often used in the decoration of eaves, halls and houses because it has some unique characteristics, like being easy to operate and durable. 因灰雕材料以石灰为主，又经过特别处理，所以具有耐酸、耐碱、 耐高温等特点，适应岭南潮湿、炎热及多雷雨、台风侵袭的自然气候。 至今，在开平的乡村中，不少的灰雕经历了百年风霜，依然屹立，其 工艺精巧，经历了时间的考验。而在碉楼的装饰上，灰雕一般用于外 墙立面，室内则多用于门楣、神位、天花等装饰。</p>

<p>Because the material of Grey Carving is mainly lime, after special treatment, it has the characteristics of acid resistance, alkali resistance and high temperature resistance and can adapt to Lingnan’s damp, hot, thundery and typhoon climate. So far, in Kaiping’s villages, a lot of Grey Carving survived after they had experienced one hundred years of wind and frost and they were so exquisitely made that they successfully passed the test of time. On the decoration of the watchtowers (a special type of Chinese residential building and it is named for its shape like a pillbox), Grey Carving is generally used on the exterior walls , while on the interior, they are mostly used for lintels, shrines, ceilings and other decorations. 开平灰雕题材广泛，通俗易懂。图案一般以吉祥意义为主，如猴 子对球、双凤朝阳、鸟语花香、八仙过海、福禄寿三仙献瑞等。后来， 随着华侨从海外带回了新的建筑材料和图案，传统的开平灰雕工艺融 入了西方绘画的元素和用料，如用红毛泥（水泥）混合石灰使灰雕更 坚固而圆滑。在内容上增加了西方题材，如巴洛克风格的山花图案， 当时的新兴事物火车、轮船、高楼大厦等，形成了中西结合的侨乡特 色。 Kaiping Grey Carving has a wide range of themes and are easy to understand. The patterns are generally based on auspicious meanings, such as monkeys on the ball, two phoenixes flying to the sun, birds singing and flowers radiating their fragrance, the eight immortals crossing the sea, and the three immortals of fortune, prosperity and longevity offering auspicious fortune. Afterwards, as the overseas Chinese brought back new building patterns and materials, traditional Kaiping Grey Carving technique became integrated with western painting elements and materials. For example, lime was mixed with cement to make the Grey Carving stronger and</p>

<p>smoother. Moreover, western themes were added to the content, such as the baroque style of mountain flowers, the new things of that time like trains、ships、skyscrapers and so on, forming the architectural characteristics of the hometown of overseas Chinese by combining Chinese and Western styles. 开平灰雕的制作首先是将石灰用水泡成灰浆，将干稻草剪碎成 段。然后将稻草段用石灰浆一层层浸泡，制成“草筋灰”。后加上水 泥、沙，用作灰雕的底部用料。其次得制作“纸筋灰”，将草根灰浸 泡20 天左右，打磨成浆后加入糯米粉、红糖等材料，混合便成“纸 筋灰”，用作灰雕的表层材料。如果需着色，就在“纸筋灰”中加入 矿物颜料。灰雕的材料制作好以后，必须在墙壁上进行施工。匠人需 根据图案的造型需要，在墙上用钢钉、铜线作筋线做坯，再用草筋灰 一层一层指引，最后用纸筋灰做成灰雕图案的表层，经过细致的批修， 栩栩如生的浮雕便呈现眼前。 The procedure of creating Kaiping Grey Carving is as follows: First, soak the lime into mortar and then cut the dry straw into sections. Then, soak the straw sections in lime slurry layer by layer to make “grass gluten ash”. Further then, add cement and sand to be used as the bottom material for the grey sculptures. Next, we have to make “paper bar ash”, soak the root ash for about 20 days, grind it into pulp, add materials such as glutinous rice flour and brown sugar, and mix it into “paper bar ash”, which will be used as the surface material of Grey Carving. If the Grey Carving needs to be colored, mineral pigment will be added into “paper bar ash”.After the material for the Grey Carving is ready, it must be constructed on walls. According to the pattern and the modeling, the craftsman needs to use steel nails and copper wire to make the base on the wall, and then cover the layers with grass gluten ash, and finally, make the top layer of Grey Carving’s pattern with paper bar ash. After carefully repair, a lifelike relief will come into view.</p>

<p>灰雕工艺，不仅注重图案的形式美，还重视图案的意义美，作品 既神情兼备，雅致多彩，又风格独特，饱含深意，反映人们对美好生 活的追求和祈求吉祥纳福的愿景。绚烂多姿的灰雕之于形态各异的开 平碉楼，是不可或缺的一部分。 Grey Carving not only places attention on the form-beauty, but also attaches importance to the significance-beauty. The works are not only full of expression, elegance and variety, but also unique in style and contain deep meanings, reflecting that people want to pursue a better life and pray for an auspicious life. The gorgeous Grey Carving is an indispensable part of Kaiping watchtower with various styles. 开平灰雕是开平乡村一种比较独特的民间艺术，在开平民间基本 上都有这种精美的雕塑。但这种民间艺术随着时代的发展，已经逐步 濒临失传的状态，人们可能知之甚少。特别是新建筑材料的出现，强 烈地冲击了灰雕这种传统的建筑风格和建筑特色。但是作为一种非物 质文化遗产，灰雕是开平民间不可多得的一种艺术精品。 Kaiping Grey Carving is an unique folk art in Kaiping villages. There are always such exquisite sculptures in the rural area of Kaiping. However, with the development of achitecture in the present era, this folk art has been on the verge of extinction, and has became rarely known. Especially, when the new building materials appeared, the traditional architectural style and building characteristics of Grey Carving has been strongly impacted . However, as a kind of intangible cultural heritage, Grey Carving is a rare fine work of folk art in Kaiping. 编译江锦菊关锦萍曹畅峰</p>

<p><strong>7 潮州牌坊</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chaozhou Paifang</strong></p>

<p>Chaozhou Paifang 牌坊又名牌楼。最早的文化起源可以追溯到周朝。在中国的许多 地区都遍布着牌坊的身影，但位于潮州的牌坊却是其中最为独特的。 其他地区的牌坊多零零散散分布各地，可是在潮州人们将牌坊聚集在 一条街道上，现存的22 座高大精美的牌坊鳞次栉比，风格独特，形 成了中国最大规模的古牌坊街。牌坊街也成为潮州一道独一无二的景 观，被誉为“天下第一牌坊街”。 Paifang, also known as Pailou, refers to the Chinese memorial archway. Its earliest cultural origin can be traced back to the Zhou Dynasty. Archways are found in many areas of China, but the archways in Chaozhou are the most unique among them. Archways in other areas are mostly scattered, but in Chaozhou they have been gathered on one street. In Chaozhou, the existing 22 tall and exquisite archways are lined up with unique styles, forming the largest ancient archway street in China. Paifang Street has also become a unique landscape in Chaozhou, known as the "First Paifang Street in the World". 尽管牌坊街上牌坊的数量众多，但是牌坊背后所蕴含的意义却不 容小觑。牌坊用于旌表，是出于对科举表现突出或者是为国家建功立 业的人进行表彰并加以奖赏。因此，牌坊街的牌坊分为两大类，一种 是科举类牌坊，另一种是宦绩坊。</p>

<p>There are a large number of archways on Paifang Street, each containing extraordinary meaning. The archways were used for ceremonies to commend and reward people who performed outstandingly in the imperial examinations or contributed to the country. Therefore, the archways on Paifang Street are divided into two categories: imperial examination and official contribution. 牌坊街上的牌坊多数兴建于明清时期。尤其是在嘉靖和乾隆两 朝，牌坊的兴建频率最高，平均三年就建立一座牌坊。这表明当时的 潮州不仅修建牌坊的风气兴盛，而且人才辈出。牌坊是身份的象征， 也是经济发展的指标。原因有以下两点： Most of the archways on Paifang Street were built during the Ming and Qing Dynasties. Especially in the Jiajing and Qianlong dynasties, the frequency of building archways was the highest, with one archway being built every three years on average. This shows that Chaozhou at that time was not only keen on building archways, but also had a large number of talents. The archway is a symbol of status and an indicator of economic development. There are two reasons: 在当时牌坊的修建也是有其限制条件的，其一是受封牌坊的人的 身份不能是一个白丁。他需要获得进士以上的身份，才能够由地方官 员上报朝廷，在得到皇帝批准后才可建立牌坊。其二是建立者要具备 足够的经济实力。修建牌坊的资金大部分由受封者自己出资，官府只 出三十两白银。由此可见，当时人们是具有一定的经济基础去负担一 座牌坊的修建。否则，也无法平均三年就出现一座新的牌坊。 At that time, there were limitations for building archways. First, the identity of the person authorized to build the archway cannot be an ordinary person without scholarly honor. He needs to obtain the status of Jinshi or above in order to be reported to the court by local officials, and only after the emperor's approval can he establish a memorial arch. The second is that it requires sufficient economic power. Most of the funds for building archways were funded by the recipients themselves, and the government only provided thirty taels of silver. It can be seen that people at that time had a certain economic foundation to afford the construction of an archway. Otherwise, a new archway would not appear in an average of three years. 每一座牌坊的背后就有一个故事。这些故事讲述了潮州先人的各 种优秀事迹。可以说，牌坊传承了潮州一代又一代的文化精神。从牌 坊的名称中我们就可以了解潮州曾经的历史。“四进士坊”“五贤” “六贤”“七俊”等都说明在某一时期潮州人才济济，金榜题名的人 不在少数。如今的潮州虽已没落，可那22 座牌坊背后的每一位英杰</p>

<p>的故事却没有为人所遗忘。现在的牌坊街在人们的努力下，不仅具有 历史情怀且焕发出现代商业的光彩。 There is a story behind every archway. These stories tell the excellent deeds of the Chaozhou ancestors. It can be said that Chaozhou people have inherited the cultural spirit of Chaozhou from generation to generation with the archway. We can understand the history of Chaozhou from the name of the archway. For example, "Four Jinshi Archway", "Five Sages", "Six Sages", "Seven Talents", etc. all show that in a certain period of time, Chaozhou had a large number of talents, many of whom had passed imperial examination. Although Chaozhou is now in decline, the story of every hero behind the 22 memorial archways has not been forgotten. With the efforts of people, the current Paifang Street not only has historical sentiments but also has achieved vigorous development in modern commerce. 每一座牌坊都是光宗耀祖的象征，是流芳百世的荣誉。于是在人 们的重视下，兴建而成的每一座牌坊都是集书法、雕刻、建筑于一体 的艺术品。牌坊正反两面都有额刻和对联，并且都是由书法大家书写 而成。在游玩牌坊街时，也能欣赏到中国特有的文化艺术。除此之外， 我们还可以从牌坊中感受到浓厚的人文气息和历史底蕴。比如，四进 士坊是为了四位品性高洁，有优越政绩的进士修建的。可见，牌坊不 仅凝聚着艺术的精华还代表着潮州的人文关怀。 Each archway represents the eternal honor to make the ancestors illustrious. Due to the high attention of people, every archway built is a work of art that integrates calligraphy, sculpture and architecture. There are engravings and couplets on both sides of the archway, which are all written by calligraphers. When visiting Paifang Street, you can appreciate the unique Chinese culture and art and also feel the strong cultural atmosphere and historical heritage from the archway. For example, the Four Jinshi Archway was built for four Jinshi with noble character and superior political achievements. It can be seen that the archway not only embodies the essence of art, but also represents the humanistic care of Chaozhou. 牌坊是潮州建筑史上的一颗闪耀的明珠。然而在潮州，牌坊并不 仅是一种建筑，它还代表着一种文化，一种传承和一种纪念。 The archway is a shining pearl in the architectural history of Chaozhou. However, the archway in Chaozhou is not only a kind of architecture, it also represents a kind of culture, inheritance and commemoration. 编译曾晓钰</p>

<p><strong>8 东莞六一一亭</strong></p>

<p><strong>Liuyi Pavilion, Dongguan</strong></p>

<p>Liuyi Pavilion, Dongguan 在东莞道滘的闸口村，有处名为国殇冢的地方，又名六一一亭， 1949 年2 月24 日落成，以纪念被日军用毒烟熏死的61 位村民。每 年清明前后、农历六月十一日，均有村民、学生前去祭祀。 In the Zhakou Village of Daojiao, Dongguan City, there is a national martyr tomb, also known as Liuyiyi Pavilion. It was built on February 24, 1949 to commemorate the 61 villagers who haid died of poisonous smoke by the Japanese army. Every year around the Qingming Festival and on the 11th, June of the lunar calendar, villagers and students go to worship the departed. 国殇冢原址是清末一户卢氏的人家住宅。1941 年农历闰六月十 一日，日军第二次报复屠村，将村民困入卢氏住宅内，释放毒烟，造 成61 人死亡。抗战胜利后，村民不忘先烈，在原宅地以红砖水泥批 荡成园林式亭冢。六一一亭，宽8.6 米、长20 米，内分前门、天井、 主亭、后冢4 个部分。四周建有护墙，墙内壁镶有19 块当时广东省 国民党军政政要员题刻的碑刻。国殇冢是日军侵华暴行的重要见证之 一，更是爱国主义教育基地。每年清明节、道滘镇中心小学都会组织 师生扫墓，进行爱国主义教育。1982 年和1988 年道滘镇政府两次拨 款重修。2002 年被列为广东省文物保护单位。 The original site of the National Martyr Tomb was the residence of a Lu family in the late Qing Dynasty. On the 11th day of June of lunar calendar in 1941, the Japanese army retaliated to conducting a slaughter for the second time, by trapping villagers into Lu's house, releasing poisonous smoke, and killing 61 people. After the victory of the Anti-Japanese War, the villagers did not forget the martyrs, and the original houses made of red brick and cement was built into a garden-style pavilion. The Liuyiyi Pavilion is 8.6 meters wide and 20 meters long, which is divided into four parts: the front door, the patio, the main pavilion, and the back tomb. The curtain wall stands around the site with 19 stone inscriptions inscribed by the Kuomintang military and political officials at the time inside the wall. The Tomb is one of the important evidences witnessing atrocities committed by the Japanese army in China, and it is also a patriotic education base. During annual Qingming(Tomb Sweeping) Festival, Daojiao Town Central Primary School organizes teachers and students to visit the graves and conduct patriotic education. In 1982 and 1988, the Daojiao Town Government allocated funds for reconstruction. In 2002, it was listed as a cultural relics protection site in Guangdong Province.</p>

<p>从远处望去，国殇冢大门紧挨着车水马龙的道滘沿江大道，周边 都是高低错落的居民房。大门柱为浅灰色碎石批荡，左右各四根，构 成一个整体。院落的格局呈中轴对称结构，通道两边植有冬青和矮松， 抬头看去即是六一一亭，视线尽头是绿色琉璃瓦覆顶的碑廊，正中央 是小篆体的“国殇冢”。亭子正上方悬挂着抗日名将由蒋光鼐题写的 匾额——六一一亭，左右楹联“碧血常新精魂不灭，大江如画烈魂归 来”，为北伐战争时期国民革命第五军军长李福林所题。匾额和楹联 均为白色大理石镂刻，笔画填以蓝色。 From a distance, the gate of the Tomb is next to the busy road along the Yangtze River, and is surrounded by residential houses. The gate pillars are made of light gray gravel, with four on the left and right each in total. The layout of the courtyard is axially symmetrical, with holly and dwarf pine planted on both sides of the middle passage. Straight ahead is Liuyiyi Pavilion. At the end of eyesight is a stele corridor covered with green glazed tiles, and in the center are small seal-shaped Chinese characters of "National Martyr Tomb". Hanging directly above the pavilion is a plaque inscribed by Jiang Guangnai, a famous anti-Japanese general — the Liuyiyi Pavilion. The left and right couplets are "Hero’s blood is always new and the soul is immortal, and the river is like a picture of the return of the fierce soul." It was made by Li Fulin, commander of the Fifth Army of the National Revolution during the Northern Expedition. The plaques and couplets are carved in white marble, and the strokes are filled with blue. 在略显简陋寒酸的国殇冢，最大的亮点莫过于亭上及碑廊、内墙 的19 块碑匾。道滘文化名人莫闲斋先生将碑文内容归纳为四组：一 为“民族正气”“民族精魂”“义烈乡邦”“义民堪敬”；二为“义 气长存”“毅魂常存”“英魂不灭”“永昭馨烈”；三为“精忠昭日 月”“大义凛然”“义薄云天”；四为“行已有耻”“宁死不屈”“临</p>

<p>危不苟”“成仁取义”。内容从传统道德的角度表达对死者“忠义节 烈”的肯定。而民国时任东莞县长何峨芳亲自着笔的《济川国殇之碑》 上，更有“匹夫匹妇忠义节烈行可歌可泣”等语句。 In the slightly humble National Martyr Tomb, the biggest light spot is the 19 tablets on the pavilion, the corridor of the stele, and the inner wall. Daojiao cultural celebrity, Mr. Mo Xianzhai, summarized the content of the inscriptions into four groups: one is "national righteousness", "national spirit", "righteous township", "righteous people are respectable"; the other is "justice lasts forever" and "permanent soul Existence", "Heroic soul will not die", "always lead to the great achievement"; three are "honest and loyal to the sun and moon", "great righteousness", "justice is on the top"; the fourth is "stick to sense of shame", " rather die than surrender", "do not succumb to danger", and "sacrifice to achieve justice" . The contents express the affirmation of the deceased's "loyalty and integrity" from the perspective of traditional morality. In the Republic of China, Dongguan County Magistrate He Efang personally wrote the "Stele of Jichuan National Memorial" together with "The loyalty and dignity of the passed people worth our admiring and following". 暮色渐沉，国殇冢静默在一隅，默默地注视着水乡的发展。一段 历史不仅仅是一个故事，更是东莞重要的城市记忆，它揭开历史的创 痕，只为唤起每个人对和平的珍视，谨此缅怀受难的同胞。 As the dusk gradually sinks, National Martyr Tomb is in the corner, silently watching the development of the water town. A piece of history is not only a story, but also an important city memory in Dongguan. It uncovers the scars of history, only to arouse everyone's cherishing of peace, and hereby valuing the memory of the suffering compatriots. 编译陈晴扬叶育彤王雪芸</p>

<p><strong>9 冯如故居纪念馆</strong></p>

<p><strong>Deng Ru's Former Residence and Memorial Hall</strong></p>

<p>Deng Ru's Former Residence and Memorial Hall 冯如故居及冯如纪念馆位于广东省恩平市牛江镇莲塘村。据村民 介绍，该村可溯源至公元1471 年冯氏先祖从仕洞村迁入此地定居之 时；村里1000 户人家均为冯姓。该村最著名的景点正是冯如故居及 纪念楼。 Feng Ru's former residence and Memorial Hall are located in Liantang Village, Niujiang Town, Enping City, Guangdong Province. According to villagers, the village can be traced back to when the ancestors of the Feng family moved from Shidong Village to settle here in 1471 AD; 1,000 households in the village all have the surname Feng. The most famous attraction of the village is Feng Ru's former residence and memorial hall. 冯如生于1884 年1 月12 日，原名冯九如，字鼎三，是中国第一 位飞机设计师、制造师和飞行家，被誉为“中国航空之父”。自幼聪 颖，富有创新精神，爱琢磨自制一些不同的小玩具，深得邻里赞赏。 Feng Ru was born on January 12, 1884, formerly known as Feng Jiuru, styled himself “Ding San”. He was the first aircraft designer of China, manufacturer and pilot, and was known as the "father of Chinese aviation." He was smart and innovative since he was a child, and he loved to make some different small toys, which was appreciated by the neighborhood. 1894 年，冯如父亲去世，于是他随亲戚到旧金山初当机械学徒。 1906 年，在旅美华侨的支持下创办了“广东制造机器工厂”开始研 究制造飞机。1909 年9 月制成第一架可载人动力飞机；1911 年1 月 在奥克兰驾驶经七次改进的双翼飞机进行表演，中山先生到现场观看 后称赞他说：“吾国大有人矣。”1911 年2 月，冯如谢绝美国人重 金聘用，将制造飞机的器材、设备和制成的飞机带回国内。辛亥革命 后接受任命成为中华民国军政府广东革命军飞机长。1912 年8 月冯 如在广州飞行表演时不幸失事身亡，遗体后葬于广州市黄花岗七十二 烈士墓，广东军政府陆军司按少将阵亡例抚恤其遗属。 In 1894, Feng Ru's father died, so he followed his relatives to San Francisco as a mechanical apprentice. In 1906, with the support of overseas Chinese in the United States, he founded the "Guangdong Manufacturing Machinery Factory" and began to research and manufacture aircraft. In September 1909, the first manned-powered aircraft was built; in January 1911, he drove a seven-time improved biplane for a</p>

<p>performance in Auckland. Mr. Zhongshan praised him after watching the show: "There are many talents in our country." In February 1911, Feng Ru declined the request of the Americans to hire him with a large amount of money, and brought back home the equipment, materials and finished aircraft. After the Revolution of 1911, he accepted his appointment as the commander of the Guangdong Revolutionary Army of the Republic of China. In August 1912, Feng Ru was killed in a crash during a flight show in Guangzhou, and his body was buried in the Tomb of 72 Martyrs in Huanghuagang, Guangzhou. The Army Department of the Guangdong Military Government compensated his family dependants of the deceased according to the level standard of major general. 冯如把毕生精力都献给了祖国的航空事业。他是第一个驾驶飞机 上天的中国人、中国第一个飞机设计师兼制造师、第一个在中国国土 上用飞机演习的人、第一个在国际飞行大赛中获奖的中国人，他提出 的航空战略理论对中华民族航空事业和人民空军发展带来的深远影 响。 Feng Ru devoted all his life to the aviation industry of his motherland. He was the first Chinese to fly a plane to the sky, China’s first aircraft designer and manufacturer, the first person to exercise aircraft on Chinese soil, and the first Chinese to win an international flight competition. The proposed aviation strategy theory has a profound impact on the development of the Chinese nation’s aviation industry and the People’s Air Force. 冯如纪念楼或称冯如博物馆共有六层。第五层和第六层顶部为橙 黄仿古覆瓦飞檐设计，楼体外墙主色调为钴蓝色。该纪念楼主要作用 为展示冯如旧照、书信以及中外报刊对他的报道内容，最顶层还曾陈</p>

<p>列有用于表达对冯如敬意的飞机。冯如故居建于清代，是一间南北向 的砖木结构的典型的三间二廊的旧式平房。外墙单砖和砂夯土墙墙 基，内墙为泥砖，俗称“金包银”结构。其总建筑面积52 平方米。 故居大厅里陈列着冯如画像、他设计制造的各式飞机模型和他驾驶飞 机的旧照，厅前有一口排水天井。在大厅旁边的卧室里，完好的保留 着冯如当年的结婚用品。 The Feng Ru Memorial Building or Feng Ru Museum has six floors. The tops of the fifth and sixth floors are designed with orange and yellow antique tile-clad cornices, and the main color of the outer wall of the building is cobalt blue. The main function of the memorial building is to display Feng Ru’s old photos, letters, and the content of reports on him by Chinese and foreign newspapers. The top floor also displays an airplane used to express respect to Feng Ru. The former residence of Feng Ru was built in the Qing Dynasty. It is a typical old-style bungalow with three rooms and two corridors with a north-south brick-wood structure. The outer wall is single brick and sand rammed earth wall base, and the inner wall is mud brick, commonly known as "golden-silver" structure. Its total construction area is 52 square meters. In the hall of the former residence, the portrait of Feng Ru, various airplane models designed and manufactured by him, and old photos of his flying airplanes are displayed, and there is a drainage patio in front of the hall. In the bedroom next to the hall, Feng Ru’s wedding supplies were kept intact. 冯如故居及纪念馆不仅蕴含了丰富的人文精神，也是恩平一处重 要的旅游景点。冯如生平的种种事迹和其中所蕴含的自强精神更是对 恩平的发展有着深远而不可磨灭的影响。1983 年6 月，基于重要的 历史价值和其浓厚的人文气息，恩平县人民政府将其核定为县级文物 保护单位；2012 年，冯如故居更被列入到广东省第七批文物保护单</p>

<p>位中。将来如若能把宣传和认识这两块短板补齐，冯如故居和纪念楼 必将有一个更加明朗可期的未来。 Feng Ru’s former residence and memorial hall not only contain rich humanistic spirit, but also an important tourist attraction in Enping, Guangdong. The various deeds of Feng Ru’s life and the self-improvement spirit contained in it have a profound and indelible influence on Enping’s development. In June 1983, based on its important historical value and strong cultural atmosphere, the Enping County People’s Government approved it as a county-level cultural relic protection site. In 2012, Feng Ru’s former residence was included in the seventh batch of cultural relics protection in Guangdong Province. In the future, if both publicity and popularity can be enhanced, Feng Ru’s former residence and memorial building will have a brighter prospect. 编译钟剑豪</p>

