<h2>四、民间美食与文化</h2>

<p><strong>1 潮汕风味小吃——鼠壳粿</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chaoshan Flavor Snacks——Gnaphalium Cake</strong></p>

<p>Chaoshan Flavor Snacks——Gnaphalium Cake 鼠壳粿，是潮汕地区的传统小吃之一，属于潮汕菜系。因为制作 鼠壳粿的材料要在冬天才能采摘，所以一般是在潮汕民间年节祭祖的 时候才有。 Gnaphalium Cake is one of the traditional snacks in Chaoshan area, which belongs to Chaoshan cuisine. Because the materials for making Gnaphalium Cake can only be picked in winter, Gnaphalium Cake is usually available when Chaoshan people worship their ancestors during New Year Festival. 相传南宋末年，元兵入侵潮汕地区，当时到处兵荒马乱，百姓流 离失所，缺衣少食，只能用野菜充饥。老百姓无意中发现一种野草， 叫做“鼠壳草”，既能充饥，还有特殊的香味，最重要的是没有毒性， 便把它采来做成食物填饱肚子。后来发现这种野草可以和大米一起磨 成米浆做成粿，便称为“鼠壳粿”。之后，人们就把摘来的青草晒干， 储藏起来，逢年过节时，随时都可以使用。后来这种食物经过民间的 逐步改进，把原来使用大米制作而成的粿皮改为使用糯米，这样做出 来的粿皮比较柔软；再把馅料从原来用番薯和红糖，改为用绿豆沙， 有的是用红豆沙，还有的是用炒熟的花生仁再加上白砂糖碾碎作馅。 这一改进使得粿皮柔软而且不会苦涩，馅料甜香，也就成为潮汕的一 种名小吃。现在这小吃从民间的一般食品登上大雅之堂，在各大餐馆、 酒店都有制作。 It is said that at the end of the Southern Song Dynasty, the yuan Dynasty’s soldiers invaded Chaoshan area. At that time, there were many places at war, people were displaced, and they were lacking in food and clothing. They could only use wild vegetables to fill the belly. One day, someone found a kind of weeds, called “Gnaphalium”, which can satisfy their hunger and has a special flagrance. The most important thing is that it is not poisonous, so they pick it to make food to fill their stomachs. Later, it was found that this weed can be ground with rice into rice milk to make cake, which is called " Gnaphalium Cake". Afterwards, people will pick the weed and dry it in the sun to store it up, and then people can use it for every festival. Later, this kind of food was gradually improved by the folk. The original material was replaced by glutinous rice, which made the cake soft. Then, the stuffing was changed from sweet potato and brown sugar to mung bean, red bean, and also ground fried peanut plus white sugar. This improvement makes the cake soft and not bitter, the filling sweet, making it a famous snack in Chaoshan. Now, this snack is not only an</p>

<p>ordinary folk food but also has been made a special cuisine in restaurants and hotels. 潮汕人很早就了解到属于“鼠壳草”的一种特有的甘香味，还有 它本身具有的药效。因此用它作为原料，制成各种小吃。这一点，在 古代一些文献中已经有了记载。如明代李时珍的《本草纲目》中提到： “北方寒食采茸母草和粉食”。这可以看出人们用鼠壳草制作成粿的 习俗，已经有很长的历史了。 Chaoshan people have known for a long time that the " Gnaphalium " has a unique sweet taste and some medical use. Therefore, it is used as raw material to make various snacks. This has been recorded in some ancient documents. For example, in the Compendium of Materia Medica written by Li Shizhen of the Ming Dynasty, it is also mentioned that "for making the cold food in the north, people mixed Gnaphalium with flour to eat". It can be seen here that people’s making cake with Gnaphalium has a long history. 鼠壳粿的制作过程其实挺简单的。把采摘来的鼠壳草，清洗干净， 放进一个干净的大锅里，再加入一定量的清水，把鼠壳粿煮的熟透， 然后捞起来放进清水中，浸泡两三天，去除掉鼠壳草的苦涩味，接着 捞起来沥干水分，放入臼中捶成棉絮状；接着在捣好的鼠壳草里加入 食用油，然后再把它倒入糯米粉中，把鼠壳草和糯米粉揉成面团状。 随便抓取大小适中的一个面团，捏成碗形，包入馅料，放入“粿印” （做粿时用的模子）中用手挤压成形，放在铺有香蕉叶的蒸笼上，放</p>

<p>入锅中蒸熟。拿出蒸笼后用剪刀将鼠壳粿一个一个剪下。吃的时候撕 去香蕉叶就可以了。趁热吃的时候口感软糯，有种入口即化的感觉； 凉了之后把它用油煎成两面酥脆，也是一种不错的吃法。 The process of making Gnaphalium Cake is very simple: pick the Gnaphalium and wash it, put it into a clean pot, add a certain amount of water, cook the Gnaphalium thoroughly, and then take it out and put it in water, soak it for two or three days to remove the bitterness of Gnaphalium, and then dry it in the sun, put it into the mortar and beat it into cotton wadding; then add edible oil into the rammed Gnaphalium, and then put it into the glutinous flour, knead the Gnaphalium and glutinous rice flour into a dough. Grab a dough of moderate size, knead it into a bowl, wrap it with stuffing, put it into "cake mold" (the mold used for making cake), squeeze it into the shape by hand, put it on the steamer with banana leaves at the bottom, and steam it in the pot. Take out the steamer and cut off the cake with the banana leave one by one with scissors. Just tear off the banana leaves when you eat. When it's hot, the Gnaphalium Cake is soft, and you may feel like that it is melting in the mouth. When it's cold, we can fry it till it becomes crispy, which is also a good way to eat it. 在我们那里，鼠壳粿只有在过年的时候家家户户才会做。当妈妈 开始准备做鼠壳粿的时候我就知道是年节临近，鼠壳粿已经不单是一 种食品，它也代表着对在外奔波的亲子们的一种想念，想念着家想念 着亲人！想念着幸福！ For us Chaoshan people, Gnaphalium Cake is only made at the Spring Festival. When my mother begins to prepare to make Gnaphalium Cake, I know that it is the New Year's Day approaching. Gnaphalium Cake is not only a kind of food, but also a symbol of parents’ missing their distant children, children’s missing their distant families and also all people’s longing to share happiness with their loved ones. 编译林佳浼</p>

<p><strong>2 客家美食—牛筋糕</strong></p>

<p><strong>Hakka Food--Beef Tendon Cakes</strong></p>

<p>Hakka Food--Beef Tendon Cakes 牛筋糕来源于广东省河源市龙川县，至今已有300 余年的制作历 史。它是客家糕点类美食，更是龙川文化的一个特色标志。1985 年 牛筋糕获得了广东省糕点优质奖。多年来，牛筋糕以不变的初心与味 道，受到了大家的喜爱，产品远近驰名，远销海外。 Beef Tendon Cakes come from Longchuan, Heyuan City, Guangdong Province and have a history of over 300 years. Beef Tendon Cakes are not only Hakka food but also a characteristic symbol of Longchuan culture. In 1985, Beef Tendon Cakes won the Guangdong Cake Quality Award. Beef Tendon Cakes have been stayed true to its original recipe for years, which is loved by its customers. These cakes have become well-known and have been sold all over the world. 自清朝时起便有了牛筋糕。因用糯米粉制作出来的糕点又黄又 韧，很像牛筋，因而取名为牛筋糕。起初，他们主要是通过沿街售卖， 以推销他们的商品，渐渐地牛筋糕受到了顾客的喜爱，而后才慢慢的 发展起来。到现在，牛筋糕已成为河源人过节送礼必不可缺的手礼。 Beef Tendon Cakes originated in Qing Dynasty. They are made from glutinous rice flour and are yellow and tough. These cakes are appropriately named because they taste like beef tendon. At first, the cakes were sold in the streets. Gradually, they were loved by customers and the business grew well. Until now, Beef Tendon Cakes have become an indispensable gift for people in Heyuan to celebrate a festival.</p>

<p>关于牛筋糕还有这样一个传说。从前，有个喜欢玩魔术的人转行 做糕点生意，为了招徕顾客，他赶着一头大水牛上街，自已腰间持了 一个小布袋，便沿街大声叫卖“牛筋糕”。街上很多人都好奇地围上 来，看到底什么是牛筋糕。当有人要向他买牛筋糕时，他便从牛肋下 拉出一条长长的“牛筋”来，交付给顾客。他这奇妙的一手，人们都 看得目瞪口呆。那些买了牛筋糕的人，也不知这些糕点是真是假，便 把它一截截掐出来，分给众人吃。众人吃了，无不啧啧称赞，都说这 牛筋糕香腻清甜，软而不粘，爽而不脆，别有风味。 There is a story behind Beef Tendon Cakes. Once upon a time there was a man who loved magic but changed his career to sell cakes. In order to drum up customers he took a big buffalo to a bazaar. He secretly tied a small cloth bag around his waist. “Beef Tendon Cakes” then he shouted loudly in the streets. In a instant, his shout attracted many passers-by, who gathered curiously to wonder what were Beef Tendon Cakes. When people wanted to buy Beef Tendon Cakes, the vendor tricked them into believing that he pulled out a long strip of beef tendon from the rib of his buffalo. The vendor then handed beef tendons in the customers. The vendor’s mysterious act stupefied all of the passers-by. At the same time the customers who bought cakes didn’t know whether they were real tendons or not and tore the food into pieces and gave them away to other passers-by to taste. All of the passers-by praised these cakes for their fresh and sweet flavour. Gradually, Beef Tendon Cakes became famous at the bazaar. 多年来牛筋糕一直沿用传统的制作方法，原材料简单易取，主要 包括糯米粉、白砂糖、植物油等。牛津糕保质期相对较短，为保证其</p>

<p>硬而不腻，软而不烂的新鲜口感，工艺人在生产过程中摒弃了传统的 大工业生产，拒绝添加任何食品添加剂，力求让牛筋糕保留食品最为 纯真的风味。到如今，市场上渐渐衍生出另一种风味的牛筋糕—芝麻 牛筋糕，即在牛津糕的表面撒上芝麻。芝麻主要分为黑芝麻，白芝麻 两种。粘上了芝麻的牛筋糕，似乎也被赋予了新的生命，带了种芝麻 味的淡淡清香，得到了大众的喜爱与认可。 For years the cake makers have been following the traditional recipe. The raw materials are easy to get, including glutinous rice flour, white granulated sugar ,vegetable oil and so on. This cake has a relatively short shelf life. In order to ensure that Beef Tendon Cakes are hard but not greasy, soft but not too tender, cake makers abandoned traditional mass industrial production and refuse to add any food additives so as to do their best to retain the purest flavor. Nowadays, Beef Tendon Cakes with sesame seeds have been introduced to the market gradually. Black or white sesame seeds are put on the top of the food. It seems that Beef Tendon Cakes with sesame seeds are given a new lease of life and the faint scent is popular with it customers. 龙川牛筋糕既是河源市市级的非物质文化遗产，又是龙川人心中 独具特色的客家美食。我们欢迎您来龙川旅游，游览赵佗文化遗址， 品尝客家美食牛筋糕，我想这趟旅程定能让你不负所望。 Longchuan Beef Tendon Cakes are not only the intangible cultural heritage in Heyuan but also the unique Hakka food in Longchuan people’ mind. In your spare time you will be welcomed to Longchuan. Here you can visit Zhaotuo cultural relic and taste Hakka food, Beef Tendon Cakes, and you will not be disappointed. 编译黄家梅</p>

<p><strong>3 金酥油糍</strong></p>

<p><strong>Golden Cakes</strong></p>

<p>Golden Cakes 在广西，逢年过节几乎大多数家庭都会亲手做金酥油糍。或许提 到这个名字，大家以为它和我们日常食用的糍粑一样，其实金酥油糍 却和糍粑大有不同。接下来我将为大家揭秘这一道客家美食。 In Guangxi the majority of families make lots of Golden Cakes during festivals. When you hear this food name, you may mistake it to be a glutinous rice cake. However, Golden Cakes are totally different from the former. In the next few paragraphs I’ll show you how to make Golden Cakes. 食材Ingredients 首先，准备适量的花生油和糯米粉。其次，准备等量的芝麻和花 生并且全部打碎，以确保馅料酥软。最后，准备芝麻及花生总用量一 半的白砂糖和融化好的黄糖，来保证油糍口感香甜。 Firstly, you need a proper amount of peanut oil and glutinous rice flour. Secondly, the same amount of sesame seeds and peanuts should be smashed so as to make the fillings soft. Thirdly, white granulated sugar is added, which weighs half of the sesame seeds and peanuts. Finally, brown melted sugar is prepared so that golden cakes are sweet. 做法Processes 第一步是和面，通过这一步骤，我们要将糯米粉和融化的黄糖充 分融合，最后要揉成一个淡黄色的面团。面团的软硬程度到大拇指可 以按下去，回轻轻恢复且不沾手最为适宜。 The first step: you need to mix the glutinous rice flour with the brown melted sugar to make a slightly yellow-colored dough. The dough should be hard so that you can press your fingers on it and the hole would disappear naturally and should not stick to your hands. 第二步是把白糖、芝麻碎及花生碎搅拌在一起，每次取适量的馅 包入巴掌大的面团里，形状包成橄榄状。在广西，这似乎是一种微妙 的统一，家家户户都会把油糍包成这样的形状，不大不小，刚好一次 的食用量。 The second step: you should stir the white granulated sugar with crushed sesame seeds and peanuts. The fillings should be covered by a palm-sized, olive-shaped piece of dough. In Guangxi, every family makes golden cakes into this olive shape, which seems a delicate consistent habit. The olive-shaped golden cakes are perfectly sized to satisfy a man’s hunger.</p>

<p>第三步是把花生油倒入锅里，升至九成热，然后一一把油糍放入 锅中油炸。每次放入的油糍数量不可太多，其个数刚好能够铺满油锅 的表面即可。放入油锅后，我们要时刻关注油糍的颜色变化，最初是 淡黄色，当油糍逐渐从锅底漂浮到油锅表面时，火要关小，保持油锅 的温度大致不变，这时我们要用筷子把油糍的正反面不停地翻动，使 其炸得均匀。一锅油糍炸5-6 分钟即可，当油糍变成金黄色，皮壳胀 发似球状，空气中弥漫着芝麻花生的香味，此时就可以沥出油捞出来 了。 The third step: you need to heat the peanut oil to just below boiling. After that, every golden cake should be fried in the hot oil. Remember that don’t put too many Golden Cakes in the pot and that the cakes can be just spread on the surface of the oil. After putting the cakes in the oil, you need to pay close attention to the changes of their color. Initially, they are light yellow. When the cakes begin to float to the surface, the heat should be turned down so as to retain almost the same temperature of the oil. At this time, you need to continuously turn over the cakes so they are evenly fried. A pot of cakes should be fried for five to six minutes. When the cakes turn golden yellow, each of them swells like a small ball and the scent of sesame seeds and peanuts fill the air, you could scoop out and drain off the oil on the cakes. 口感Taste 经过油炸之后，油糍色泽金黄、皮圆发亮、外表酥脆、内部柔软， 融化后的白糖、芝麻碎和花生碎一同挤入你的口中，不会太甜，也不 会起渣。口感软糯香甜，可口诱人，品尝一个之后你就只会想再多吃 几个，怎么都吃不够。 After being fried, the cakes are golden, round ans sparkling. When you bite it, you’ll feel that the outside is crisp but the inside is soft. In an instant, crushed sesame seeds and peanuts with melted sugar flow into your mouth. The texture is smooth and the taste is not too sweet and it’s delicious. Once you eat one, you want more. You just can’t get enough of it.</p>

<p>在我们老家有一种说法，吃油糍吃的并不是其本身，而是一种团 圆。逢年过节，亲戚走动，大家一起动手做金酥油糍，有说有笑，共 度佳节，其乐融融，最后再一起享受劳动的成果，真是这世上最简单 而纯粹的快乐了。 In our hometown, it’s said that it’s not eating Golden Cakes that is important. That is also the bringing together the community. During festivals, relatives visit each other and make Golden Cakes themselves, talking, laughing, celebrating festivals and last enjoying their food, which is the purest and simplest joy in the world. 编译温雅琪</p>

<p><strong>4 棉城美食——鲎粿</strong></p>

<p><strong>Miancheng Gourmet -- Limulus Kueh</strong></p>

<p>Miancheng Gourmet -- Limulus Kueh 棉城这座潮阳古邑，有着丰富的人文历史，有着数不尽的珍馐佳 肴。其中最令我喜爱的就是名不见经传的小食——鲎粿。 Miancheng is an old county in Chaoyang and it has a rich history and numerous delicious food. My favorite food is Limulus Kueh though it is little known. 鲎粿是著名的一款棉城的小食，具有悠久的历史。《潮阳县志》 载：“潮邑鲎粿乃粉粿中之精品，清康熙年间也以奉客。而粉粿则唐 乃有之。" 由此可见，从大约三百多年以前，鲎粿已是招呼奉客的佳 肴了。 Limulus Kueh is well known in Miancheng and it has a long history. According to Chaoyang County Annals, Chao County’s Limulus Kueh is the best one in Meal Kueh. During Kangxi Period, it was also served to guests. However, Meal Kueh appeared in Tang Dynasty. Based on this book, Limulus Kueh was served as an excellent cuisine nearly three hundred years ago. 除了包裹着各种鲜香的食材的粉糯的肠粉之外，鲎粿也是独属于 我的家乡棉城的地方特色了。鲎粿的制作和肠粉的制作也有着异曲同 工之妙，肠粉是用到米浆加入一些粉类调成糊状，在上蒸框里蒸时在 加入其他的馅料，比如加入肉糜、虾、香菇等等。而鲎粿的做法是将 磨成浆的稀饭加入木薯粉然后在和匀，然后取一部分面糊倒入特制形 状的鲎模具里，放入喜欢的食材，比如常见的组合就有肉糜、虾、鹌 鹑蛋和香菇，有些人还喜欢放入鱿鱼干。再倒入一些面糊填满模具， 就可以放上锅蒸。只是蒸熟之后的鲎粿比肠粉多了一道工序----炸。 将蒸熟的鲎粿下入油锅炸到表面酥脆，捞出沥干剪开表面，淋上酱油 和辣椒酱，一份美味酥香的鲎粿就出锅了。 Besides soft steamed vermicelli rolls, which are covered by different types of fresh ingredients, Limulus Kueh is also a regional speciality in my hometown. The way that steamed vermicelli rolls are made is almost the same as Limulus Kueh. The former is made of rice milk added by mushy flour and they are steamed in the steamer basket plus other fillings, such as meat paste, shrimps and mushrooms. However, Limulus Kueh is made of rice milk added by tapioca flour. Firstly, they should be kneaded evenly. Secondly, a proper amount of part of panada is put in a specially-made mould and the ingredients which you love can also be put in such as meat paste, shrimps, quail eggs and mushrooms. Also you can add some dried squids</p>

<p>if you like. Thirdly, the mould should be covered fully by the remaining panada. Fourthly it can be steamed on the pot. What differentiates Limulus Kueh and steamed vermicelli rolls is the frying process for the former. After steaming, Limulus Kueh should be put in the pot with heated oil until its outside is crisp. Fifthly, you could scoop out all of the Limulus Kueh and drain off the oil on it. Then, you could sprinkle soy and chilli sauce. Finally, delicious and crisp Limulus Kueh is ready. 鲎粿的表皮金黄酥脆，颜色不仅诱人，吧唧咬一口外酥里嫩，在 加上咸辣的酱料更是把鲎粿里头馅料的鲜香给发挥得淋漓尽致。鲎粿 是一年四季串上棉城的大街小巷都能买上的小食，不仅饱腹感强，而 且味道鲜美、层次丰富，很值得你来棉小城的时候品一品。 The color of Limulus Kueh is golden yellow and its outside is crisp. If you bite it, you’ll find the inside is soft and its fresh and delicious scent of the fillings emits perfectly with the help of soy and chilli sauce. Whenever you come to Miancheng, you can taste Limulus Kueh in the streets. This food can not only fill you up but also be fresh, delicious and rich-flavored. Limulus Kueh is highly worth tasting if you come to Miancheng. 关于鲎粿由来的传说有很多。有说是媳妇孝敬无牙婆婆而创制出 来的，有说是以鲎为食材做成潮汕特色的粿品，也有说是因为物质匮 乏，杀了鲎后，用鲎的血加入其他浆水材料制成的粿品。无论是哪一 种说法，这都不妨碍它独有的鲜香美味。不过据老一辈人的说法就是 以前的鲎粿是没有馅料的，只是后来食材种类丰富多样了，大家根据 自己的口味就添加了虾、肉、蛋等各种馅料。所以现在的鲎粿是最受 欢迎也最具美味的一种潮汕美食。</p>

<p>There are a lot of stories behind this food. It’s said that Limulus Kueh is made by a daughter-in-law to serve her toothless mother-in-law. It’s also said that this food is special in Chaoshan and it was added by limulus. Of course, some people said that in the past people lacked food so that people killed horseshoe crabs and used their blood and other starch solution to make Meal Limulus. Whatever the stories are, Limulus Kueh is still specially delicious. But the older generation said that there were no fillings in previous Limulus Kueh but later with the increasing of various food people added shrimps, meat, eggs and so on based on their own tastes. Therefore, present Limulus Kueh is the most popular and delicious food in Chaoshan. 如果你来到棉城，这座潮阳古邑，我会带你仰望文光塔的古老肃 穆，会带你品尝这也有着悠久历史的美味---鲎粿。 If you come to Miancheng, an old county in Chaoyang, I’ll show you around the solemn Man Kwong Tower and take you to taste the delicious food with a long history, Limulus Kueh. 编译 蔡莹丽</p>

<p><strong>5“摆猪羊”和“甜粿年”</strong></p>

<p><strong>“Laying Pigs and Goats” and “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice”</strong></p>

<p>“Laying Pigs and Goats” and “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice” 除旧迎新，在广东省揭东县新亨镇，一个名为硕联的村庄都会举 行一次“摆猪羊”、“摆甜粿”的闹元宵活动。活动由硕联村属下的 十个自然村（俗称十社）轮流主办。这里的“摆猪羊”和“摆甜粿” 分别可以理解为猪羊祭和甜粿祭。由于每个社十年才轮流一次，故而 对于每个社来说，都是倾尽全力，去办好这十分难得的展示自身为村 作贡献的大事。村民每年通过“摆猪羊、营锣鼓、摆甜粿”等一系列 元宵活动，庆祝过去一年生活的富足安康，同时祭拜神明，祈盼新的 一年风调雨顺、生意兴隆！ Shuolian Village, located in Xinheng Town, Jiedong County, Guangdong Province, celebrates the Lantern Festival by holding the activities of “Laying Pigs and Goats” and “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice” to welcome the New Year. These activities are organized by ten smaller natural villages affiliated to Shuolian Villages in turns. Here “Laying Pigs and Goats” and “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice” can be understood as a sacrifice of pigs, goats and sweet glutinous rice. Every village in the ten smaller natural ones does their utmost to show themselves and make a contribution to Shuolian Village because they hold the activities every ten years. Through laying pigs and goats and placing sweet glutinous rice and playing gongs and drums villagers celebrate the well-being of the past year and worship Gods to pray for fair weather and booming business in the coming year.</p>

<p>据考证，硕联村“摆猪羊”的习俗大约起源于明朝中期，距今已 有500 多年的历史。明代中期，工商业的发展，使一些族姓成为村里 大户人家，他们出于对生意兴隆的期盼，以及调和与周围邻里其他族 姓的关系，自养自宰肥硕的猪羊摆上神台，供奉财神赵公明和关公， 祭神完毕后，便将猪羊分给邻里和亲戚朋友。随着时代变迁和社会经 济的发展，各种族姓不断加入聚居，硕联村也逐步发展成52 姓氏20 社（自然村）的大村，外来族姓也入乡随俗，各家各户都逐渐有能力 “摆猪羊”祭拜财神。为避免村里发生不必要的纠纷，村里长者约定 由其中10 个较大的社每年轮流“摆猪羊”祭拜，于是这一独特的习 俗便延续至今。2009 年此项民俗活动被列入广东省级非物质文化遗 产名录。 According to research, the custom of laying pigs and goats originated in the middle of Qing Dynasty approximately. Now it has a history of over 500 years. During the middle of Qing Dynasty the development of industry and commerce enabled some tribes to become the wealthy and influential families. Therefore, in order to pray for blooming business and mediate relationships with their neighbors as well as other tribes, these rich families raised and killed fat pigs and goats themselves and put them on the table of God to offer sacrifices to two Gods of Wealth in Chinese folk tales, namely Zhao Gongming and the Duke Guan. After that all of the pigs and goats would be given away to the neighbors, relatives and friends. With the changing of times and development of social economy, different tribes lived together increasingly so that Shuolian Village has expanded to be a large village with 52 family names and 20 natural villages. Immigrated tribes also observed Shuolian’s customs and gradually each family was able to lay pigs and goats to offer sacrifices to Gods of Wealth. In order to avoid unnecessary disputes, the seniors in Shuolian set the rules that only ten bigger villages could hold the activity of “Laying Pigs and Goats ” in tuns. Hence, this unique custom has been inherited and it is listed in the intangible cultural heritage of Guangdong Province in 2009.</p>

<p>祭拜财神不仅仅只是供奉猪羊，还有一年一度新鲜甜粿的供奉和 大鹅的供奉，被村民们称为“甜粿年”和“鹅年”。硕联村十社摆猪 羊每年还会轮流分到“摆甜粿”和“鹅年”。甜粿是潮汕地区的一种 特色甜品。所谓“甜粿年”就是要祭拜甜粿，“鹅年”就得祭拜鹅。 每五年轮一次“鹅年”，“鹅年”时庆祝活动规模较小，只是祭拜神 和唱潮剧，时间也较短。“甜粿年”则不同，每个社十年轮一次甜粿 年，也要“摆猪羊”。每年的主办社都是从上一年就开始认真准备， 春节前就把村里的大路小巷挂满灯笼，家家户户贴上春联，村子里里 外外都是喜气洋洋，一片喜庆欢腾。 Worshiping Gods of Wealth is not only through offering sacrifices of pigs and goats. Fresh sweet glutinous rice and geese are also offered annually, which are called “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice” and “Laying Geese”. These two activities are also assigned to the ten villages in turns. Sweet glutinous rice is a special dessert in Chaoshan. “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice ” and “Laying Geese” mean worshiping this dessert and geese respectively. The later is held every five years and the scale is smaller and lasts for a short time, only worshiping Gods and singing Chao opera. In comparison, “Placing Sweet Glutinous Rice” plus “Laying Pigs and Goats”is held every ten years by each village. The host begins to make very careful preparations in the previous year. Before the Spring Festival all of the streets in the village are decorated by lanterns and every family sticks couplets. Everywhere is filled with joy and happiness in the village.</p>

<p>过“摆猪羊”等一系列民俗活动，庆祝过去一年生活的富足安康， 同时祈盼新的一年风调雨顺、生意兴隆、吉祥好运、生活美满。“摆 猪羊”等习俗这一隆重朴实，具有独特的和潮汕文化特色的民俗活动 在当地颇具影响，也有了一定的民俗文化研究价值。 Villagers celebrate the well-being of the past year and pray for fair whether, blooming business, success, luck and happiness in the coming year through the custom activities such as “Laying Pigs and Goats”. These customs are simple but grand with unique Chaoshan cultural characteristics so that they are influential locally and well worth investigating their folk customs. 每一年都会迎来这喜庆的几天，身为当地人的我，这不仅仅是我 最期待的日子，这也是在揭阳新亨地区的大街小巷的村民们最期待的 日子,期盼每年都能吉祥顺利、圆圆满满。我也希望在未来的日子里 我们的节日风俗能吸引世界各地的人来一起庆祝，一起来迎接这份美 好和喜悦。 Every year we welcome these festive days. As a local girl, I really look forward to them. So do all of the villagers in Xinheng Town, Jieyang City to pray for success and happiness every year. I also hope that our customs could attract people from all over the world to come, celebrate and welcome happiness and joy together. 编译倪煜琪</p>

<p><strong>6 竹升面——广东人的记忆</strong></p>

<p><strong>Bamboo-Pressed Noodle——The Memory of Cantonese</strong></p>

<p>Bamboo-Pressed Noodle——The Memory of Cantonese “老板，我的面好了没有啊？” “Excuse me? Is my noodle ready? ” “再等一下。来了，来了！” “Wait a minute, please! Here is yours.” 这样的对话每日发生在广东省各种街头角落的面店里，这面，它 是谁呢？它就是竹升面！ Such conversation takes place every day in many noodle restaurants in every street corner of Guangdong province. 中国地大物博，也孕育出了博大精深的饮食文化。在这里我们先 不论川菜、粤菜那些八大菜系有多么深奥，先说说面条为何这么受人 们宠爱吧！随着科技的发展，面条也发生了巨大的变革。如今市面上 已经有经过脱水而能存放很久的面条，只要把它和一些青菜肉类放烧 开的水里煮上七八分钟，就能收获一顿美餐，省得煮饭炒菜麻烦多多。 在餐馆，面条也是最快做好的。如此之便利，自然是大家的心头好。 China covers a vast territory and has abundant resources, so it has bred a profound diet culture. Let aside the esoteric eight major Chinese cuisines like Sichuan cuisine and Cantonese cuisine at the beginning, but start from the convenient and immensely popular noddles. Along with the development of technology, noodle has undergone a huge transformation. There are dehydrated noodles on the market that can be stored for a long time. People can enjoy a nice meal by putting the noddles together with some green vegetables and meat into boiling water for seven or eight minutes, which saves a lot of trouble in cooking. In the restaurant, noodles are always the fastest to serve. Thus everyone is fond of its convenience and delicacy. 作为主食里的面条就有无数的种类，比如说青海省的手擀面、湖 北省的热干面、山西省的拉面等等，他们都有着浓郁的浇头或是汤底。 而广东，这个注重养生护体的沿海城市，讲究饮食清淡素口，但是由 于它天气之炎热潮湿，一碗爽口解腻的竹升面便默默存在于大家的日 常三餐里。而竹升面的名字来源自它的制作方法。师傅要用上浑身重 量将粗大的竹竿用力去揉搓、打压面团，极其费力气；而它又称作碱 水面，就是以面里有碱水得称，制作面条者需要使用在面团里加入碱， 用来削去多余的酸味，使得做出来的面条味道更好。如此细细制作出</p>

<p>来的面条，纤细微黄、爽口弹牙，得到了大家一致的爱称——银丝细 面。由小见大，所有好粤菜毕生追求的，无非是一个“鲜”字，而隐 匿在日常小店里这种面条就默默地体现着“鲜”。 As one of staple foods, there are countless varieties of noodles, such as Shouganmian noodles(Hand-made noddles) in Qinghai Province, Reganmian(hot noodles with sesame paste) in Hubei Province, Lamian noodles in Shanxi Province, and so on, all of which have rich ingredient and soup bases. However, as a coastal city, Guangdong pays more attention to health preservation. Therefore, Cantonese people are keen on a light diet food. Due to the hot and humid weather in Guangdong, a bowl of tasty and refreshing Bamboo-pressed noodle has naturally become a part of everyone's daily meals. Bamboo-pressed noodle takes its name from its production method. The master needs to use his whole body weight to rub the thick bamboo pole and suppress the dough, which is extremely laborious. It is also called alkaline water because noodle makers add alkali to the dough, which strips away excess acidity and makes the noodles taste better. Bamboo-pressed noodle is delicately made and have a smooth taste, which has been unanimously loved by everyone and enjoy a reputation of filamentary silver noodle. All lovers of Cantonese cuisine pursue the the quality of "freshness" as their life-long pursuit, and these small noodle shops expressed their pursuit of "freshness" silently. 走在广州的街头，到处都可以见到各种各样的面店，无不冒着氤 氲热气的大汤锅。我们随机走进一家普通的小店，去前台点上一碗竹 升面，坐在旁边干净的凳子上，看着厨房透明玻璃窗后头，厨师熟练 地抓起一团团新鲜的竹升面和云吞或是鱼蛋或是饺子扔进小漏网里 面，然后挂在大汤锅边上，一股股食物的香气直往鼻子里面涌去，引 得馋虫蠢蠢欲动，食客们不住地抬头去看自己那一份面好了没有，有</p>

<p>那心急的甚至要走去看看什么时候能吃。面条出锅了，倒在大汤碗里 面，舀上一碗细心熬制的高汤，撒上切成段的小葱与韭黄，放入翠绿 新鲜的生菜，一份美味就端到了客人的面前。拿起筷子，挑起一缕细 细的面条，放入口中慢慢咀嚼，那爽口的感觉回馈到牙齿上，那清甜 的味道返还到舌头中，那诱人的香气钻入到鼻底下，叫人欲罢不 能…… Rambling along the street of Guangzhou, noodle stalls are everywhere--with a steaming cauldron of soup.Go to the front desk and order a bowl of bamboo pressed noodle, choose a clean bench to sit, we could see the scene of whole kitchen behind the transparent glass windows: a chef picked up a fresh ball of Bamboo-pressed noodles and throw it into the noodle net with some wonton or fish eggs or dumplings together, then hung the net with noodles on the edge of a large soup pot. And then a strong aroma of food rushing straight to the face of diners, which seduce the appetites of the diners. Several minutes later, noodles are out of the pot, and be poured in the bowl that full of soup, and then match with some chopped scallion and chives, or some green fresh lettuce, so a bowl of delicious noodle is presented in the diner’s front. 竹升面曾获得过无数奖项，但真真正正落到实处的去奠定了基础 的还是它的美味。因此，从早晨到夜晚都有街坊去光顾，不论是小朋 友还是老人家，不论是上班族还是学生，一代代的人都在赞美着竹升 面。 Bamboo-pressed noodles have won lots of awards, but the essential is its tasty flavor. Therefore, form day to night, customers usually patronize it. No matter the young or the old, office workers or student, every generation all praise it. 编译 梁诗敏苏萍张淼智</p>

<p><strong>7“越吃越少年”——普宁油柑</strong></p>

<p><strong>"The More You Eat, the More Young" - Puning Emblica</strong></p>

<p>"The More You Eat, the More Young" - Puning Emblica 油柑学名余甘，以果形圆大，果皮光滑，果肉半透明，肉色淡黄 或赤黄时最美味，吃起来酥脆而无渣，甘甜生津，反之，颜色越青绿 的油柑，味道越苦涩，在咀嚼时还伴有渣。油柑可以生吃，生吃时先 酸涩，随后甘甜，回味无穷，也可以用盐腌制，还可以制作成凉果。 与其他鲜美甜口的水果不同，就算油柑完全熟透之后，刚一入口，它 给人的感觉仍是苦涩的。揭阳多地均有产油柑，普宁为主产区，而狮 头油柑更是其中一个优良的品种。 Emblica is also known as Yu Gan, which is round in shape, smooth in the skin, translucent in the flesh, and the most delicious when it turns ripe to be pale yellow or red yellow. It tastes crisp without slag, and sweet. On the contrary, the greener the emblica is, the more bitter the taste is, and there are also slag when chewing. It can be eaten raw, sour and then sweet and has a long aftertaste. It can also be salted and made into preserved fruit. Different from other delicious fruits, the first taste of it is still bitter even when the emblica is fully ripe. Many places in Jieyang are rich in emblica. Puning is the main producting area, and ShiTou Emblica is one of the excellent varieties. 在普宁地区，油柑是大人们的最爱，人们喜欢在茶余饭后嚼上几 颗。但人们吃油柑，并不在乎它的果肉，而是慢慢品尝果肉中的汁液。 当你第一口咬它的时候，先是一股又苦又涩的汁液充斥口腔，第一次 品尝的人受条件反射会毫不犹豫地马上把它吐掉；可是当你咬第二口 时，慢慢地把汁液吞下去，就会有一股清爽甘甜的津液从口腔、舌下 渗涌而出，越嚼越有味道。吐出细小的果核之后，喝上一杯温开水， 会有一股神奇的甘甜气息充盈在整个口腔，同时还伴随着美妙的清 甜。 In Puning area, emblica is the favorite of adults, people like to chew a few after dinner. When people taste emblica, they don't care about its flesh, but about its juice. In your first bite, a bitter juice fills your mouth in an instant, and people who taste it for the first time will subconsciously spit it out. But as you take a second bite and swallow the juice, you will feel fresh and sweet. The more you chew, the tastier. After spitting out the tiny seeds, drinking a cup of warm water, the whole mouth will have a magical and wonderful sweet. 除了神奇美妙的口感，食用油柑更是发挥着多种作用，例如去油</p>

<p>助消化、润肺清嗓、解暑止渴，消痰止喉痛等作用，果汁更有祛风、 止泻之功效，在我国作为民间中药已有2000 年的历史。 In addition to its wonderful taste, the emblica has a variety of functions, such as removing grease to aid digestion, moistening lungs and clearing throat, relieving summer-heat and thirst, eliminating phlegm and relieving throat pain, etc. The fruit juice has the effect of dispelling wind and relieving diarrhea. In China, it has been used as a folk traditional medicine for 2,000 years in China。 古时候，人们常常服用油柑果实，用以治疗消化不良、胃腹痛、 感冒、牙疼、咽喉痛，疝痛、痢疾、咳嗽等疾患。早在明代，李时珍 在《本草纲目》中就记载，油柑有“久服轻身、延年长生”作用，而 现代科学证实，油柑不仅能明显治疗和预防胃癌，还对乙型肝炎、高 血脂、高血压、高血糖等均有较好的疗效，研究还证明，油柑果汁具 有防癌和抗衰老作用。 In ancient times, people often took the emblica fruit to treat indigestion, stomachache, cold, toothache, sore throat, colic, dysentery, cough and other diseases. As early as the Ming dynasty, Li Shizhen has recorded that the long-term use of emblica has the effect of relieving the tension of body and prolonging life in Compendium of Materia Medica. Furthermore, the modern science has proved that emblica fruit can not only cure and prevent gastric cancer obviously, but also have good curative effect on hepatitis B, hyperlipidemia, hypertension and hyperglycemia. What’s more, studies also proved that its juice can prevent cancer and aging. 无论是鲜食油柑，盐渍油柑，还是在煮制加工过程中保证所含维 生素均不被破坏的蜜饯油柑，都能起到作用。因此，民间流传着“甘 回味甜，越吃越少年”的谚语，还有“油甘吃了回味甜，老人吃了变</p>

<p>少年”的民谣。 Whether fresh emblica, salted emblica, or preserved emblica has a good medical effect. Therefore, a lot of Puning folks believe that the emblica will make elder more younger. And the exaggerated medical function of rejuvenating effects has been made into folk songs. 由于油柑在众多水果中营养排列前茅，后被卫生部列入“既是食 品又是药品”的名单，同时，联合国粮农组织还把油柑与山楂、白榄 列为“世界三大杂果”，并安排经费和组织专家对油柑进行研究和开 发利用。 Because of its nutritional arrangement in many fruits is among the best, emblica has been listed in the list of "both food and medicine" by the Ministry of Health. At the same time, the United Nations Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) makes Puning emblica, hawthorn and white olive as "the world's three major fruit", and provide funds and experts on the research development and utilization of emblica fruit. 除了具有药用价值，油柑果实还可以做成染料，油柑叶常用来填 充枕头以透气散热，油柑树木呈赤色，且坚硬，可用于制作家具，油 柑树皮是化学工业的重要原料。 In addition to its medicinal value, emblica fruit can also be made into dye, emblica leaves are often used to fill pillows with the function of air permeability and heat dissipation, emblica trees are red, and hard, can be used to make furniture, meanwhile, the emblica bark is an important raw material in the chemical industry. 在普宁地区，几乎有地的人家都会有几颗油柑树，待到果实成熟 时，家家户户提起大筐采果，小小的枝头上密密麻麻全是油柑。盛产 期，走在街道上，都能看到小贩们成筐成筐地摆在路边，人们排着队 按斤按斤地购买。 In Puning area, almost every family will have a few emblica trees. When the fruit is ripe, even those small branches are covered with emblica, then every family will pick up a large basket of fruit. During the harvest period, when you walk on the street you will see vendors on the streets with baskets of emblica and people line up to buy the fresh and delicious emblica. 编译赖雪萍刘珂刘秀英</p>

<p><strong>8 揭西美食</strong></p>

<p><strong>Jiexi Cuisine</strong></p>

<p>Jiexi Cuisine 身为揭西人，实在难以容忍家乡美食不被世人熟知。揭西美食是 所有在外游子心心念念的家乡味道，以下是一些代表美食： As a native of Jiexi, it is a great honor to introduce the cuisine of my hometown to the people across the world. Of course, for me, and for those who floating outside as well, Jiexi cuisine is the taste of hometown. When we talk about Jexi cuisine, I have to introduce the following representative delicacies to you. 擂茶是客家的传统的食俗,广东客家擂茶的发源地就是揭西县河 婆镇。几乎所有客家人都知道如何制作擂茶，热情好客的客家人常常 以擂茶待客作为其传统的礼节。（百度百科）河婆擂茶要先把茶叶、 烤花生、烤芝麻等放在擂缸里擂成酱，然后再加少许食盐（也可以加 糖），然后将沸水冲进缸里。食擂茶，要把擂茶舀进大米饭里，混成 粥，再加上虾米，花生，葱，韭菜，大蒜，菜脯等炒熟了的配料。擂 茶芳香可口，能增进食欲，提神醒脑。 Leicha tea is a traditional delicacy for Hakka cuisine, which originated from Hepo town, Jiexi County of Guangdong Provenience. All of the Hakka people know how to make Lei Tea, especially women. Hakka people are hospitable, Leicha tea is a traditional food to entertain their distinguished guests. Leicha tea has a variety of ingredients. According to the different seasons, the ingredients and traditional Chinese medicines used in making Leicha tea are different, while the making process is basically the same. People put tea, roasted peanuts and roasted sesame seeds and crash it into a sauce firstly, then add a little salt (or sugar), and the last procedure of the making of Leicha tea is to flush boiling water into the jar that filled with the ingredients of Leicha tea. Leicha tea usually eat together with rice, people scoop Leicha tea into rice and mix it into porridge, then some people might plus fried ingredients such as shrimp, peanuts, onions, leeks, garlic, preserved vegetables and so</p>

<p>on according to their personal taste. Leicha tea is fragrant and delicious, which can increase appetite and refresh the mind. 揭西水粄是另一揭西传统美食，用料上乘、做工精细。首先，将 浸泡后的优质米细细地研磨成半浓稠的米浆，然后在特制的直径约三 十公分的正方形铁板内舀上一勺米浆，左右晃动使其均匀，再用猛火 蒸。五分钟后，一张蒸熟了的透明爽滑的米浆皮就做好了，将其揭下， 把炒熟了的肉末，豆角，鲜笋，咸菜等馅放入，再卷成圆筒状就可以 了。水粄细嫩可口，多食不腻，可作为正餐食用。 Jiexi Shuiban rice cake is another traditional delicacy of Jiexi districts, it selects superior material and make in excellent workmanship. First of all, grind the soaked high-quality rice into semi-thick rice milk, then scoop a spoonful of rice paste into a special square iron plate with a diameter of about 30 centimeters, shake it left and right to make it uniform, and then steam it over high heat. Five minutes later, a transparent and smooth steamed rice paste skin is ready. Take it off, put in the stuffing of fried minced meat, beans, fresh bamboo shoots and pickles, and roll it into a cylinder. The rice noodle is delicate and delicious, can be eaten as a staple food. 红桃粄，因其外边是桃红色称之为桃粄。每逢喜庆节日或是年结 时分，家家户户都会做上几对红桃粄拜神，祭祀。它有一个很好的寓 意就是吉祥如意，红红火火。红桃粄的原材料是面粉加水按比例混合， 揉搓成适当的面团，再往里面放炒香了的花生碎和菜脯。与其他粄不 同的是，桃粄是有一个专门的模子的，木质的模子有漂亮的花纹，所</p>

<p>以做好的桃粄正反都有漂亮精致的花纹，然后放进蒸锅蒸熟就可以食 用了。其实桃粄还有另外一种食法，就是将蒸熟了的桃粄烹炸一遍， 炸后的桃粄外焦里嫩，是另一番美味。 Hongtaoban is a kind of rice cake that similar as Shuiban, and it is named Hongtaoban(tao in Chinese language means peach, and peach contain a good meaning in China, which represents lucky and longevity) as its peach color. On festive occasions or at the end of the New Year, every household will offer a few dishes of Hongtaoban (peach colored rice cake) to worship their gods and praying for a good luck and prosperous future. The raw material of is rice flour, which mixes with water in proportion and knead into proper dough, and then putting into it the stir-fried peanut pieces and preserved vegetables. In order to make the food more attractive, the stuffed rice cake is placed in a wood mould with delicate patterns. After a few minutes steam, you can taste the delicious and pleasant looking Hongtaoban rice cake. In fact, peach cake has another way of cooking, which is to fry the steamed peach cake and make it crispy on outside and meltingly tender on the inside. 碗粄，用粘米粉加白糖加在30 度的水，尽量和稀，越稀就越软， 最后加上发酵粉，放置两三个小时后，往碗里加上发酵好的米糊，用 大火蒸，还要裹上布条不漏气，这样会更容易熟。它特别的是用碗来 做模具，所以蒸好的碗子粄外形精致，底部光滑完整，顶部膨胀开裂 像一朵盛开的花，甜甜的碗子粄让人看了心情愉悦，吃了心里甜丝丝 的，最重要的是它的笑预兆着来年合家过上平安顺利，笑口常开的美 好日子。</p>

<p>Wanban rice cake has a similar making procedure as Shuiban rice cake and Hongtaoban rice cake, which takes rice flour and sugar as raw materials. The mixed rice flour knead with 30 degrees of water to make it as soft as possible, and then mix with some yeast powder, and let it stand for about two or three hours. After three hours, put the fermented rice paste to a bowls and steam it with high heat and cover with gauze to prevent the air leakage. It usually is shaped with bowl, so it is named as Wanban rice cake (Wan means bowl in Chinese language). The steamed Wanban rice cakes has a delicate appearance, the bottom part is smooth because of the smooth bowl mould, and the top of Wanban rice cake swells and cracks into a blooming flower shape. Meanwhile, it contains a good meaning for Jiexi people, the crack shape make the rice cake looks like a smiley appearance which omens for a safe and smooth coming year of the family. A bit of sweet Wanban rice cake makes people pleasant and comfortable. 揭西豆干是漂泊在外的揭西人念念不忘的味道。它的制法是用大 豆磨浆，加上少许薯粉，石膏等原料配制,蒸熟后包成白或黄两种颜 色的方块状。它的烹饪之法可分为炒，煎，油炸三种。其中油炸豆干 最为脍炙人口，油炸豆干，皮薄而酥脆，内肉白而嫩滑，被称为“外 金内银”。尤其是在冬天，品尝一口油炸豆干，香味久存于口齿之中， 又烫又脆，额头上闪着汗，也是十分有趣的画面。若以葱蒜盐水作为 蘸料，味道更上一层楼。 Jiexi fried dried tofu is an unforgettable taste for those Jiexi people who wandering away. It is made by grinding soybean pulp, adding a little potato powder, gypsum and other raw materials preparation, steamed after the package into white or yellow two color square block. It can be cooked in three ways: stir-fry, pan-fry and deep-fry. Among them, the deep-fried dried beans are the most popular among Jiexi people. With thin and crisp skin and white and tender insider, fried dried beans are</p>

<p>known as "gold outside and silver inside". Especially in winter, a bite of hot, crispy, deep-fried dried beans will leaves the aroma of fried Doufu lingering in your mouth and sweat glistening on your forehead, which composed a peaceful and joyful scene of winter. 揭西菜脯是在外游子必备的家乡味道。菜脯是以生萝卜为原料， 经过腌制、加工和晾晒，外地人称之为“萝卜干”。其呈棕红色，皮 面光滑，咸淡适宜，是搭配早餐白粥的一道家珍小菜。在揭西，家家 户户的老人几乎都会做这道小菜，他们会把腌制并加工后的萝卜装进 闲置的瓶子里，给在外打工的孩子们备着。现在的青年人不大喜欢喝 白粥，但他们会将菜脯配合其他食材，做成各类美食，比如菜脯冬瓜 汤，菜脯蛋饼等。</p>

<p>Jiexi dried preserved vegetables is an essential hometown flavor of a wanderer. Preserved vegetables is made from raw radish, which is pickled, processed and air-dried. Outsiders call it "dried radish." It is brownish-red, with smooth skin and suitable saltiness. It is a home-cooked side dish for breakfast that usually match with white porridge. In Jiexi, the elder in every household can cook this side dish. They will put the pickled and processed radishes into bottles and preserve them for their children whom working outside. Young people nowadays don't like to eat white porridge, but they might combine the preserved vegetables with other ingredients to make various kinds of delicacies, such as preserved vegetables and wax gourd soup, preserved vegetables omelets, etc. 编译陈锦玲 陈彩玲符湛敏</p>

<p><strong>9 一碗濑粉寓意深</strong></p>

<p><strong>The Profound Meaning of Laifen</strong></p>

<p>The Profound Meaning of Laifen 众所周知，正所谓“食在广东”，在广东这座城市美食更是数不 胜数。相信你一定听过这么一句话广东人什么东西都可以用来煲汤。 而在我居住的佛山高明这座城市，它有一道特具代表性的美食，是的， 一提起高明你就会想起高明的濑粉，它不仅仅成为了高明这座城市的 标志性卡片，更是佛山十大名小吃之一。而且自2006 年以来每年的 10 月13 号都会举行“高明濑粉节”，现场教授如何制作濑粉和提供 品尝，高明濑粉节目前已经连续举办了13 届了。 Guangdong is famous for food, there is a saying called “eating in Guangdong” which highly praises the delicious Cantonese delicacies. I believe you must have heard the saying that Cantonese people can use anything to make soup. And in my hometown Gaoming county of Foshan city, there is a special representative food, it named Laifen noodle, a kind of Seto noodles. It has not only become the landmark card of Gaoming, but also one of the top ten snacks in Foshan. And since 2006, every year on October 13th will be a "Gaoming Seto-noodle Festival", the sponsor of the food festival will invite some chef to teach people how to make Laifen noddle and also provide opportunity of tasting. Until now, the Gaoming Laifen noodle festival has been held for 13 sessions consecutively. 濑粉在高明人的生活中已成为一种不可或缺的习俗。在早上大家 都喜欢点上一碗热腾腾的濑粉，然后元气满满的开启新的一天。特别 是每逢过节或非常喜庆的日子，你都可以在餐桌上看到它的踪影。因 为传说中濑粉有着长长久久、吉祥如意和丰衣足食的好寓意。 Eating Laifen noodle has became an inseparable custom for locals in Gaoming. People prefer to order a bowl of freshly cooked Laifen noodle in the morning to start an energetic day. As there are many legends have expressed the good meaning of Laifen noodle, such as everlasting love, good luck, ample food and clothing, happiness ect., it is also very popular for Gaoming people to eat Laifen noodle to celebrate their festivals or other jubilant day. 濑粉主要以用稻米打磨出来的粘米粉为原材料，在高明，濑粉大 多数是由人们手工制作出来的，因为做出来的粉的口感与和粉时的力 度有着非常重要的关系，打磨粉的力度越恰当，做出来的濑粉才会越 有嚼劲。濑粉的名字起源具有一定的当地特色，之所以称之为濑粉是 由于制作时要把米粉团从木孔中“濑”出一条条长长的爽滑且带有韧 性的粉。而“濑”字则源于“水从细沙上流过”这一动作。</p>

<p>The main ingredient of Laifen noodle is the sticky rice flour which be ground by rice seed. Most of the Laifen noodle in Gaoming are hand-made, and the taste and texture of the noodle is decided by the strength of kneading of dough. The origin of the name has a certain local characteristics, the word “Lai” is a local dialect which used to describe the motion of rushing out of the rice dough from a mould hole. 高明濑粉以熬了好几小时的猪骨浓汤为汤底，再加上一把葱、姜、 蒜、鸡蛋丝、头菜丝、花生碎等配料，而每一种配料都有它的寓意。 例如，葱表示翠意绵绵、姜代表将心比心、蒜则寓意着如意算盘、花 生碎代表妙笔生花、头菜丝寓意着万事如意、鸡蛋丝代表今生今世。 濑粉的搭配更是十分丰盛，可以选择与牛腩、瘦肉猪肝、猪杂、猪脚 等进行搭配。满满的一碗濑粉真是色香味俱全，非常诱人且令人流连 忘返。 Laifen takes thick pork bone soup that brewed over several hours as the soup base, and plus a handful of scallion, ginger, garlic, egg strips, shredded cabbage, crushed peanuts and other ingredients to make it more tasty, and each of these ingredients expresses a good wish according to their Chinese pronunciation,color and shape. For example, scallion(green color) means" vitality", ginger(Chinese</p>

<p>pronunciation:Jiang, the meaning of Jiang has been expanded into “Jiang xin bi xin”,which means put oneself in others’ position) means "heart to heart", garlic (Chinese pronunciation: Suan, here represents a traditional Chinese manual calculation tool, which has been used as a metaphor for subjective intention of desire ) means "satisfying subjective desire", crushed peanuts(Chinese pronunciation of Peanut: Hua Sheng, Chinese people usually convert the word into Sheng Hua, which means usually takes to describe someone’s art of writing is brilliant as beautiful flower) mean "brilliant writing", shredded cabbage means "Everything goes as you wish", egg strips mean "A wonderful present life". A bowl of Laifen noodle are rich of ingredients, you can choose whatever you like to make a unique delicacy for yourself and your distinguished guests. A full bowl of Laifen noodle with its perfect combination of color, aroma and taste, which it's so alluring that you'll always miss this taste. 高明濑粉制作流程传说是由善于种植水稻的古代高明瑶人传给 汉人的，这样算起来高明濑粉已有超过五百多年的历史了。在八十年 代以前，高明的经济状态还处于比较贫穷的时期，所以大多数农户一 般都会在粮食丰收后留一些晚稻, 然后把它磨成粉晒干，储藏于密封 罐中，等到庆祝节日时把它做成濑粉。据说濑粉还有清热降火的功效， 小孩子上火不愿意吃药，大人就会煮碗濑粉给他清火。 Gaoming Laifen noodle has a history of more than 500 years. According to legend, the making technique of Gaoming Laifen noodle was invented and passed down by the ancient Yao people to the Han people of Gaoming district who were good at growing rice. Before the eighties, Gaoming's economy was still in a relatively poor status, people are in short supply, therefore, Laifen became a delicacy for festival. There is a convention that a great majority of farmers would keep some late grown rice after a good harvest, and then ground it into flour, dried it and stored it in sealed jars, until the festivals to make it into a bowl of delicious Laifen noodle. It is said that Laifen noodle also has a certain of medicine effect of clearing away internal heat of people, so when children are reluctant to take medicine, parents usually cook a bowl of Laifen noodle to help him clear away the heat. 高明濑粉在民间还有个“黎十万调灶”的传说。传说在明代高明 更楼的坨程村，从武当山学习归来的黎十万由于没有学到可以养活自 己谋生法术，而遭到村里人的怀疑。而刚好在这一年的大年三十，村 里的每家每户都发生了特别奇异的事，全村的火灶都没了灶口，没有 办法做濑粉。然而黎十万却不在意，好像什么事都没发生地请村民各 自回家，这时火灶突然复原。从此，村里的人便有了每逢年三十就守 着火灶做濑粉的习惯。</p>

<p>There is an another legend about Laifen in Gaoming among folks, which is called “Li Shiwan moves away stoves”. Li Shiwan was a villager of Gaoming district who went to Wudang Mountain for learning magic art and didn’t acquire any skills to make a living, so he was ostracized by the other folks of the village. Just in a New Year's eve, something weird happened that every family in the village lost their stoves, it was no way for them to cook a bowl of Laifen to celebrate the big festival. The villagers believed it was a trick of Li Shiwan, so they came to Li Shiwan and ask him to give back their stoves. Li Shiwan didn’t show any surprise and told the villagers their stove already back to their kitchen, then the villagers went back and found that their stoves suddenly came back. From then on, the people in the village has formed the custom of guarding their fire stove by sitting around the fire stove to cook Laifen noodle every New Year's eve. 高明濑粉的独特美味给我留下了非常深刻的印象，濑粉做法虽较 为朴素，但却很耗时间，且追求制作精美，这也反映出高明人们勤劳 节俭和朴实热情的美好品质。尽管如今机器生产十分发达，但现在高 明很多店铺依然坚持采用传统手工制作的手法，让高明濑粉这种传统 美食继续传承发扬下去，让更多的人吃到高明的濑粉，感受高明濑粉 的魅力。 I am deeply impressed by the unique delicacy of Laifen noodle. It reflects the fine quality of diligence, frugality and simple enthusiasm of the Gaoming people. Although the machine changes the production and makes the food more accessible. Gaoming people still prefer to the traditional handmade techniques, more and more people are keen on the inheritance and development of this traditional food and its techniques. For many artisans of Laifen technique in Gaoming, Laifen stand for Gaoming, to make more people taste the flavor of Laifen and feel the charm of Laifen has became their mission. 编译郑柔莎刘心怡姚佳旭</p>

<p><strong>10 汕尾擂茶</strong></p>

<p><strong>Ground Tea of Shanwei</strong></p>

<p>Ground Tea of Shanwei 五味调和是境界，是理解更是手段，是中庸之道。陆河的客家人 一直在实践着这种五味调和天然材料的食物——擂茶。汕尾陆河，是 榕江和漯河水系发源地，具有独特的客家风情的福佬文化，有客俗桃 源之称。 The harmony of five tastes is the realm, understanding, measure, and golden mean. The Hakka people in Luhe have been eating this food made with natural materials with the five tastes in harmony – ground tea. Luhe County in Shanwei City is the birthplace of Rongjiang River and Luohe River. It has a unique Hakka style and Gefulao culture, and is known as a Hakka paradise. 汕尾的几乎每家每户都会有喝擂茶的习惯，饮茶有利于健康，已 为世人所共知，擂茶不仅可以清饮，也可以配炒米而饮，而陆河人以 擂茶招待客人仍是最隆重的礼节，也是从古至今的传统风俗。擂茶， 成了客家社交活动中必不可少的饮料。 Almost every family in Shanwei has the habit of drinking ground tea. Drinking tea is good for health which has been known to the world. Ground tea can not only be drunk alone (light drinking), but also be served with fried rice. However, it is still the most formal etiquette for Luhe people to entertain guests with ground tea, and is also a traditional custom from the ancient times to the present. Ground tea has become an indispensable drink in Hakka social activities. 擂茶被称为最古老的茶道之一，又名三生汤，起于汉，盛于明清， 流传已久。关于擂茶的起源，目前公认的说法为广东省揭西县河婆镇 南关城老妇人何婆售卖的街边小吃。当时的南关城是潮汕和惠州经商 的必经之路，而何婆的擂茶解决了往来客商的疲劳，因此名声远播。 古代的南关城也就是如今的潮汕地区，于是擂茶文化成为了这个地区 口口相传的独有文化，而擂茶也成为这个地区特有的美食。 Ground tea is one of the most ancient tea ceremony, and another name is Sansheng soup, because the soup made from three raw materials. Then ground tea, originated in the Han Dynasty, flourished in the Ming and Qing Dynasties, has been circulating for a long time. As for the origin of ground tea, it is generally accepted that ground tea is a street snack sold by an old woman, Granny He, in Nanguan Town, Jiexi County, Guangdong Province. At that time, Nanguan Town was the only way to do business in Chaoshan area and Huizhou city, and this old woman’s handmade tea</p>

<p>fixed the fatigue of travelling merchants, so it was well-known. The ancient Nanguan Town is now Chaoshan area, so the culture of ground tea has become the unique culture handed down by mouth in this area, and the ground tea has also become the unique food in this area. 在汕尾始终流传着这样一句话：无擂茶不成客。热情好客的汕尾 人家里少不了擂茶，也越来越多人认为在汕尾才能喝到正宗的擂茶。 地形气候不同使得擂茶在汕尾地区也衍生了许多的制作方法，其中汕 尾陆河的客家擂茶可谓是大家喜爱度最高的一种了。 In Shanwei city, there is always a saying that "no ground tea, no guest". The warm and hospitable people in Shanwei can't live without ground tea, and more and more people think that only in Shanwei can they drink authentic ground tea. Different terrain and climate make ground tea in Shanwei made in a lot of production methods. Among them, ground tea of Luhe County is one of the most popular. 陆河人制作擂茶有一套称为“擂茶三宝”的工具：一是圆形且内壁 有粗密沟纹的陶制擂钵；二是用上等山楂木或油茶树干加工制成的擂 棍；三是用竹篾制成的过滤碎渣的“捞子”。擂茶的整个过程讲究“一 粗二顺三韧劲”，“粗”指研磨茶叶时可以简单擂几下，粗略粉碎即可； “顺”是指研磨芝麻时力求用力均匀平顺，不可用力过猛过急，要将芝 麻尽数研磨成酱，不要将芝麻压进陶纹里；“韧劲”是指随着熟花生米 等佐料的不断增加，研擂越来越费劲，擂茶工作要持之以恒。汕尾人 家里都有一个陶钵，当地话叫“牙钵”，土黄色，普通的电饭锅内胆大</p>

<p>小，外壁光滑，内里刻意凿出粗糙的纹路，配着一支半米长的实木” 茶槌“，海丰人世世代代吃的咸茶，就是在这样古老简单的工具里做 出来的。 The people in Luhe have a set of tools for making ground tea, which were called "three treasures of ground tea". One was a round pottery bowl with thick grooves on the inner wall. The second is a stick made of hawthorn wood or camellia tree trunk. The third is a sieve made of bamboo strips and used for filtering broken slag. The whole production process of ground tea pays attention to three key points: rough, smooth, and tenacity. "Rough" refers to roughly mashing tea leaves during grinding. "Smooth" refers to grinding sesame seeds evenly and smoothly to grind all the sesame seeds into paste. "Tenacity" means that with the constant increase of seasonings such as cooked peanuts, it is more and more difficult to grind, and the work of tea grinding should be perseverant. Shanwei people have a pottery bowl at home, which is called "tooth bowl" in the local dialect. It is yellow and the same size as a regular rice cooker. The outer wall is smooth and the inner wall is deliberately chiseled with rough lines, matched with a half-meter long solid wood "tea hammer". Haifeng people eat salty tea for generations that is made in such an ancient simple tool. 简易版的擂茶，茶叶不需要好的，碎茶即可，开水冲洗一遍，加 几片薄荷树上摘下的叶子，放入牙钵，在腿间夹一条毛巾，牙钵放在 毛巾内，两腿夹紧，双手握住茶槌，探入牙钵，顺时针碾压，这便是” 擂“。这道程序直到把茶叶薄荷叶碾压得烂烂的，拿开茶槌，放下牙 钵，撒进些许盐粒，刚煮开的滚水一冲，芳香四溢，一碗擂茶就好了， 加上苞米花生芝麻即可饮用了。海丰人有时还习惯在擂茶里再添加一 些剁碎的菠菜、白菜、芹菜、生菜、青蒜、荷兰豆、香菇、粉丝、虾 米、瘦猪肉、香肠、鱿鱼等富有营养的东西，用骨头汤或鸡汤煨之， 上面再撒以炒米、花生、胡椒等，做成一种极好的“点心”——菜茶。 菜茶在海丰城乡很是普遍，每逢农历正月十三那天，这里都会处处张 灯结彩家家喝菜茶。 A simple version of ground tea does not need good tea. The tea can be broken leaves. Rinse the tea leaves with boiling water, add a few mint leaves, put them into the pot, put a towel between the legs, and put the pot in the towel, clamp the legs tightly, then hold the tea mallet with both hands and reach into the pot, and roll clockwise, then the tea is smashed. In this procedure smash the leaves of the tea and mint until they are crushed, take away the hammer and put down the bowl, sprinkle some salt with boiling water, fragrant overflow, a bowl of ground tea is done, and then add peanuts and sesame. Haifeng people sometimes add in ground tea some chopped spinach, Chinese cabbage, leeks, celery, lettuce, snow peas, mushroom, vermicelli,</p>

<p>shrimp, lean pork, sausage, squid and other nutritious, with bone soup or chicken soup simmer, sprinkle with parched rice, peanuts and peppers, etc., make it a delicious dessert called "vegetable tea". Vegetable tea in Haifeng County is very common. Every year on the thirteenth day of the first lunar month, every family here will decorated with lanterns and drink vegetable tea. 陆河有另一种用料极为讲究的擂茶称“油茶”，亦称“生茶”。主要 用料有鲜艾叶、薄荷叶、生茶叶、枫树嫩芽、紫苏叶、番香、香苏、 鸡脚刺、玫嫩芽、芫荽菜等。这是一种纯天然原材料制成的美味，包 含了各种药材草药，更由于油茶具有生津止渴，防风祛寒、开胃健脾、 清热解毒、延年益寿的功效，因此最受旅游者和当地人喜欢，汕尾的 大街小巷也开了许多的油茶店，一到正午和晚上，队伍也是人满为患。 在陆河，擂茶搭配米饭乃是普通人家每天中午的主食。并且，每年正 月初七被定为“开茶日”，这一天要用七种菜一起擂成“七样菜茶”。七 样菜即红生菜、芹菜、芥兰菜、葱、蒜、芫荽、荷兰豆、豌豆等七种 蔬菜，人们以此为原料，有的加佐料炒成七菜就茶当餐，有的加新起 锅的猪油渣一块炒熟，放进茶钵研擂，制作成油茶。陆河擂茶是广东 汕尾陆河县家喻户晓的美食，是客家人自制的纯天然食品，风味独特。 2012 年入选广东省第四批省级非物质文化遗产保护代表性名录也在 2011 年入选了广东省非物质文化遗产保护名录。如今，它不仅兴盛 在广东海陆丰(汕尾)地区，而且随着当地居民的迁徙，还日益向广东、 福建等其他沿海地区，乃至海外蔓延。据说，海丰籍的音乐巨匠马思 聪，在病危临逝，对身边亲人喟然长叹的乃是：“可惜我再也不能回 到海丰食擂茶了……”作为汕尾人，我们很为自己的家乡感到骄傲， 因为正是这些朴素的美食让我们心里始终保持一颗朴素的心，未来随 着港澳大湾区的发展建设，每个小地区的各种文化都会为广为人知， 当你来到汕尾的时候，一定要去喝一碗香喷喷的擂茶才不虚此行！ Another kind of ground tea, called "you tea" or “sheng tea”, is also known as "the tea with a special flavor". The main ingredients are fresh wormwood leaf, mint leaf, raw tea, maple bud, perilla leaf, saffron, fragrant perilla, chicken foot thorn, rose bud, coriander, etc. This is a kind of delicacy made of pure natural raw materials, including various medicinal herbs. Because of its functions of promoting body fluid and relieving thirst, preventing wind and cold, appetizing and invigorating the spleen, clearing heat and detoxification, and prolonging life, it is most popular among tourists and local people. There are many camellia oil shops in the streets of Shanwei, and the street is full of people at noon and evening. In Luhe, the ground tea with rice is the staple food for ordinary people at noon every day. In addition, the seventh day of the first month of each year is designated as the "tea day". On this day, seven kinds of</p>

<p>vegetables are used to make "seven kinds of tea". The vegetables include red lettuce, celery, mustard, green onion, garlic, coriander, lotus beans, peas and other vegetables, all raw materials. Some of them are fried with seasonings and add into the tea as food. Some of them are fried with fresh pig oil residue, and then put into a tea bowl to make camellia oleifera. Luhe ground tea is a well-known delicacy in Luhe County, Shanwei, Guangdong Province. It is a pure natural food made by Hakka people with unique flavor. In 2012, it was selected into the fourth batch of provincial intangible cultural heritage protection representative list of Guangdong Province, and was selected into the intangible cultural heritage protection list of Guangdong Province in 2011. Nowadays, it not only flourishes in hailufeng (Shanwei) area of Guangdong Province, but also spreads to other coastal areas such as Guangdong, Fujian and even overseas with the migration of local residents. 编译林雅铃杨美华刘平龙</p>

<hr />

<h2>五、民间风景名胜与文化</h2>

<p><strong>1 安铺古镇</strong></p>

<p><strong>Anpu Ancient Town</strong></p>

<p>Anpu Ancient Town 安铺古镇建立于明朝时期，相传至今已有五百多年的悠久历史。 安铺古镇最初称为暗铺，嘉庆二十四年才改名为安铺，它隶属于石城 县。根据有关文献记载，早在清朝嘉庆期间，安铺镇就是一个繁华的 集贸中心，曾与中山小榄镇、顺德容奇镇、东莞石龙镇并称为“广东 四大古镇”。 Anpu Ancient Town was established in the Ming Dynasty and has a long history of more than 500 years. The ancient town of Anpu was originally called An-pu(this “An” is read in falling tone in Chinese) which was renamed Anpu only in the twenty-fourth year of Jiaqing(the 7the emperor of Qing Dynasty). It was under the jurisdiction of Shicheng County. According to relevant records, Anpu Town was a prosperous market and trade center during the period of the King Jiaqing’s ruling. It was once known as on of the "Four Ancient Towns in Guangdong" together with Xiaolan Town in Zhongshan City, Rongqi Town in Shunde District, and Shilong Town in Dongguan City. 安铺古镇历史悠久，环境优越，文化气氛浓郁，并保留了极具特 色的文化遗产，有较为人知的有：中山公园，文笔塔，安铺白戏，安 铺八音等等，是一座极具特色的文化古城。 The ancient town of Anpu has a long history, superior environment, strong cultural atmosphere, and retains unique cultural heritage. Some of the more well-known ones include: Zhongshan Park, Wenbi Tower, Anpu Baixi, Anpu Bayin, etc.It is indeed a unique cultural ancient city. 安铺古镇之中山公园。中山公园建立于1931 年，它是国内第一 个镇级中山公园。建造历时三年，建成时颇见规模，文化气息浓厚， 一直到1944 年至1945 年间，由于受日本侵华战争的影响，园区遭到 破坏。后来，随着经济发展，镇委为满足人民休闲娱乐的需要，从 1980 年起，才大规模开展修复扩建工程，历时五年，园内面貌焕然 一新，风景美不胜收。 Zhongshan Park. Zhongshan Park was established in 1931. It is the first town-level Zhongshan Park in China. It was quite large and had a strong cultural atmosphere when the project was finished for the first time after 3-year construction . From 1944 to 1945, the park was destroyed due to the impact of the Japanese invasion of China. Later, with the economic development, in order to meet the people's leisure</p>

<p>and entertainment needs, the town committee started a large-scale restoration and expansion project from 1980. It took five years to give the park a brand new look with outstanding scenery. 安铺古镇之文笔塔。文笔塔在1994 年被列入县级文物保护单位。 文笔塔座落于安铺古镇，始建于清同治二年（公元一八六三年），内 供文曲星君站立偶像，学子文士，常至殿阶朝拜，以求上进，“文笔 塔”的名称由此传诵开。根据《安铺镇志》记载，原塔于1946 年时 被误为"四旧"拆掉，后于1993 年重建。新建的文笔塔高七层，约33 米，文笔塔的廊檐共有八个角，微微往上翘，塔角由下至上逐渐变小， 十分有层次感。 Wenbi Tower. Wenbi Tower was listed as a county-level cultural relic protection site in 1994. Located in Anpu Ancient Town, it was built in the second year of Emperor Tongzhi in the Qing Dynasty (1863). The tower is used for standing statue of Wenquxingjun(a famous god of wisdom in Chinese traditional legends and tales). Scholars and learners often worships at the temple steps for good luck in national competitive examination, starting making Wenbi Tower increasingly well-known and popular. According to the Anpu Town Official Records, the original tower was mistakenly demolished as the "Four Old" in 1946, and then rebuilt in 1993. The newly built Wenbi Tower is seven stories high of about 33 meters. The eaves of the Tower at each level have eight corners, gradually becoming smaller from bottom to top, which is layered. 安铺古镇之白戏。每个地方都有其各具特色的戏曲，最为出名的 中国十大经典戏曲虽然不包括安铺白戏，但作为小戏种的它，也颇具 历史特色。安铺白戏也称"粤西白戏"。据史料记载，安铺白戏起源于 清朝乾隆年间，由安铺曲龙村民创造，用本地白话演唱，用木偶辅助 表演，通过敲击竹筒作为伴奏的一种“竹筒戏”，后来又经过不断改 良，才成就了今天独具地方特色的白戏。</p>

<p>Anpu Baixi(the local puppet show). Each place has its own unique operas. Although the most famous Chinese top ten classic operas do not include Anpu Baixi, as a small opera, it also has historical characteristics. Anpu Baixi is also called "Western Guangdong Baixi". According to historical records, Anpu Baixi originated in the Emperor Qianlong period of the Qing Dynasty. It was created by the villagers of Qulong in Anpu. The art was sung in local vernacular and performed by puppets manipulation as assistance together with knocking on bamboo pipes as accompaniment, all as called "bamboo pipe play". Today, improvements have been made and resulted in present Baixi with unique local characteristics. 安铺古镇之安铺八音。"八音"是中国古代乐器的统称。"安铺八 音"指的是流传于安铺古镇的一种器乐演奏艺术，距今已有一百多年 的历史。据史料记载，安铺音乐爱好者李六朋对古代"八音"进行创新 改编，采用了本地特色民族乐器包括:手铃、小扣锣、木鱼、清磐、 煞板、横萧、洞萧、高胡、二弦、三弦、等共22 件，共由22 个人各 执一件组成八音队，所演奏的传统曲目有《到春来》《小桃红》《陶 浪沙》《三仙会》等。每年元宵及端午佳节，八音队成员个个穿长衫 马褂，头戴红顶圆礼帽，脚踏薄底便鞋列队上街游演。 Anpu Bayin. "Bayin" is the collective concept for Chinese ancient music performed by various traditional instruments. "Anpu Bayin" refers to the art of instrumental music that has been passed down in the ancient town of Anpu, with a history of more than 100 years. According to historical records, Anpu music enthusiast Li Liupeng has made an innovative adaptation of the ancient "Bayin", by using local national musical instruments including: hand bell, small buckle gong, wooden fish, Qingpan, Shaban, Hengxiao, Dongxiao, Gaohu, Erxian, Sanxian and the like amounting to 22 pieces in total. A group of 22 members will perform one piece each to form a Bayin team. The traditional repertoires are performed include "In Spring", "Little Peach Red", "Tao Langsha", "San Xian Hui" and so on. During annual Lantern Festival and Dragon Boat Festival, the members of the Music Team wear long gowns and jackets, red top hats, and light-soled sandals and parade on the streets. 安铺古镇是广东古老文化传承的基地之一，以上这些文化现象是 当地一道特色亮丽的风景线，更是文化传承史上的一朵奇葩。它们将 为中国传统文化未来走出国门，走向世界，继续迸发无限活力。 The ancient town of Anpu is one of the bases for the inheritance of ancient cultures in Guangdong. The above cultural phenomena come into a beautiful landscape in the local area, making a wonderful work in the history of cultural inheritance. They will continue to burst out infinite vitality for the future of Chinese traditional culture going abroad and to the world. 编译伍后思</p>

<p><strong>2 达濠古城</strong></p>

<p><strong>Dahao Ancient City</strong></p>

<p>Dahao Ancient City 达濠古城位于广东省汕头市濠江区，是全国保留最完好的袖珍古 城。像达濠古城这种保留很完整的古城在全世界也是十分罕见的。 Dahao Ancient City is located in Haojiang District, Shantou City, Guangdong Province. It is the best preserved pocket ancient city in China. Ancient cities with complete preservation like Dahao Ancient City are also very rare in the world. 达濠古城是始建于康熙五十六年（1717 年）面积只有0.014 平 方公里。明清以来，达濠处于优越的地理位置，是汕头一处重要的物 资集散地，也是沿海贸易的战略要地。沿海商贸的发达也吸引来了海 盗，所以在达濠地区经常有海盗出没。沿海居民和商人经常遇到抢劫， 海盗们杀人越货、无恶不作。尽管官府多次派兵围剿海盗，但是收效 甚微。因此，在清朝初期两广总督杨琳就派兵在达濠建城墙。古城建 成后，达濠的治安得到了有效改善。 Dahao Ancient City was built in the 56th year of Kangxi (1717) with an area of only 0.014 square kilometers. Since the Ming and Qing Dynasties, Dahao has been an important material distribution center in Shantou and a strategic location for coastal trade due to its advantageous geographical location. The development of coastal trade has also attracted pirates. Coastal residents and merchants often encounter pirates killing people and looting goods. The government has sent troops many times to</p>

<p>encircle and suppress pirates but with limited success. Therefore, in the early Qing Dynasty, Governor Yang Lin of Guangdong and Guangxi sent troops to build the city wall in Dahao. After the completion of the ancient city, the public security of Dahao has been effectively improved. 达濠古城建成历时一年半，古城四周都有古城墙围着，墙高5 米， 厚1.3 米，四个转角都建有瞭望台。四边的古城墙合起来的长度大约 是494 米。达濠古城有两个城门，一个是达善门，一个是西濠门。达 濠古城隐匿于闹市之中，循着熙熙攘攘的海旁四巷走到尽头，便可到 达西濠门。站在任意一个城门，都可以清楚地望见另一个。东门到西 门之间有一条长约100 米、宽3 米的小路相通，这是小城唯一的街道， 达濠古城的袖珍在此得到完全体现。 It took one and a half years to build Dahao Ancient City. The city is surrounded by walls, which are 5 meters high and 1.3 meters thick, and there are observation decks on all four corners. The total length of the ancient city walls on all four sides is about 494 meters. There are two gates in Dahao Ancient City, one is Dashan Gate and the other is Xihao Gate. Dahao ancient city is hidden in the busy city. Walking along the bustling Haipang Sixiang to the end, you can reach Xihao Gate. Standing at any gate, you can clearly see the other. There is a small road about 100 meters long and 3 meters wide between the east gate and the west gate, which is the only street in the small town. The “pocket” of Dahao Ancient City are fully reflected here. 清朝时期的达濠古城是达濠的政治、军事、经济集为一体的中心， 达濠古城内西面设有“水师左营守备府”，相当于团一级的军事指挥 部；东面设“招宁司巡检署”，即现在的公安局；北面则设“招收盐 场”，相当于现在盐务局，三个机构坐落于东西北三个方向形成“品” 字形布局。民国初期，国民政府又在城内修建了群英、盛德两所小学， 并将招宁司巡检署改为达濠警察所。可惜1939 年日军侵占达濠，达 濠古城被日军侵占，使其成为了一座空城。现如今已经历三个世纪， 风云变幻，波橘云诡，达濠的变化可谓翻天覆地，然而这座古城却完 整保存下来。 In the Qing Dynasty, Dahao ancient city was the center of Dahao's politics, military and economy. In the west of Dahao ancient city, there was a "Left Camp Garrison of Navy", which is equivalent to the military headquarters at the regiment level; in the East, there was the "Inspection Office of Zhaoning Department", which is now the Public Security Bureau; in the north, there was a "Zhaoshou Salt Field", which was equivalent to the salt bureau. These three organizations were located in three directions of East, West and North, resembling the Chinese character "品" in</p>

<p>shape. In the early period of the Republic of China, the national government built two primary schools, Qunying and Shengde, and transformed the Inspection Office of Zhaoning Department into Dahao Police Station. Unfortunately, Dahao was occupied by Japanese army in 1939, which made it an empty city. Now it has gone through three centuries. Dahao has undergone earth-shaking changes. However, it has been completely preserved. 编译郑永彬</p>

<p><strong>3 梅关古道</strong></p>

<p><strong>Mei guan Ancient Road</strong></p>

<p>Mei guan Ancient Road 梅关古道风景区位于广东省韶关市南雄市珠玑镇。梅关古道是我 国保存得最完整的古驿道。它始建于秦朝，古老的道路从梅岭向南北 两边蜿蜒而下，连接北部的江西章水和南部的广东浈水，像一条纽带， 把长江和珠江连接起来。古道宽约6 尺，人行道上整齐地铺有孵化石。 这条路被茂密的灌木丛包围,两边是茂密的树木和山脊。 The Meiguan Ancient Road Scenic Area is located in Zhuji Town, Nanxiong City, Shaoguan City, Guangdong Province. Meiguan Ancient Road is the most complete ancient post road in China, which was built in the Qin Dynasty. It winds down from Meiling to the north and south, connecting Zhangshui in Jiangxi in the north and Zhenshui in Guangdong in the south, which functions as a link connecting the Yangtze River and the Pearl River. The road is about 6 feet wide and is surrounded by dense bushes. Its sidewalk is neatly paved with hatching stones, with dense trees and ridges on both sides. 梅关古道距广东省南雄市梅岭山顶约30 公里。相传梅岭以在战 国时期南下的越人领袖的姓氏命名，因中原处于动荡之中，许多越人 移居岭南。其中一支以梅绢为首的越人，翻山越岭来到大庾岭上，被 岭南风光吸引，在梅岭一带安营扎寨。他们发扬自己勇敢顽强，艰苦 创业的民族传统，这一区域得到了迅速发展。因为梅娟是首率队的先 驱者，后来又因攻破秦王朝而被项王授予十万户候，所以人们称此地 区为梅岭。</p>

<p>The Road is about 30 kilometers away from the top of Meiling Mountain in Nanxiong City, Guangdong Province. According to legend, Meiling was named after the surname of the leader of the Yue people who went south during the Warring States Period. Because central areas in ancient China were in turmoil, many Yue people moved to Lingnan. Among them, a group of Yue people headed by Meijuan overcame the mountains to reach the Dayu Mountain. They were attracted by the scenery of Lingnan and settled in Meiling area. They carried forward their national tradition of being brave, tenacious, and hardworking, which enabled the region to develop rapidly. Because Mei Juan was the pioneer who led the team, and was later awarded Wanhuhou, a Marquis of the highest rank in the Han Dynasty, by King Xiang for defeating the Qin Dynasty, people call this area Meiling. 梅岭是一个古老的战场，也是红军在革命战争中进行过多次战斗 的地方。特别是陈毅同志率领部队在该地区打了三年游击战，面对险 境写了《梅岭三章》，使梅岭更加出名。命名梅岭的另一个原因是梅 花树。梅岭的梅树遍布岭南岭北。每年冬天，梅花盛开，并成为梅花 世界。“庾岭寒梅”让这里成为我国历史上四大探梅胜地之一。 Meiling is an ancient battlefield and also the place where the Red Army fought many times in the Revolutionary War. In particular, Comrade Chen Yi led his troops to fight guerrilla warfare in the area for three years, and wrote "Three Chapters of Meiling" in the face of danger, which made Meiling more famous. Another reason for naming Meiling is because of plum blossom which are all over Lingnan and Lingbei. Every winter, plum blossoms bloom, making Meiling become a world of plum blossoms. Plum blossom of Yuling endows Meiling with the reputation of one of the four major plum blossom resorts in China.</p>

<p>梅岭古道的重要作用使历代政府高度重视古道的建设。梅岭在岭 南经济和文化发展史上发挥了重要作用。自梅岭由越民开发后，它就 成为了中原汉人向南迁徙的立足点。中原文化逐渐在梅岭扎根并传播 到岭南。随着粤汉铁路和雄余高速公路的通车，梅岭古道完成了南北 主要交通通道的历史使命。 Due to the key role of the Meiling Acient Road, all governments since ancient times attach great importance to its construction. Meiling is essential in the history of Lingnan's economic and cultural development. Since it was developed by the Yue people, it has become a foothold for the Han Chinese from central areas in ancient China to migrate south, with their culture gradually taking root in Meiling and spreading to Lingnan. With the opening of the Guangzhou-Wuchang Railway and the Nanxiong-Dayu Expressway, the Meiling Ancient Road has completed its historical mission serving as the main north-south traffic passage. 编译金纯妃</p>

<p><strong>4 水东街</strong></p>

<p><strong>Shuidong Street</strong></p>

<p>Shuidong Street 水东街是惠州市区的发源地，地处东江与西枝江交汇处，总长约 750 米，宽14-18 米，始建于北宋元丰年间，清末民初曾是惠州的商 业旺地，广府文化、潮汕文化和客家文化在此交融。抗日战争时期， 大半条水东街及200 余间店铺被日军付之一炬，后虽经多次重建，但 已不复往日盛况。为了保护惠州文化，惠州市政府十年来致力于复兴 水东街，在街东侧建成了古今合璧的建筑群，同时，也保留部分老街 风貌。 Shuidong Street, the birthplace of Huizhou City, is located at the intersection of Dongjiang River and Xizhijiang River, with a total length of about 750 meters and a width of 14-18 meters. Built in the Yuanfeng period of the Northern Song Dynasty (1078-1085), it was once a thriving commercial center in Huizhou in the late Qing Dynasty and the early Republic of China, as well as an integration of Guangzhou culture, Chaoshan culture and Hakka culture at that time. During the Anti-Japanese War, more than half of Shuidong Street and 200 shops were burned down by the Japanese army. Although it has been rebuilt for many times since then, it is no longer as grand as it used to be. Now in order to protect Huizhou culture, the Huizhou municipal government has been committed to revitalizing Shuidong Street for the past ten years. Now a complex of ancient and modern buildings is built on the east side of the street, while some old street’s features are retained.</p>

<p>老街虽然看似古旧，但是较完整地保留了传统骑楼建筑。两侧房 屋大多为传统中式“金”字型瓦顶，几乎很少采用西式屋顶和壁面。 屋内的楼梯间比较窄小，但门窗上的木雕十分精致。楼墙上有两种管 道，粗的管道是烟管，细的管道是排水管。骑楼特殊的结构使街道两 边形成两条长廊，上层住人，下层是人行道，雨天行人不忧雨。想当 年鼎盛时期，街上开满各式各样的客栈、布店、药店、杂货铺、当铺， 登楼倚窗眺望，东江水面上往来的船只，与水东街道上熙熙攘攘的商 人游客，绘就了一幅近代的《清明上河图》。 The Street looks old, but it retains the traditional arcade-house completely. The shape of most houses’ tile roofs is like traditional Chinese character “gold”, and few western-style roofs and walls are used. The stairwell inside the house is relatively narrow, but the wood carvings on the doors and windows are very delicate. There are two kinds of pipes on the wall: the thick one for smoke vent and the thin one for drainage. The special arcade structure creates two long corridors on both sides of the street. The upper floor is inhabited, while the lower floor is a sidewalk. When it rains, pedestrians need not worry about getting wet. In its heyday, the street was filled with various inns, cloth shops, drugstores, groceries and pawnshops. Looked out from the windows on the upper floor, the street was bustling with merchants and tourists, with boats passing on the water of the Dongjiang River. What a lively picture of “Riverside Scene at Qingming Festival” in modern Huizhou! 改造后的水东新街，由三条纵向平行街道组成，中间一条主街为 商业步行街。街面建筑保留了原水东街中式建筑的风格，但是在女儿 墙、窗楣、壁柱的形式以及栏杆花饰方面做出了些许改变。古城文化 与现代文化相融合，使坐落在东江边的水东街，成为一个充满惠州岭 南文化风味的标识。三条街上都布置了许多供人们休憩的座椅，琳琅 满目的商铺和香气诱人的小吃吸引了越来越多的游客，水东街逐渐成 为新的城市休闲中心。 The renovated Shuidong Street is composed of three longitudinal parallel streets, with a commercial pedestrian street in the middle. The street buildings have retained the original Chinese architectural style, but some changes have been made in the parapet, window lintel, pilasters and railings. The integration of ancient city culture and modern culture makes Shuidong Street, which is located beside Dongjiang River, a symbol full of Lingnan cultural flavor. The three streets are decorated with many seats for people to have a rest. The dazzling shops and tempting snacks attract more and more tourists. Shuidong Street is gradually becoming a new urban leisure center.</p>

<p>值得一提的是，在水东街最东端，坐落着广东六大名楼之一的合 江楼。北宋诗人苏东坡曾在此居住过一年多，并写下了《寓居合江楼》。 脍炙人口的佳句，使得合江楼声名鹊起。合江楼主体墙面为青灰色花 岗岩，给人以清雅肃穆之感。建筑造型为清代官式风格，瓦灰墙白， 柱子为红色，拱梁上绘有彩画。建筑向上逐渐变窄，顶部是重檐攒尖 顶，每层都有环绕挑台。登楼远眺，两江四岸的城市风貌可尽收眼底。 It is worth mentioning that Hejiang Attic, one of the six famous attics in Guangdong, is located at the easternmost end of Shuidong Street. Su Dongpo, a poet in the Northern Song Dynasty, lived here for more than one year and wrote his poem Living in Hejiang Attic. The beautiful lines win universal praise, which makes Hejiang Attic famous. The main wall of Hejiang Attic is turquoise granite, brimming with a sense of elegance and solemnity. The Attic was in the official style of the Qing Dynasty, with gray tiles, white walls, red pillars and color painted arched girders. The Attic gradually narrows upwards, topped by a double eave with a pointed roof, and each floor has a wraparound terrace. Looked out from the Attic terrace, the two rivers and the riverside city landscape can be panoramically viewed. 夜幕降临，水东街人流逐渐增多。站在合江楼旁的码头边上，吹 着略带腥味的河风，看着远处的城市灯火通明，让人不禁也会有和苏 东坡一样的感慨：“不辞长作岭南人”。 As night falls, the number of people in Shuidong Street gradually increases. When you stand on the dock beside the Hejiang Attic, feeling the slightly fishy breeze and looking at the city lights in the distance, you will have the same feeling spontaneously as Su Dongpo: “I’d rather live in Lingnan area forever”. 编译周倩如</p>

<p><strong>5 缚娄国</strong></p>

<p><strong>Fulou</strong></p>

<p>Fulou 惠州位于东江中下游，处在广东三种著名的文化交汇地带，这三 种文化分别是：客家文化、广府文化和潮汕文化，因此惠州的文化非 常丰富。 Located in the middle and lower reaches of the Dongjiang River, Huizhou is at the intersection of three famous cultures in Guangdong, namely: Hakka culture, Guangfu culture and Chaoshan culture. Therefore, Huizhou’s culture is very rich. 缚娄国的遗址是在惠州市博罗县被发现的。博罗于1985 年出土 了七件保存完好的中原地带春秋时期的青铜器和编钟。在后来的1996 年和2000 年，相继出土了大量的陶器、瓷器、玉器、水晶等文物。 这让我们联想到战国末年时期，吕不韦所作的《吕氏春秋》。其中记 载到：“坜汉之南，百越之际, ……缚娄、阳禺、欢兜之国，多无君”。 其中的“缚娄”，因这些出土的文物，而被证实真实存在。 Fulou is an ancient state of ancient China. Its ruins were discovered in Boluo County, Huizou city. In 1985, Boluo unearthed seven well-preserved bronzes and chime bells from the Spring and Autumn Period. In 1996 and 2000, a large number of cultural relics such as pottery, porcelain, jade, crystal were unearthed one after another. This reminds us of Spring and Autumn Annals written by Lu Buwei in the late Warring States Period. It was recorded that: “In the south of Lihan, where Baiyue tribe was settled down, ... Some ancient countries like Fulou, Yangyu and Huandou had no monarch.” Because of these unearthed cultural relics, the "Fulou" has been proved to be a real existence. 古代人认为南方是“蛮荒之地”、“瘴疠之地”，他们认为南方 地区文明落后。唐朝、宋朝这些朝代的君主，贬官都热衷将那些官员 流放到南方地区，如诗圣杜甫，就曾被贬黜到惠州。而缚娄国遗址的 现世，不仅证实了岭南在先秦时期并非“蛮荒之地”，还改写了岭南 的文明史。缚娄国遗址的面世可以让岭南人自豪地说出，岭南地区的 文明并不逊色于中原地区，我们的文明史也可以追溯到三千年前。 Ancient people thought the South was a savage place, and they believed that the southern region was backward in civilization. The monarchs of Tang Dynasty or Song Dynasty were keen to exile the guilty officers to the south, such as the poet Du Fu, who was demoted to Huizhou. However, the present life of the Fulou site not only confirmed that Lingnan was not a savage place in the period of the early Qin Dynasty,</p>

<p>but also rewrote the civilization history of Lingnan. The appearance of Fulou ruins can make Lingnan people proud to say that the civilization of Lingnan area is not inferior to that of the Central Plains, and our civilization history can also be traced back to three thousand years ago. 相传缚娄国是于春秋战国时期由罗氏建立，在公元前337 年后消 失。从出土文物看，缚娄国的制陶业尤为发达。据报道，在博罗梅花 墩、银岗，惠城区官桥瓦窑岭，以及与博罗相邻的广州增城西瓜岭、 龙川登云镇等地，都发现了先秦窑址和陶片。在当时，我们发现东江 流域呈现出一个分布宽广、颇具规模的龙窑群，所以有不少专家和学 者认为，惠州是南方陶器的发源地之一。 It is said that the state of Fulou was founded by Luo during the Spring and Autumn Period and the Warring States Period, and disappeared after 337 BC. From the unearthed cultural relics, the pottery industry in Fulou was particularly developed. It is reported that pre-Qin kiln sites and pottery shards have been found in MeiHuadun and Yingang in Boluo, Wayaoling, Guangqiao, Huicheng District, and Xigualing, Zengcheng, Guangzhou and Dengyun Town, Longchuan, which are adjacent to Boluo. At the time, we found that Dongjiang River basin presents a Longyao group with wide distribution and large scale. So many experts and scholars believed that Huizhou was one of the birthplaces of the southern pottery. 除了制陶技术外，出土的大量青铜器也一一证实着缚娄国曾经的 青铜器制造水平很高。缚娄国遗址的墓葬群，是广东迄今所发现和挖 掘同类墓葬中，数量最多、出土物最精美、品种最丰富的青铜时代墓 葬群。据当时的研究人员研究了解到，这里出土的编钟与中原出土的 同期编钟相似，却又有大量花纹不同的地方，这也说明，在当时，缚</p>

<p>娄国所处的岭南地区已经与中原地区有所联系，并在文化交流的过程 中，又保留着自己独有的文化特色。 In addition to potting technology, a large number of bronzes unearthed also confirmed that the state of Fulou had a high level of bronze manufacturing. The tomb group in the Fulou state site was the largest number of unearthed objects, the most exquisite varieties and the most abundant bronze age tomb group of the same kind found and excavated tombs in Guangdong. Researchers at the time learned that the chimes unearthed here were similar to those unearthed in the Central Plains at the same time, but there were lots of different patterns. It also showed that, at the time, Linnan area where Fulou state was located had been connected with the central plains, and retained their own unique cultural characteristics in the process of cultural exchange. 由于时代久远，缚娄国的兴起发展乃至结束的所有故事，都在历 史的长河中、朝代的更替中消失。缚娄国距今已有三千多年的历史， 这个先秦小国后来发生了什么，因何而起，又因何而灭，我们只能从 古籍和出土的文物中一点点探索。 Due to the long time, all the stories from the rise to the end of Fulou have faded into history. Fulou has a history of more than 3000 years. Why it came into being and why it disappeared? We can only to explore from ancient books and unearthed cultural relics for what then happen to this small pre-Qin ancient country. 缚娄国那开放容纳、择善而从却又不失自己的独特的谦敬态度， 让它的文明更加闪烁，让它的文化更加丰富。缚娄国，虽然它消失 在了历史的长河之中，但它那包容谦逊的精神，却在如今的中国传统 美德中熠熠生辉。 With an open, merit-based, unique and humble attitude, Fulou makes civilization more brighter and its culture more rich. Although Fulou has faded into the long history, its spirit of humility is shining brightly in today’s traditional Chinese virtues. 编译叶婷范杰璇张璐瑶</p>

<p><strong>6 梅庵-千年古刹有梅有佛</strong></p>

<p><strong>Mei'an Temple- An Millennium Ancient Temple</strong></p>

<p>Mei'an Temple- An Millennium Ancient Temple with Plum Blossom and Buddhism 梅庵位于广东肇庆端州区的梅庵岗上，始建于北宋至道二年，最 初是为纪念中国佛教禅宗六祖惠能，在六祖惠能插梅的地方建庵，故 称梅庵。1996 年11 月，经国务院批准，梅庵被列入全国重点文物保 护单位。梅庵，顾名思义，寺院种有梅。传闻唐朝时六祖惠能客居古 端州城西岗时，在山岗上插梅为记。北宋至道二年（公元996 年）， 智远法师来到肇庆，为纪念先师六祖惠能曾在城西小山岗种植梅树， 将那小庵扩建，创建了“梅庵”。梅庵在宋代建成砖木结构的庵堂， 凭着六祖惠能在此插梅而蜚声四海。 Mei'an Temple is located in Mei'angang, Duanzhou District, Zhaoqing, Guangdong Province. It was built in the second year of Zhidao of the Northern Song Dynasty, in memory of Hui Neng, the sixth generation of Chinese Chan Buddhism. It was named Mei'an since it was built in the place where Hui Neng planted plum blossom. In November 1996, with the approval of the State Council, Mei'an Temple was listed as a major national-level protected historical and cultural site. As the name suggests, there are plum blossoms in the temple. It was said that Hui Neng lived in Chengxigang of ancient Duanzhou and planted plum blossom here in Tang Dynasty. In the second year of Zhidao of the Northern Song Dynasty (AD 996), master Zhi Yuan came to Zhaoqing and built the temple to commemorate his teacher Hui Neng</p>

<p>for planting plum blossom in Chengxigang. It was built with brick and wood in the Song Dynasty and has been famous for Hui Neng’s planting plum blossom here. 六祖惠能生性偏爱梅花，外出云游，每到一处都插梅为记。传说 他在回故乡新州途中，曾经客居端州城西一山岗。六祖见山岗后枕北 岭，前俯西江，实在是一处风水宝地，于是便在岗上植梅，并以锡杖 掘井为记。传闻六祖惠能带领众人来到枯井旁，亲自点燃了香烛。焚 香过后，六祖惠能将锡杖高举，往枯井用力一插。锡杖仿佛有裂石开 碑的力量，将堵着泉眼的顽石一插而穿。六祖惠能将锡杖往上一拔， 有股清泉即从洞眼中汩汩喷涌而出，引来了围观的人齐声欢呼。喷涌 出来的泉水十分清沏，很快就将那枯井灌得满满的。住持用瓜瓢将井 中的水酹了一瓢，凑到嘴巴上，尝了一口，异常甘美，荡气回肠，有 如醇酒佳酿。六祖惠能环看四周，说:“这山岗本是土壤肥沃，但由 于以前缺水，引致草木不长，太荒芜了。如今，井里有甘泉涌出，我 们在这岗上多种些花草树木吧。”“好呀！”住持苍老的脸上绽开了 笑容，“但是种什么花木好呢？”六祖惠能说:“岁寒三友，以梅为 首。我看这土壤最适合种植梅花。”众僧听后，都说这山岗上种植梅 花最好。第二天，六祖惠能亲自动手，带领着众僧在庵堂四周种植梅 花，随后返回新州故里，不久便圆寂于家乡。六祖惠能以锡杖引水及 “插梅为标记”的故事一传十，十传百，在民间广泛流传。 Hui Neng had a natural preference for plum blossom. He was keen on planting plum blossom in places where he travelled. It is said that on the way back to his hometown Xinzhou, he once lived on a hill in Chengxi of Duanzhou City. Behind this hill was Beiling Mountain and in front was the West River. He believed that this place was really a valuable one, so he planted plum blossom on the hill and digged a well with a tin rod. He led the people to the dry well and lit incense and candles to worship. After the worship ceremony, he raised the tin rod high, and then thrust it into the dry well. The rod seemed to have the power to crack the stone and open the stele, piercing the stubborn stone blocking the spring eye. After that, Hui Neng pulled out the rod, and suddenly a clear spring gushed out from the cave's eyes, which drew people's cheers in unison. The spouting spring water was very clear and quickly filled the dry well. A buddhist abbott took a scoop of the water in the well with a melon dipper, and tasted it. It was very luscious and refreshing, like a mellow wine. Hui Neng looked around and said, "This hill was originally fertile, but due to lack of water, it used to be barren. Now, there are springs gushing out from the well. So, let's plant some flowers and trees on this hill." The abbot smiled and said, "That’s great! But what should we grow?" “I think this soil is most suitable for growing plum blossom which ranked first among ‘Three Cold-weather Friends’.” After listening, all the monks agreed with him.</p>

<p>The next day, Hui Neng led the monks to plant plum blossoms around the nunnery. After that, he returned to his hometown Xin Zhou, and soon passed away. The story of Huineng using tin rod to divert water and planting plum blossom has been widely spread among the people. 梅庵内现存有大雄宝殿、六祖井、山门和六祖殿等建筑。经过时 间的洗涤，岁月的沉淀，愈发显得沉寂和庄严。透过这小小的梅庵， 我们仿佛又能看见六祖同他的弟子在岗上种植梅树，万树梅花迎风绽 开的情景。每年逢梅花盛开的季节，吸引了各地的旅客来此祭拜。人 们顺着那阵阵的梅花香，追寻禅宗六祖慧能的故事。 In Mei’an Temple, buildings remaining include the Daxiong Hall, Liuzu Well, Shanmen and Liuzu Hall. As time passed, it became more and more silent and solemn. Here, we seem to be able to see Hui Neng and his disciples planting plum blossoms on the hills, and plum blossom trees blooming in the wind. Every year when the plum blossoms are in full bloom, this place attracts tourists from all over the place to worship. Smelling the bursts of plum blossoms, people kept telling and listening to the stories of Hui Neng. 编译徐佳佳</p>

<p><strong>7 叱石观音寺</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chishi Guanyin Temple</strong></p>

<p>Chishi Guanyin Temple 在广东省江门市蓬江区杜阮镇，有一座叱石山，当中有一座叱石 观音庙，山上有许多石羊，并有黄大仙庙，这是源于“叱石成羊”的 传说。 In Duruan Town, Pengjiang District, Jiangmen city, Guangdong Province, there is a Chishi Mountain with a Chishi Guanyin Temple. And there are many stone sheep on the mountain, and a Wong Tai Sin Temple, which comes from the legend of "Shouting to the stone to become the sheep". 黄大仙字初平，有着叱石成羊的传说，根据黄大仙自述，相传黄 大仙在金华山得道升仙，曾经云游到此，随他而来的仙童留下脚迹至 今尚存。这里的寺庙取名叱石，在大雄宝殿左亭命名为小金华。 Wong Tai Sin's another name is Huang Chuping, and he had a legend of "Shouting to the stone to become the sheep". According to Wong Tai Sin, it is said that Wong Tai Sin had become the immortal in Jinhua Mountain. He once wandered here, and the fairy boy who came with him left his footprints that still exist. The temple here was named Chishi and the left pavilion in the Great Buddha’s Hall was named Xiaojinhua. 黄初平原本是一个牧羊童，在浙江金华府城北的金华山牧羊。金 华这个名字，乃是金星婺女争华之地，因此命名。在这座山的北面， 有一座赤松山，黄初平在这里居住。这里很少有游人到来，树木茂盛，</p>

<p>云雾缭绕，树木青翠，高山巍峨，有不少山穴隐藏其中，其中有个山 洞名叫金华，是神道居住的名山胜地三十六洞之一。 Huang Chuping was originally a shepherd boy, shepherding sheep in Jinhua Mountain in the north of Jinhua City, Zhejiang Province. Jinhua is where Venus and Wu Nu competed with each other, so it is named. In the north of the mountain, there is the Chisong Mountain, where Huang Chuping lived. There are few visitors to come here. The trees are lush and green. The lofty mountains was enveloped in mist, and many caves are hidden in the mountain. One of them is called Jinhua, which is one of the thirty-six caves in the famous mountain resort where Taoist lives. 黄初平从小家庭贫困，连煮谷壳都没办法继续生活。黄初平八岁 开始牧羊，一直到十五岁，有幸得到了仙人的指点，仙人带黄初平到 石室之中修炼。在洞中炼药修炼，抛弃了一切凡尘的事，潜心修道， 四十年不食人间烟火，终于悟得修道玄机。 Huang Chuping grew up in a poverty and could not even continue to live by cooking chaff. Huang Chuping began herding sheep at the age of eight. Until he was fifteen, he was fortunate to get the guidance from an immortal, who took him to a stone room for practice. He practiced and refined medicine in the cave, abandoning all worldly things. Concentrating on the cultivation of Taoism for forty years, he finally realized the mystery of Taoism. 黄初平自十五岁那年出去放羊后杳无音讯，他的哥哥黄初起一直 寻找他。直到四十多年后，在赶集时刚好遇到了擅长占卜的道士，便 询问这位道人黄初平的下落。道士说：“金华山中有一个牧羊儿，不 知是否是初平。”黄初起终于在金华山的一个山洞中找到了容颜未改 的黄初平，这才兄弟相见。 Huang Chuqi, Huang Chuping's big brother, had been looking for Chuping since he went out to graze sheep at the age of 15 and had not been heard of. It was not until more than forty years later that he met a Taoist who was good at divination when he went to the fair and asked him the whereabouts of Huang Chuping. The Taoist said, “There is a shepherd boy in Jinhua mountain. I don't know if it is him.” Huang Chuqi finally found Huang Chuping, whose appearance did not change. The brothers met in a cave of Jinhua Mountain. 黄初起问起弟弟羊群的下落，黄初平说在山的东面，一起去看看。 但是只见白石遍布，黄初起说哪里有羊？黄初平笑道：“羊都在，你 看不见”。然后便大叫：“叱！叱！羊起！”满山白石应声而起，都 变成了羊。看得黄初起目瞪口呆，这才相信弟弟得道。黄初起也因此 开始修炼，久而久之，兄弟二人皆成仙，合称二黄君。黄大仙本来姓</p>

<p>黄，名叫初平，是东晋丹溪人，因为隐居在赤松山，所以他的名号叫 赤松仙子，和之前张良的赤松仙子有所不同。 Huang Chuqi asked his brother the whereabouts of the sheep, Huang Chuping said that they were in the east of the mountain. But seeing white stones everywhere, Huang Chuqi said, "Where are the sheep?" Huang Chuping laughed and said, "The sheep are here. You can't see them." Then he shouted out, "Chi! Chi! Get up!" In response, the mountain white stones rose and turned into sheep. Huang Chuqi was dumbfounded, then he believed his brother realized the mystery in practicing. As a result, Huang Chuqi began to practice. Over time, the two brothers both became immortals, collectively known as the Erhuangjun. Wong Tai Sin was originally named Huang Chuping. He was from Danxi in the Eastern Jin Dynasty. Because he lived in seclusion in the Chisong Mountain, he was called Chisong Fairy, which was different from Zhang Liang's Chisong Fairy. 编译李咏诗</p>

<p><strong>8 南澳宋井</strong></p>

<p><strong>Nan’ao Songjing</strong></p>

<p>Nan’ao Songjing “忽逢桃花林，夹岸数百步”，每每去到那里总会让我想起陶渊 明的著作《桃花源记》，那里没有桃花，望眼欲穿的是一片汪洋大海， 有山有树有礁石，还有一口悠久历史的宋井。 “A man suddenly came to a grove of peach blossom forest. It lined both banks for several hundred paces.” Every time going to Nan’ao Island always reminds me of Tao Yuanming's A Travel of Peach Blossom Source. There is no peach blossom but a vast sea with hills, trees and reef. There is also a well called Songjing with long history which created in Song Dynasty. 小时候，最爱听奶奶讲故事。每每睡不着时，奶奶总会给我讲海 的那边，南澳的故事。南澳是隶属于汕头的海岛。家乡和海岛虽然不 远，但是隔了一片海。 When I was young, I loved to listen to my grandmother telling stories. Whenever I couldn't fall asleep, my grandmother would always tell me the Nan’ao Island stories. Nan’ao Island belongs to Shantou. My hometown is only a sea away from the island. 奶奶曾说，在很久以前，曾祖母跟着几个姐妹乘船去过一次。她 说，到那里之后，有很多景象让她感到惊奇。首先是那里清澈见底的 海水，以及小山拥簇的地貌。其次是被当地一些人的着装所震惊，在 那个人年代里，当地人还有一些穿着清朝的服饰，留着小辫子。曾祖 母跟着几个姐妹走得匆忙，去的时候忘记带水了，于是乎找了一位当 地的大姐，这位大姐把她们带到了一口井前面，并告诉她那口井叫做 宋井。那个时候听奶奶说到这里的时候，我总会发出疑问，“海岛里 的井水会是咸的吗？”这时候奶奶都会笑着说先睡觉明天告诉你，然 而我等到好久都没知道答案。 My grandmother once said that a long time ago, great-grandmother went on a boat with some of her sisters. She said that after arriving there, she was amazed by many sights. The first was the clear water and the hilly landscape. The second was the locals dress. At that time, some local people still wore Qing dynasty costumes and kept pigtails. My great-grandmother was in such a hurry with her sisters that she had forgotten to bring water, so she found a local elder sister, who took them to a well and told her that it was called Songjing. When I heard grandma said that, I would always ask her, “Will the well in the island be salty?” At this time grandma would smile and ask me to sleep. She would tell me the answer the next day. But I waited for a long</p>

<p>time and didn’t get the answer. 就在2015 年的时候，南澳大桥建成通车。我抱着强烈的好奇心 前往，第一次踏入那里时，迎面吹来的是一阵泛着大海味道的海风。 这时候的南澳，已经和奶奶口中描述的有很大的不同了。现代化建筑 已经很多，俨然就是一个热门的旅游海岛了，虽然知道那宋井的井水 肯定是淡水，但还是想去那里看看。 The Nan’ao Bridge was completed and opened to traffic in 2015. I went there with a strong curiosity. After I arrived there, I was greeted by a sea breeze. At this time, Nan’ao has been very different from what grandma described. There are a lot of modern buildings, and it seems to be a popular tourist island. Although I know that the well water of Songjing must be fresh water, I still want to have a look. 当我走到宋井旁边时，看到了井边的那块碑，才明白了其名字以 及它的历史意义。原来那是南宋末年，元兵南下，南宋王朝撤离京城 临安后，不断南逃，在福州被拥立为皇帝。以后又从海路南撤，在大 将张世杰和礼部侍郎陆秀夫等护送下来到了南澳，就住在现在的澳前 村一带。据说当时为饮用水之需，他们在澳前村一带挖了三口井，一 为龙井，专供皇帝饮用；一为虎井，供大臣饮用；一为马井，供随从 人员和士兵饮用。天长日久，三口井都被潮水和沙子掩盖了，有时又 会显露出来。现在看到的这口是马井，其余两个还未被发现。 When I walked to Songjing, I saw the tablet beside the well and understood its name and its historical significance. It turned out that in the late years of the Southern Song Dynasty, Yuan troops moved southward. After the Southern Song withdrew</p>

<p>from the capital Lin’an, they kept fleeing south and were proclaimed emperor in Fuzhou. Later, he withdrew from the south of the sea road and was escorted down to Nan’ao by General Zhang Shijie and Lu Xiufu of the ceremony department assistant minister. He lived in the current Aoqian village. It is said that at that time, they dug three wells in the vicinity of Aoqian Village for drinking water. One was called Longjing (Dragon Well), dedicated to the emperor; One was called Hujing (Tiger Well) for the minister, and the other was called Majing (Horse Well) for the attendants and soldiers. Over time, all three wells were covered by the tide and sand, sometimes revealing themselves again. Songjing, which we see now, is the Majing (Horse Well). The other two have not been discovered yet. 宋井之奇，在于700 多年来，时隐时现。古井虽离波浪滔滔的大 海仅10 多米，常被海潮掩没，但是潮退之后井水不带咸味，而且长 年清泉不绝，水质清纯甘甜，久藏而不变质，故被称为“神奇宋井”。 The wonder of Songjing lies in the fact that it disappears from time to time for over 700 years. Although the ancient well is only more than 10 meters away from the surging sea and is often covered by the tide, the water in the well does not taste salty after the tide ebb, and the water is pure and sweet all the year round. The water has been stored for a long time without going bad, so it is called "Magic Songjing". 自那之后，还是会常常光顾南澳岛，也许是想去看那口经历沧桑 的马井，也许是想去找找那里的虎井和龙井的踪迹，也许这就是历史 的神奇魅力吧！ Since then, I still often visit Nan’ao Island. Perhaps I want to see the vicissitudes of Majing (Horse Well), or perhaps I want to look for the traces of Hujing (Tiger Well) and Longjing (Dragon Well) there. This is the magic charm of history! 编译谢育菲徐嘉颖熊曼芳</p>

<p><strong>9 榄邑史文</strong></p>

<p><strong>History of Siulam</strong></p>

<p>History of Siulam 小榄古时占珠江口的几个小岛屿，因地方的小山丘形似橄榄而得 名。虽然地方不大，但拥有着源远流长的人文历史，更少不了自身独 具特色的传统文化。 Xiaolan occupied several small islands at the mouth of the Pearl River in ancient times, and was named by the small hills in the area resembling olives. Although the place is not large, it has a long history of humanities, and inevitably its own unique traditional culture. 小榄的发迹史亦是一部珠江三角洲的迁民史，这里的姓氏文化也 由此变化发展。由于宋元明清的人民迁居、聚居，人口大大发展，并 逐渐形成较大规模聚落，带来了丰富的传统文化与民俗，如狮子舞、 咸水歌、木偶戏等如今成为小榄非物质文化遗产，很多民间故事更是 流传至今，不少富有传奇色彩，伴随着小榄粤语的乡音，口口相传。 The history of Xiaolan’s rise is a history of migration in the Pearl River Delta, and the surname culture here has also changed and developed accordingly. Due to the migration and settlement of people in Song, Yuan, Ming and Qing Dynasties, the population has greatly developed and gradually formed large-scale settlements, bringing rich traditional culture and folklore, such as lion dance, salt water song, puppet show, etc., which have now become Xiaolan intangible cultural heritage. Many folk tales have been passed down by word of mouth from ancient to present, and many of them are legendary, accompanied by the local accent of Xiaolan Cantonese. 小榄族姓众多，来自四面八方，又在明清两代科举鼎盛时期官宦 辈出，因此逐渐形成了权势较大的姓氏，尤以何、李、麦三姓最为突 出，如官至明朝大学士的何吾驺、官至南京礼部尚书的李孙宸都声名 在外。历史上，慈恩坊（今中大街）、西闸坊（葵溪）多为何姓聚居； 泰宁是李氏聚居地；滘口又称“麦局”，多麦姓聚居；罗涌因罗姓而 得名，更有起了姓氏宗祠来祭拜先祖，成了地方独具特色的景点，这 些族姓势力也对小榄的演变、发展产生了潜移默化的影响。 The Xiaolan family name is numerous from all directions. During the heyday of the imperial examinations in the Ming and Qing dynasties, many officials came out. As a result, they gradually formed more powerful family name, especially the three most prominent He, Li, and Mai, such as He Wuzhu, a grand secretary of Ming</p>

<p>Dynasty, and Li Sunchen, an official to the Nanjing Rites Department. In history, Ci’enfang (now Zhongda Street) and Xizhafang (Kuixi) are the place where He family live most. Taining is the place where the Li family live; Jiaokou is also known as "Mai Ju", with the surname Mai inhabited; Luo Yong got its name from Luo family name, and ancestral halls were used to pay homage to the ancestors, which became unique local attractions. These family name forces also had a subtle influence on the development and evolution of Xiaolan. 小榄是中国菊花艺术文化之乡,菊花种植乃至餐饮名菜都成就了 小榄“菊城”的美称。菊花是小榄的精神之根，最早有香山县的诗社 泰宁诗社在榄乡诞生，随后小榄的诗词坊社甚至跟小榄菊花会文化的 诞生有所关联，古因榄邑诗社发展，文人墨客偏好以文会友，每逢菊 开时节，好菊者聚集社所，饮酒赋诗，访探题咏，称为“菊社”，菊 社在清乾隆年间得到扩大，便命名为“甲戌菊花大会”。至今，菊花 大会都以1 年一小展、3 年一展、10 年一中展、60 年一大展的模式 展出，更相传有逃难的胡妃、苏妃在小榄种植菊花的传说，如今听来 十分有趣。 Xiaolan is the hometown of chrysanthemum art culture China. Chrysanthemum planting and even famous catering have made Xiaolan the reputation of "Chrysanthemum City". The chrysanthemum is the root of the spirit of Xiaolan. The first poetry society of Xiangshan County, Taining Poetry Society, was born in Lanxiang. Later, the poetry workshop of Xiaolan was even related to the birth of Xiaolan Chrysanthemum Society culture. During the development of the society, literati prefer to make friends. Every time when the chrysanthemum blooms, the good chrysanthemums gather in the community, drink wine, write poems, and visit the inscriptions. It is called "the chrysanthemum society". The chrysanthemum society was expanded during the Qianlong period of the Qing Dynasty and named is the</p>

<p>"Jiaxu Chrysanthemum Conference". So far, the Chrysanthemum Conference has been exhibited in the mode of one small exhibition in one year, one exhibition in three years, one mid-term exhibition in ten years, and one large exhibition in 60 years. According to legend, there are legends of concubine Hu and Concubine Su who planted chrysanthemums in Xiaolan, which now sounds very interesting. 除此之外，关于菊花少不得是它所衍生的一系列美食，有将菊花 瓣拌上沙糖直接食用，清香爽口，回味无穷;也有将菊花瓣直接倒入 米酒中浸泡成为菊花酒；也有将菊花撒在水榄八宝饭上，成为清香扑 鼻的菊花美食；同时，也有将菊花做成菊花糠。在小榄的饮食习俗中， 以菊花鱼球最有代表性。其中，公记、中记、罗富记三家所做的菊花 鱼球闻名省港澳，是当地极有影响力的风味食品之一。 In addition, the chrysanthemum must be a series of delicacies derived from it. There are chrysanthemum petals mixed with sugar and eaten directly, which is refreshing and has an endless aftertaste. Some chrysanthemum petals are directly poured into rice wine and soaked to become chrysanthemum wine; The chrysanthemums are sprinkled on the Chinese rice pudding to become a fragrant chrysanthemum food; At the same time, chrysanthemums are also made into chrysanthemum chaff. Among the eating customs of Xiaolan, chrysanthemum fish ball is the most representative. Among them, the chrysanthemum fish balls made by Gongji, Zhongji and Luo Fuji are well-known in Hong Kong and Macao, and they are one of the most influential local flavor foods. 庄子曰：水不及也不厚，其负大舟也无力，一个地方都需要有深 厚的历史文化底蕴发展起来，而小榄还有很多榄邑山水、历史痕迹和 生动故事，正静静躺在如今的某个角落，等待着我们去挖掘。 Zhuang Zi said: “The water is neither thick nor strong, nor is it strong enough to carry a big boat.” Any place needs to develop with profound historical and cultural heritage. Xiaolan, however, still has many landscapes, historical traces and vivid stories lying quietly in some corner of today, waiting for us to dig. 编译麦淑婷</p>

<p><strong>10 潮绣</strong></p>

<p><strong>Chaozhou Embroidery</strong></p>

<p>Chaozhou Embroidery 潮绣（潮州刺绣）与广绣（广州刺绣）合称粤绣，与苏州的苏绣、 湖南的湘绣、四川的蜀绣并称为中国四大名绣。潮绣古色古香，繁花 似锦，栩栩如生，令人叹为观止。 Chaozhou embroidery and Guangzhou embroidery are collectively called Guangdong embroidery, known as the four famous embroideries in China together with Suzhou embroidery, Hunan embroidery and Sichuan embroidery. With its antique, colorful and lifelike beauty, Chaozhou embroidery never fails to impress. 19 世纪的英国艺术家波西尔曾在《中国美术》一书中写道:“中 国人长于刺绣花鸟，而广东人于此技术尤为专长”。可见，中国潮绣 在当时便已传入欧洲并产生了巨大影响。 “The Chinese are good at embroidering flowers and birds, and the Cantonese are especially good at this technique.” Stephen Wootton Bushell (1844-1908), a British artist in the 19th century, wrote in his book Chinese Art. It can be seen that Chaozhou embroidery had been introduced into Europe at that time and had a great influence. 潮绣起源于唐代，明清时期形成鲜明的风格。到了清朝乾隆年间， 潮州的绣庄、绣坊比比皆是，潮州西门外天地坛、布梳街和开元寺附 近就有绣庄20 多家。绣品出口到新加坡、泰国和马来西亚，占领了 南洋市场，特别是具有浓厚地方民俗特色的厅堂，佛教寺庙摆设的绣 品更是供不应求。 According to historical records, Chaozhou embroidery originated in the Tang Dynasty (608-907), and formed its distinctive style in the Ming and Qing dynasties (1368-1912). During the reign of Emperor Qianlong (1736-1795) of the Qing Dynasty, embroidery shops and workshops could be found everywhere in Chaozhou. More than 20 shops were set up near Tianditan Street, Bushu Street and Kaiyuan Temple. Chaozhou embroidery were exported to Singapore, Thailand and Malaysia, and occupied the Southeast Asia market. It was especially popular in those countries’ halls with strong local folk characteristics, and was even in short supply in the Buddhist temples. 到了上世纪六七十年代，潮绣发展到全盛时期，各类刺绣工人遍 布城镇和村庄，从业人员多达10 万人，产值过亿。村中的幼童从小</p>

<p>耳濡目染，在闲时也跟着父母学习潮绣技艺。与此同时，平绣和珠绣 得到长足发展，他们轻松掌握了珠绣技艺，为潮州成为世界上最大的 珠绣晚礼服和婚纱生产地做出了贡献。 In the 1960s and 1970s, Chaozhou embroidery reached its heyday. As many as 100,000 embroiders of all kinds were found in towns and villages, with an output value of over 100 million yuan. Children in the villages learned craftsmanship from their elders, mastering difficult embroidery skills. At the same time, flat embroidery and bead embroidery have been greatly developed. Embroiders easily mastered the bead embroidery skills and made a contribution to Chaozhou becoming the largest production center of beaded evening dresses and wedding dresses in the world. 潮绣根据刺绣材料不同，可分为绒绣、线绣、金银线绣、金绒混 合绣四大类：在各种丝、绸、缎上，以平绣针法用丝绒绣出飞禽鸟兽、 吉祥器物，用作画片、挂屏的绒绣；纯用丝线平面绣制而成的线绣； 针法复杂，且拥有其他绣种所没有的“二针企鳞”针法的钉金绣，又 称金银线绣；以及以金银线为主，绒线为辅的金绒混合绣。 According to embroidery materials, Chaozhou embroidery is divided into four categories: woolen embroidery, silk thread embroidery, gold and silver thread embroidery, and gold velvet embroidery. Woolen embroidery is mostly used for pictures and wall hangings, where all kinds of birds, animals, and auspicious utensils are flat embroidered on various silks and satins with woolen. Silk thread embroidery is flat embroidered purely with silk thread. Gold and silver thread embroidery is quite complicate, and has a unique embroidery technique. Gold velvet embroidery mainly uses gold and silver thread, supplemented by woolen.</p>

<p>而从刺绣技艺来看，潮绣设计严谨,色彩华丽，在中国刺绣中独 具一格。潮绣针法繁多，纹理清晰，色彩浓艳，装饰性强，尤其是富 有浮雕效果的垫高绣法，与其它绣法有很大区别。而金碧辉煌、粗犷 雄浑的钉金绣也令人称道。潮绣常以人物、龙凤、动物、花卉等作为 题材，构图饱满匀称，色彩热烈喜庆，适合用于庙堂会所的装饰和喜 庆。 In terms of embroidery skills, Chaozhou embroidery is unique among Chinese embroideries in its rigorous design and gorgeous colors. There are many embroidering skills in Chaozhou embroidery, presenting an effect of clear textures, rich colors, and strong decoration. Among all the skills, the embossed one is especially different for its stereoscopic effect. What’s more, its gold and silver thread embroidery is magnificent, bold and powerful, which is also commendable. Chaozhou embroidery often uses subjects such as characters, dragons and phoenixes, animals and flowers, creating a full and well-proportioned composition, as well as warm and festive colors. It is quite suitable for decoration and celebration in temples and halls. 自上世纪50 年代以来，潮绣一直是我国领导人赠送各国元首和 国际友人的重要礼品。国家十分重视潮绣的保护与传承，2006 年， 潮绣经国务院批准被列入第一批国家级非物质文化遗产名录。 Since 1950s, Chaozhou embroidery has become an important gift given by Chinese leaders to other heads of states and international friends. Our country attaches great importance to the protection and inheritance of Chaozhou embroidery. In 2006, it was approved by the State Council to be listed in the first batch of national intangible cultural heritage. 编译张力天王茜朱敏怡</p>

<p><strong>11 忠信花灯</strong></p>

<p><strong>Zhongxin Festive Lantern</strong></p>

<p>Zhongxin Festive Lantern 河源是岭南文化发祥地之一，位于广东省东北部沿海与山区的交 界处，是中国为数不多的纯客家地区。自秦置县始，“开发岭南第一 功臣”的南越王赵佗在此传播中原文化。2000 多年中原文化与百越 文化的交融积淀,让河源既体现出其他地区客家族群的文化特征，又 建立起自身独特的民俗特点。 Heyuan City, one of the cradles of Lingnan culture, is also one of the few pure Hakka areas in China. It is located at the border between the northeast coast and the mountainous area in Guangdong Province. It is said that Zhao Tuo (240 BC-137 BC), the first king of Nanyue Kingdom (Today’s Lingnan area) in the late Qin Dynasty, spread the Central Plains culture here. So he is respected as “the first hero of developing Lingnan”. The integration of Central Plains culture and Baiyue culture over the past 2000 years has made Heyuan not only have the cultural characteristics of Hakka ethnic groups in other regions, but also establish its own unique folk characteristics. 客家人的生活受山区环境影响，形成了一些独特的客家习俗，如 “上灯”。“上灯”，即“添丁”，客家人为上一年出生的男孩举行 庆贺灯会。上灯的时间一般为农历正月十一至十五之间，主家做或买 一个考究的花灯挂在自家祖堂上，点燃花灯，把它升至厅堂三分之一 的高度，以示添子添丁。 Hakka people’s life is mainly affected by the mountainous environment, and has formed some unique customs, for example, Hakka Lantern Festival. In Hakka dialect, “lantern” sounds the same as “boy”, so Hakka family should hold a lantern show to celebrate the baby boy born the previous year. The festival is usually hosted from the 11th to 15th day of the first lunar month. The family makes or buys an elegant festive lantern to hang on their ancestral hall, then lights and raises the lantern to one third of the height of the hall as a symbol of one more boy born in the family. 花灯工艺令人震撼！我国的花灯相传起于汉代，兴于唐宋，至今 已有2000 多年历史，是中华民族优秀的文化遗产。客家花灯是中国 元宵花灯的一个分支，忠信花灯是这一分支上的闪亮明珠。忠信花灯 节是广东省河源市连平县忠信镇地区独特的节日，已有600 多年历 史。按照忠信的传统风俗，每年正月初九，当地人家当年生了男孩就 要在祠堂里挂起花灯庆祝，以告知祖先和乡亲。吊灯仪式一般有放灯</p>

<p>绳、选灯、迎灯、上灯、暖灯、化灯6 道程序，其间还有客家锣鼓、 舞龙狮、祭祖、饮灯酒等热闹场景。吊一盏花灯就是一次盛会。 The handicraft of lantern is really amazing! Originating in the Han Dynasty (202 BC-220 AD) and flourishing in the Tang and Song Dynasties (618-1279), Chinese lantern has a history of more than 2,000 years and is an excellent cultural heritage of the Chinese nation. Hakka festive lantern is a branch of the Chinese Lantern Festival, and Zhongxin festive lantern is the shining pearl of this branch. Zhongxin festive lantern is from Zhongxin Town, Lianping County, Heyuan City, Guangdong Province, which is a unique local festival with a history of more than 600 years. According to the traditional custom of Zhongxin Town, local people should hang lanterns in their ancestral hall on the ninth day of the first lunar month to celebrate the birth of a boy, so as to let their ancestors and villagers know. The ceremony generally consists of 6 procedures: dropping the lantern cord, selecting the lantern, welcoming the lantern, hanging the lantern, lighting the lantern, and ending. There are also Hakka drums and gongs, dragon and lion dances, worship, drinking festive wine and other lively scenes. Hanging a lantern is a grand occasion. 作为非物质文化遗产，忠信花灯综合了多种传统艺术形式，主要 体现在编织、印花、剪、刻、裱、装饰等一系列制作工艺上。忠信花 灯造型独特，其结构从上到下分为灯盖、灯身、灯裙，从里到外一般 有二至四层，规格大者直径有12 米，小的也有40 厘米。花灯大多用 竹编骨架，有四角、六角、八角、十二角。忠信花灯的灯裙最为特别， 由各种各样的花案彩色灯带组成，外用彩色灯带点缀，灯带上有各种</p>

<p>各样的花案；灯内装置各种形象画片旋转流动，形成“走马灯”动感。 忠信花灯的制作，凝聚了忠信人民在地方手工艺上的卓著成就，寄寓 了劳动人民百业兴旺、丰衣足食的美好愿望和祈盼。 As an intangible cultural heritage, Zhongxin festive Lantern has integrated a variety of traditional art forms, which are mainly embodied in its weaving, printing, cutting, engraving, mounting, decorating and a series of production techniques. It has a unique shape, divided into lantern cover, body and skirt from top to bottom, and has two to four layers from inside to outside. The diameter of the large lantern is 12 meters and the small one is 40 centimeters. Most lanterns are made of bamboo, with four, six, eight, or twelve corners. The lantern skirt is the most special, which is decorated with a variety of flower-painted colorful light belts. All kinds of images and pictures are installed in the lantern to rotate and flow as a dynamic “walking lantern”. The production of Zhongxin lanterns embodies the outstanding achievements in local handicrafts of Zhongxin people, and contains working people’s good wishes for prosperity. 忠信花灯不仅蕴含了丰富的人文精神，也展现了宗族凝聚力，同 时也繁荣了客家经济。政府每两年或三年举办一次花灯节，让花灯走 出祠堂。忠信镇周边有10 多个花灯制作点，其中以忠信镇上坣村上 寮屋最为出名，有“花灯村”之称。该村全村人都是花灯制作传承人， 故此，2017 年6 月，该村被连平县文广新局审核认定为“连平县忠 信花灯上寮屋制作基地”。 Zhongxin lantern not only implies rich humanistic spirit, but also shows the clan cohesion. At the same time, the Hakka economy is also promoted to prosperity. Every two or three years, the government may hold a Lantern Festival to make the lantern not the exclusive for ancestral hall. Around Zhongxin Town, there are more than 10 lantern production sites. Among which Shangliao Community of Shangtang Village in Zhongxin Town is the most famous, known as “Lantern Village”. All the villagers here are inheritors of lantern making. Therefore in June 2017, the village was approved as the Zhongxin Festive Lantern Production Base by the county authority. 花灯灿烂逢盛世，用忠信花灯这条金线串起一系列客家民俗民 风，让花灯文化、客家文化不断传承。 Lanterns are always bright and prosperous. Zhongxin lantern is like a guide to lead our lantern culture and Hakka culture to be inherited and passed down forever. 编译赖庚午</p>

<p><strong>12 荣昌折扇</strong></p>

<p><strong>Rongchang Folding Fan</strong></p>

<p>Rongchang Folding Fan 荣昌折扇，又称“折股扇”，是一种民间的手工艺术品，也是一 种装饰性的美术品。2019 年11 月，《国家级非物质文化遗产代表性 项目保护单位名单》公布，重庆市荣昌区文化馆获得荣昌折扇项目 保护单位资格。 Rongchang Folding Fan, also named Folding Fan, is a folk handicraft and decorative art. In November 2019, the List of National Intangible Cultural Heritage Representative Projects Protection Units was published, and the Cultural Center of Rongchang District, Chongqing City was granted the protection unit of Rongchang Folding Fan project. 中国折扇制作历史久远，是民族文化的一个组成部分，它与竹文 化、佛教文化有着密切关系，历来中国都有制扇王国之称。荣昌折扇 与苏州绢绸扇、杭州书画扇并称为“中国三大名扇”。重庆市荣昌 县四宝之一的荣昌折扇，经历代艺人刻苦钻研、精工创制，逐步发展 成为具有独特风格的中国传统工艺品，其精雅宜士人，其华灿宜艳女。 折扇虽是日用小商品，但独具收则折叠，用则撒开，折撒自如，携带 方便的特点。 A long history has seen the making of Chinese folding fan, which is a component of national culture and has a close relationship with bamboo culture and Buddhist culture. China has always been known as the kingdom of fan-making. Rongchang Folding Fan, Suzhou Silk Fan and Hangzhou Calligraphy and Painting Fan are the three famous fans in China. As one of the four treasures of Rongchang County, Chongqing City, Rongchang Folding Fan has gradually developed into a unique traditional Chinese handicraft with artists’ assiduous study and elaboration. This exquisite and gorgeous fan is suitable for both ladies and gentlemen. Small daily commodity as it is, the folding fan has integrate characteristics of folding, spreading, easy-carrying. 荣昌折扇看起来并不复杂，但制作起来却工序繁多。据师傅介绍， 荣昌折扇制作大致可以分为16 个工段、145 个操作工序，而且每一 个工段都有自己的行会，比如以写画工种组成的丹青会、以糊白扇页 组成的熏风会、以削楠竹扇骨为主的青山会、以漆刻雕工组成的三仙 会等。荣昌折扇造型轻盈灵巧，线条外圆内方，明快流畅;其选料考 究，制作精细，工艺精湛，是实用与工艺相结合的日用佳品。由于品</p>

<p>种齐全，花色繁多，高、中、低档产品均有，可谓男女老少皆宜，雅 俗共赏，深受各阶层人士的喜爱。 It is seemingly uncomplex, yet the making process of Rongchang Folding Fan is complicated, which can be generally divided into 16 stages and 145 operating sequences, according to the worker. Each society is responsible for one stage. For instance, Danqing Society is responsible for writing and painting, Xunfeng Society for pasting the white page, Qingshan Society mainly for cutting ribs made of bamboos , Sanxian Society for lacquering and carving, and so forth. Dexterity and lightness, round outside and square inside, smooth lines, selected materials, elaborate and exquisite workmanship make Rongchang Folding Fan a fine daily goods; its variety and diversity make it suitable for and well welcomed among all ages and stages. 荣昌折扇，从农耕时代走向信息时代，历经400 多年悠悠历史。 据《荣昌县志》记载，折扇古称聚头扇，又名卷扇。根据历史记载是 唐朝日本遣唐使朝贺皇帝唐太宗以贡品入国，当时被称为倭扇。宋代 倭扇开始在官家和民间广泛出现，并规模生产，而真正全面被百姓所 喜欢和普及是明朝。 Four hundred years have witnessed the development of Rongchang Folding Fan from the agrarian age to the information age. According to the Records of Rongchang County, Folding Fan was called Head-folding Fan, also Scrolling Fan. It is recorded that in the Tang Dynasty, Kentoushi presented tribute to Emperor Taizong of Tang, which was called Japanese Fan. In the Song Dynasty, The Japanese Fan was widely appeared in the governmental and nongovernmental places and . and the folk, and produced on a large scale. Actually, it was in the Ming Dynasty that the Japanese</p>

<p>fan was popularized among the common people. 中国四大名扇--荣昌折扇(巴蜀扇)，始于1551 年明代嘉靖年间， 明末已成为贡品入朝。如今，荣昌折扇不仅成了国家级非物质文化遗 产，也是重庆著名的文化名片，具有极大的艺术价值、欣赏价值和收 藏价值。2002 年四月，荣昌折扇公司440 余把雕刻书画扇进入亚洲 议会和平协会第三界重庆年会，作为专用礼品赠送参会外宾。其消费 功能除具有折扇的普通功能外，还普遍用于广告载体、礼品赠送、纪 念品发放、强身健体、文艺演出、室内装饰、艺术品收藏等消费领域。 多年来，其产品不仅销往全国各地，而且还先后出口印度、泰国、缅 甸、日本等国家，深受中外顾客的厚爱。 Rongchang Folding Fan (Bashu Fan), as one of the four most famous fans in China, started in 1551 during the years of Jiajing in Ming Dynasty and became a tribute to the court at the end of the Ming Dynasty. Now, it, with great value for art, appreciation and collection, has not only become a national intangible cultural heritage, but also a famous cultural identity of Chongqing. In April 2002, more than 440 carved calligraphy and painting fans from Rongchang Folding Fan Company were contributed to third chongqing annual conference of the AAPP, being the special gift to foreign guests. In addition to being consumed for the common functions of folding fans, Rongchang Folding Fan is also widely used as advertising carriers, gifts, souvenirs, or for body building, artistic performance, interior decoration, art collecting and other consumption fields. Over the years, their products are not only sold to the places all over the country, but also exported to India, Thailand, Myanmar, Japan and other countries, and deeply loved by Chinese and foreign customers. 近几十年，荣昌折扇生产又有长足发展，已有正棕、全楠、皮底、 硬青、串子、全棕、檀香、绸面、羽毛、胶质等345 个品种，并由写 画派生出印花折扇，为旅游、文艺等部门广泛采用。虽然荣昌折扇的 纳凉效果比不上风扇与空调，但是其便携性与传统文化的艺术价值却 是难以替代。 In recent decades, Rongchang Folding Fan has made great progress in production, including 345 material, such as palm, pure bamboo, leather bottom, hard green, string seed, pure coir, sandalwood, silk, feather, gum, etc., and there are writing and painting school for printing folding fans, widely used by tourism, art or other departments. Although the cooling effect of Rongchang folding fan is not as good as that of fans and air conditioners, its portability and artistic value of traditional culture cannot be replaced. 编译钟雅婷</p>

<p><strong>13 惠州文化“三宝”</strong></p>

<p><strong>The"ThreeTreasures"ofHuizhouCulture</strong></p>

<p>The"ThreeTreasures"ofHuizhouCulture 作为国家历史文化名城，惠州在隋唐已是“粤东重镇”，一直是 东江流域的政治、经济、军事、文化中心，素有“岭南名郡”、“粤 东门户”、“半城山色半城湖”之称。惠州是客家人最重要聚居地和 集散地之一，且由于海外华人、港澳台民众人数是客家四州之首，因 此惠州也被称为客家侨都。本篇主要讲述的有惠州民间采风、客家地 方剧的汉剧和客家美食的“东江名菜”。 As a national historical and cultural city, Huizhou has been the “important position of eastern Guangdong”since the Sui and Tang Dynasties, and has always been the political, economic, military, and cultural center of the Dongjiang River Basin，also well known as "Half City Lake, Half City Mountain". Huizhou is one of the most important settlements and distribution centers for the Hakkas, and because the number of overseas Chinese, Hong Kong, Macao and Taiwan is the highest among the four Hakkas District, Huizhou is also known as the capital of Hakka overseas Chinese. This article mainly tells the folk customs of Huizhou, the Han opera of Hakka local drama and the "Dongjiang Famous Dish" of Hakka cuisine. 大亚湾一带渔乡地区曾经的迎亲仪式较为特别。迎亲的两条渔船 贴着“喜”字，四周围插上彩旗在大海中破浪前行。二十位妇女领着 渔船，头附红带、插满金簪银钗，光脚，手拿着彩竿。鞭炮、锣鼓一 起鸣响，妇女们踩着鼓点，摆动彩竿用力划水，口中发出吆喝声，两 船面向呼应。船顶层的狮子也随声起舞，摆动属于它们自己的舞蹈，</p>

<p>婀娜多姿。改革开放使大亚湾的渔村面貌发生巨大变化，但现代化的 生活依然掩不住浓郁的渔家传统气息。 The wedding ceremony in the fishing township area of Daya Bay was quite special. The two fishing boats welcoming each other were marked with the word "Happiness", and colorful flags were put up around them and they sailed through the sea. Twenty women led the fishing boat, with red ribbons on their heads, full of gold hairpins and silver hairpins, bare feet, and colored rods in their hands. Firecrackers, gongs and drums sounded together, and the women stepped on the drums, swung the colored poles and struck hard, shouting in their mouths, and the two boats faced each other. The lions(acted by people) on the top of the ship also danced with the sound, swinging their own dance gracefully. The reform and opening up have brought great changes to the fishing villages of Daya Bay, but the modern life still cannot conceal the strong traditional flavor of fishermen. 除此之外，令人更加难忘的是客家的地方汉剧。它与粤剧、潮剧 并列为广东三大剧种。惠阳汉剧团吸纳来自汕头、韶关和梅州等地的 汉剧人才，成功地演出了《海瑞罢官》等。曾经汉剧在惠州是非常受 欢迎的。比如，当年的《秦香莲》在惠州人民会场（现花都影剧院） 首演时，轰动整个惠州。演出的每一场都是爆满。虽现在少有人唱汉 剧，但仍有人每逢聚会或是除夕前会组织汉剧的演出。 In addition, what is even more memorable is the local Han opera of Hakka. It is listed as on of the three major operas in Guangdong together with Cantonese opera and Chaozhou opera. Huiyang Han Opera Troupe attracted talents from Shantou, Shaoguan, Meizhou and other places and successfully performed Hai Rui Dismissed from Office. Once Han Opera was very popular in Huizhou. For example, when Qin Xianglian premiered in Huizhou People's Hall (now Huadu Cinema) caused a sensation throughout Huizhou. Every performance of the show was full of audiences. Although few people sing Han opera nowadays, there are still people who organize Han opera performances at parties or before New Year's Eve.</p>

<p>要想记住一个城市，那么这个城市必须要用美食深深地吸引你。 而惠州美食有三件宝：东江盐焗鸡、酿豆腐、梅菜扣肉。尤其是梅菜 扣肉在海内外颇具盛名。其实，这是东江客家人在饮食文化方面的杰 作。惠州梅菜的主要产地是矮陂镇土桥村。北宋年间，苏东坡住在惠 州时，专门挑了两位惠州名厨到杭州西湖去学厨。他们归来时，苏东 坡又叫他们仿杭州西湖的"东坡扣肉"，用梅菜制成"梅菜扣肉"。令人 惊喜的是，梅菜扣肉肥而不腻，爽口美味，深受大众喜欢。 If you want to remember a city, then food must be one of the reasons. There are three treasures of Huizhou cuisine: Dongjiang salt-baked chicken, stuffed tofu, and Meicai Kourou (steamed pork with preserved vegetable). In particular, Meicai Kourou is quite famous at home and abroad. In fact, this is a masterpiece of Dongjiang Hakkas' food culture. The main producing area of Huizhou Meicai is Tuqiao Village, Aipi Town. During the Northern Song Dynasty, when Su Dongpo lived in Huizhou, he specially selected two Huizhou chefs to learn how to cook in West Lake, Hangzhou. When they returned, Su Dongpo told them to imitate the "Dongpo Kourou" from West Lake in Hangzhou and make "Mei Cai Kourou" with plum vegetables. Surprisingly, the meat is fat but not greasy, and it is refreshing and delicious, which is popular among the public. 惠州客家文化，既有源于梅州、赣南、闽西客家的传统，又善于 吸取广府、闽南文化的精华，形成独特的风采。惠州是一个包容且独 特的城市。梅菜扣肉不与杭州西湖的“东坡扣肉”雷同，是新事物对 旧事物的包容。大亚湾地区的迎亲仪式至今还有浓郁的渔家传统气 息，是现在对过去的包容。地方汉剧吸纳各地的人才，是本地对外地 的包容。 Huizhou Hakka culture originates from the Hakka traditions of Meizhou, Gannan and Western Fujian, absorbing the essence of Cantonese and Southern Fujian culture to form a unique style. Huizhou is an inclusive and unique city. Meicai Kourou is not the same as the "Dongpo Kourou" of West Lake in Hangzhou, demonstrating the tolerance of new things to old things; The welcoming ceremony in the Daya Bay area still has a strong fisherman tradition, speaking for tolerance of the past to the present; Local Han opera attracts talents from all over the world, meaning tolerance of the local to the outside world. 编译唐玉瑜严粤莹张晓彤</p>

